:: ---- gr.allowtelemetry.del (repair) -----------------------------
::P|gr.allowtelemetry.del|DELETE|DELETE|DELETE|DELETE|DELETE|
::T|EN|gr.allowtelemetry.del.001|REMOVE THE TELEMETRY LEVEL LOCK
::T|EN|gr.allowtelemetry.del.002|Removes two leftover registry values that falsely mark this PC as managed by an organization; there is no privacy change since they never actually lowered data collection on Home or Pro, this just un-greys the Settings dropdown.
::T|FR|gr.allowtelemetry.del.001|RETIRER LE VERROU DE NIVEAU DE TELEMETRIE
::T|FR|gr.allowtelemetry.del.002|Supprime deux valeurs de registre residuelles qui font croire a tort que ce PC est gere par une organisation ; aucun changement de confidentialite puisqu elles ne reduisaient deja rien sur Famille ou Pro, cela redonne juste la main sur la liste de Parametres.
::X|EN|gr.allowtelemetry.del.001|  What it is      : Two registry values that pin the diagnostic data level
::X|EN|gr.allowtelemetry.del.002|                    by policy instead of letting the Settings app own it.
::X|EN|gr.allowtelemetry.del.003|                    The second location, under
::X|EN|gr.allowtelemetry.del.004|                    CurrentVersion\Policies\DataCollection, is a legacy
::X|EN|gr.allowtelemetry.del.005|                    path that many optimizer scripts still write and that
::X|EN|gr.allowtelemetry.del.006|                    nothing ever cleans up.
::X|EN|gr.allowtelemetry.del.007|
::X|EN|gr.allowtelemetry.del.008|  Actual effect   : Deletes both values. The level reverts to the one
::X|EN|gr.allowtelemetry.del.009|                    shown on the Diagnostics & feedback page and the
::X|EN|gr.allowtelemetry.del.010|                    organization banner goes away.
::X|EN|gr.allowtelemetry.del.011|
::X|EN|gr.allowtelemetry.del.012|  Gain            : For privacy on Home or Pro: no measurable gain,
::X|EN|gr.allowtelemetry.del.013|                    because 0 was never honoured there in the first place.
::X|EN|gr.allowtelemetry.del.014|                    The real gain is that Settings stops lying to you -
::X|EN|gr.allowtelemetry.del.015|                    you get an ungreyed dropdown and no false claim that
::X|EN|gr.allowtelemetry.del.016|                    an organization manages this machine.
::X|EN|gr.allowtelemetry.del.017|
::X|EN|gr.allowtelemetry.del.018|  Cost            : Nothing. This is a pure repair and applies without
::X|EN|gr.allowtelemetry.del.019|                    asking.
::X|EN|gr.allowtelemetry.del.020|
::X|EN|gr.allowtelemetry.del.021|  Windows default : Both absent. The level is a user choice made in
::X|EN|gr.allowtelemetry.del.022|                    Settings.
::X|EN|gr.allowtelemetry.del.023|
::X|EN|gr.allowtelemetry.del.024|  Possible values:
::X|EN|gr.allowtelemetry.del.025|    DELETE               : Both values removed. The diagnostic data level
::X|EN|gr.allowtelemetry.del.026|                           goes back to whatever Settings > Privacy &
::X|EN|gr.allowtelemetry.del.027|                           security > Diagnostics & feedback shows, and
::X|EN|gr.allowtelemetry.del.028|                           the "Some settings are managed by your
::X|EN|gr.allowtelemetry.del.029|                           organization" note on that page disappears.
::X|EN|gr.allowtelemetry.del.030|                           This is the shipped state.
::X|EN|gr.allowtelemetry.del.031|    0                    : "Security" - diagnostic data limited to what
::X|EN|gr.allowtelemetry.del.032|                           Windows Update and Defender need. Honoured only
::X|EN|gr.allowtelemetry.del.033|                           on Enterprise, Education and IoT Enterprise. On
