:: ---- gr.copilot.del (preference) ------------------------------------
::P|gr.copilot.del|1|SKIP|DELETE|DELETE|DELETE|
::T|EN|gr.copilot.del.001|BRING BACK THE COPILOT BUTTON
::T|EN|gr.copilot.del.002|Brings back the built-in Copilot taskbar button and shortcut; this is purely about access, not performance, since Copilot never ran as a background process either way.
::T|FR|gr.copilot.del.001|RETABLIR LE BOUTON COPILOT
::T|FR|gr.copilot.del.002|Retablit le bouton et le raccourci Copilot integres a la barre des taches ; c est uniquement une question d acces, pas de performance, puisque Copilot n a jamais tourne en processus de fond.
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.001|  What it is      : Two policy values, machine and user, that switch off
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.002|                    the built-in Copilot entry point. Same pair as the
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.003|                    setup question, reached from the restore menu.
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.004|
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.005|  Actual effect   : Deletes both, so the Copilot button and its shortcut
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.006|                    come back where the build still has them.
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.007|
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.008|  Gain            : You get the built-in entry point back, if you use it.
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.009|                    Nothing else changes.
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.010|
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.011|  Cost            : Copilot reappears near the taskbar and can be launched
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.012|                    by accident. That is the entire cost.
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.013|
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.014|  Windows default : Both values absent, Copilot available.
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.015|
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.016|  Possible values:
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.017|    1                    : The integrated Copilot entry point is turned
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.018|                           off: the taskbar button and the shell shortcut
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.019|                           stop working. It does not uninstall the Copilot
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.020|                           Store app, and it frees no memory, because
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.021|                           nothing was resident to begin with - Copilot is
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.022|                           launched, not hosted.
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.023|    0                    : An explicit "Copilot allowed by policy". A
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.024|                           third state, not the shipped one - it still
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.025|                           marks the setting as policy-managed. Do not use
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.026|                           it to undo the block; delete the value.
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.027|    DELETE               : Value absent, which is the shipped condition.
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.028|                           Copilot is available; whether its button is
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.029|                           pinned is then an ordinary taskbar setting you
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.030|                           can change by right-clicking, with no policy
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.031|                           involved.
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.032|    SKIP                 : Leave whatever is there. Correct on a machine
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.033|                           where nobody looks at the taskbar.
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.034|
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.035|  Why these profiles : Be honest about what this knob is: it has no
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.036|                       measurable effect on frame times, memory, boot or
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.037|                       battery, because Copilot is not a resident process
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.038|                       - it is an app you either launch or do not. So four
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.039|                       of the five profiles have no performance reason to
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.040|                       touch it, and this table says so rather than
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.041|                       inventing one. Only gaming writes 1, and for a
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.042|                       purely visual reason: that profile wants a bare
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.043|                       taskbar and no shell surface it did not ask for.
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.044|                       Server skips because a headless box has no taskbar
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.045|                       to clean and no background cost to remove. Office
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.046|                       and laptop match the Windows default, laptop
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.047|                       included - there is no battery argument here in
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.048|                       either direction, and pretending otherwise would be
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.049|                       exactly the folklore this rewrite exists to remove.
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.050|
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.051|  Known problems  : None known. If you only want the button gone, right-
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.052|                    clicking the taskbar removes it without any policy
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.053|                    value and without the managed-by-your-organization
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.054|                    marking.
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.055|
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.056|  Unverified      : On 24H2 and 25H2 Copilot ships as an ordinary Store
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.057|                    app (Microsoft.Copilot). TurnOffWindowsCopilot governs
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.058|                    the integrated shell entry point; I cannot confirm how
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.059|                    much of the modern app experience it still reaches, so
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.060|                    both writing it and deleting it may do less than the
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.061|                    name suggests on a current build.
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.062|
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.063|  Target          : reg delete "HKLM\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Windows\W
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.064|                    indowsCopilot" /v "TurnOffWindowsCopilot" /f and reg
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.065|                    delete "HKCU\Software\Policies\Microsoft\Windows\Windo
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.066|                    wsCopilot" /v "TurnOffWindowsCopilot" /f (OPTY.bat
::X|EN|gr.copilot.del.067|                    lines 1641-1642)
::X|FR|gr.copilot.del.001|  Ce que c est    : Deux valeurs de strategie, machine et utilisateur, qui
::X|FR|gr.copilot.del.002|                    coupent le point d entree Copilot integre. Meme paire
::X|FR|gr.copilot.del.003|                    que dans la question de configuration, atteinte depuis
::X|FR|gr.copilot.del.004|                    le menu de restauration.
::X|FR|gr.copilot.del.005|
::X|FR|gr.copilot.del.006|  Effet reel      : Supprime les deux : le bouton Copilot et son raccourci
::X|FR|gr.copilot.del.007|                    reviennent la ou la version les propose encore.
::X|FR|gr.copilot.del.008|
::X|FR|gr.copilot.del.009|  Gain            : Vous retrouvez le point d entree integre, si vous vous
::X|FR|gr.copilot.del.010|                    en servez. Rien d autre ne bouge.
::X|FR|gr.copilot.del.011|
::X|FR|gr.copilot.del.012|  Cout            : Copilot reapparait pres de la barre des taches et peut
::X|FR|gr.copilot.del.013|                    se lancer par erreur. C est tout le cout.
::X|FR|gr.copilot.del.014|
::X|FR|gr.copilot.del.015|  Defaut Windows  : Les deux valeurs absentes, Copilot disponible.
::X|FR|gr.copilot.del.016|
::X|FR|gr.copilot.del.017|  Valeurs possibles :
::X|FR|gr.copilot.del.018|    1                    : Le point d entree Copilot integre est coupe :
::X|FR|gr.copilot.del.019|                           le bouton de la barre des taches et le
::X|FR|gr.copilot.del.020|                           raccourci du shell cessent de fonctionner. Cela
::X|FR|gr.copilot.del.021|                           ne desinstalle pas l application Copilot du
::X|FR|gr.copilot.del.022|                           Store, et cela ne libere aucune memoire,
::X|FR|gr.copilot.del.023|                           puisque rien n etait resident : Copilot se
::X|FR|gr.copilot.del.024|                           lance, il ne tourne pas en fond.
::X|FR|gr.copilot.del.025|    0                    : Un "Copilot autorise par strategie" explicite.
::X|FR|gr.copilot.del.026|                           Troisieme etat, pas l etat d origine : le
::X|FR|gr.copilot.del.027|                           reglage reste marque comme gere par strategie.
::X|FR|gr.copilot.del.028|                           Ne l utilisez pas pour annuler le blocage,
::X|FR|gr.copilot.del.029|                           supprimez la valeur.
::X|FR|gr.copilot.del.030|    DELETE               : Valeur absente, c est-a-dire l etat livre.
::X|FR|gr.copilot.del.031|                           Copilot est disponible, et la presence de son
::X|FR|gr.copilot.del.032|                           bouton redevient un simple reglage de barre des
::X|FR|gr.copilot.del.033|                           taches, modifiable par un clic droit, sans
::X|FR|gr.copilot.del.034|                           aucune strategie.
::X|FR|gr.copilot.del.035|    SKIP                 : Laisse ce qui est en place. Correct sur une
::X|FR|gr.copilot.del.036|                           machine dont personne ne regarde la barre des
::X|FR|gr.copilot.del.037|                           taches.
::X|FR|gr.copilot.del.038|
::X|FR|gr.copilot.del.039|  Pourquoi ces profils : Soyons clairs sur la nature de ce bouton : il n a
::X|FR|gr.copilot.del.040|                         aucun effet mesurable sur les temps d image, la
::X|FR|gr.copilot.del.041|                         memoire, le demarrage ou l autonomie, parce que
::X|FR|gr.copilot.del.042|                         Copilot n est pas un processus resident - c est
::X|FR|gr.copilot.del.043|                         une application que vous lancez ou pas. Quatre
::X|FR|gr.copilot.del.044|                         profils sur cinq n ont donc aucune raison
::X|FR|gr.copilot.del.045|                         technique d y toucher, et ce tableau le dit au
::X|FR|gr.copilot.del.046|                         lieu d en inventer une. Seul le profil gaming
::X|FR|gr.copilot.del.047|                         ecrit 1, pour un motif purement visuel : il veut
::X|FR|gr.copilot.del.048|                         une barre des taches nue, sans surface imposee.
::X|FR|gr.copilot.del.049|                         Le serveur passe son tour, parce qu une machine
::X|FR|gr.copilot.del.050|                         sans ecran n a ni barre des taches a nettoyer ni
::X|FR|gr.copilot.del.051|                         cout de fond a supprimer. Bureautique et portable
