::P|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore|1|1|1|1|1|
::T|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.001|BRING BACK SUGGESTIONS AND TIPS
::T|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.002|Restores eight suggestion and tip settings; seven are just cosmetic banners and toasts, but the eighth lets Windows quietly download promoted apps into your profile again.
::T|FR|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.001|RETABLIR SUGGESTIONS ET CONSEILS
::T|FR|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.002|Retablit huit reglages de suggestions et de conseils ; sept ne sont que des bannieres et notifications cosmetiques, mais le huitieme laisse de nouveau Windows telecharger discretement des applications promues dans votre profil.
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.001|  What it is      : Eight ContentDeliveryManager values under the current
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.002|                    user, covering Settings suggestion banners, the Start
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.003|                    menu suggestions, the tips toasts, the lock-screen
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.004|                    text overlay, and the two that govern automatic app
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.005|                    delivery.
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.006|
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.007|  Actual effect   : Deletes all eight, which puts every one of them back
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.008|                    to enabled behaviour.
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.009|
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.010|  Gain            : None for you. It exists so a profile can be returned
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.011|                    to stock.
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.012|
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.013|  Cost            : Suggestions, tips, the lock-screen overlay and
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.014|                    silently installed promotional apps all come back -
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.015|                    and the last of those is the one with teeth.
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.016|
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.017|  Windows default : Normally present with 1; absent behaves identically.
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.018|
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.019|  Possible values:
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.020|    SilentInstalledAppsEnabled=0 :
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.021|        The one that actually does something. Windows stops silently
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.022|        downloading and installing promoted apps into your profile in the
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.023|        background. At 1 it may install them at any time, which is a real
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.024|        download and a real disk write you did not ask for.
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.025|    PreInstalledAppsEnabled=0 :
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.026|        Stops the OEM and Microsoft preinstalled-app provisioning from re-
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.027|        running on this profile. Affects what appears on a newly created
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.028|        profile; it does not remove apps already installed.
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.029|    SystemPaneSuggestionsEnabled=0 :
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.030|        Removes the "occasionally show suggestions in Start" entries.
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.031|        Cosmetic - no process, no download, no measurable gain.
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.032|    SubscribedContent-338389Enabled=0 :
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.033|        Turns off the "get tips and suggestions when using Windows"
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.034|        toasts. Notification-only; no measurable gain.
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.035|    SubscribedContent-338393Enabled=0 :
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.036|        Removes suggested content from one of the Settings pages. Purely a
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.037|        banner; no measurable gain.
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.038|    SubscribedContent-353694Enabled=0 :
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.039|        Removes suggested content from a second Settings surface. Same
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.040|        nature as above.
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.041|    SubscribedContent-353696Enabled=0 :
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.042|        Removes suggested content from a third Settings surface. Same
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.043|        nature as above.
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.044|    RotatingLockScreenOverlayEnabled=0 :
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.045|        Removes the text overlay - the tip or fun fact and its "like what
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.046|        you see" link - drawn on top of the Spotlight lock-screen image.
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.047|        It does not stop the image itself from rotating; that is the
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.048|        separate Spotlight policy.
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.049|    1                    : For any of the eight: the feature is on. This
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.050|                           is what the values ship as once
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.051|                           ContentDeliveryManager creates them.
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.052|    DELETE               : Absent behaves as enabled for all eight.
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.053|                           Deleting is a restore, never a way to turn
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.054|                           something off.
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.055|
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.056|  Why these profiles : Seven of these eight are banner and toast
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.057|                       cosmetics: turning them off removes no process, no
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.058|                       service and no measurable CPU, RAM or disk load,
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.059|                       and any guide that lists them as a speed-up is
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.060|                       padding a list. SilentInstalledAppsEnabled is the
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.061|                       exception, and it is a real one - it is the switch
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.062|                       that decides whether apps get downloaded into your
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.063|                       profile without you asking, which costs bandwidth
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.064|                       on a metered link and disk on a small SSD. That is
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.065|                       why the office row is split rather than all-or-
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.066|                       nothing: a family PC should still stop unrequested
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.067|                       installs, but it is also the machine where a new
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.068|                       user genuinely benefits from the built-in hints, so
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.069|                       the six cosmetic ones stay at default there.
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.070|                       Gaming, server and laptop take all eight to 0
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.071|                       because none of them wants any of it.
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.072|
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.073|  Unverified      : On a brand-new profile a few of these eight may not
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.074|                    exist yet - ContentDeliveryManager creates them the
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.075|                    first time the corresponding surface is shown. Since
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.076|                    absent behaves as enabled, DELETE and 1 are
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.077|                    behaviourally identical for the Windows answer, but a
::X|EN|gr.cdm.suggestions.restore.078|                    report that says "written" should not claim it
