:: ---- db.copilot.off (preference) ------------------------------------
::P|db.copilot.off|1|SKIP|DELETE|DELETE|DELETE|
::T|EN|db.copilot.off.001|TURN WINDOWS COPILOT OFF
::T|EN|db.copilot.off.002|Disables the built-in Copilot taskbar button and shortcut; there is no performance gain since Copilot never ran in the background, this only removes it as something to launch by accident.
::T|FR|db.copilot.off.001|DESACTIVER WINDOWS COPILOT
::T|FR|db.copilot.off.002|Desactive le bouton et le raccourci Copilot integres ; aucun gain de performance puisque Copilot ne tournait jamais en fond, cela retire seulement la possibilite de le lancer par erreur.
::X|EN|db.copilot.off.001|  What it is      : Two policy values, machine and user, that disable the
::X|EN|db.copilot.off.002|                    built-in Copilot entry point.
::X|EN|db.copilot.off.003|
::X|EN|db.copilot.off.004|  Actual effect   : Writes 1 to both. The Copilot button and its shell
::X|EN|db.copilot.off.005|                    shortcut stop working.
::X|EN|db.copilot.off.006|
::X|EN|db.copilot.off.007|  Gain            : No measurable gain. Copilot is not resident, so there
::X|EN|db.copilot.off.008|                    is no memory freed, no CPU saved, no boot time
::X|EN|db.copilot.off.009|                    recovered and no battery gained - the only thing you
::X|EN|db.copilot.off.010|                    get is one fewer thing to launch by accident. Anyone
::X|EN|db.copilot.off.011|                    selling this as a performance tweak is selling
::X|EN|db.copilot.off.012|                    folklore.
::X|EN|db.copilot.off.013|
::X|EN|db.copilot.off.014|  Cost            : You lose the built-in entry point. The standalone
::X|EN|db.copilot.off.015|                    Copilot app, if installed, is untouched.
::X|EN|db.copilot.off.016|
::X|EN|db.copilot.off.017|  Windows default : Both absent, Copilot available.
::X|EN|db.copilot.off.018|
::X|EN|db.copilot.off.019|  Possible values:
::X|EN|db.copilot.off.020|    1                    : The built-in Copilot entry point is disabled:
::X|EN|db.copilot.off.021|                           taskbar button and shell shortcut stop
::X|EN|db.copilot.off.022|                           responding. It does not uninstall the Store app
::X|EN|db.copilot.off.023|                           and it frees no memory - Copilot has no
::X|EN|db.copilot.off.024|                           resident process to remove.
::X|EN|db.copilot.off.025|    0                    : Explicitly allowed by policy. A third state -
::X|EN|db.copilot.off.026|                           it marks the setting as managed while
::X|EN|db.copilot.off.027|                           permitting it. Not the shipped condition.
::X|EN|db.copilot.off.028|    DELETE               : Absent, the shipped state. Copilot available,
::X|EN|db.copilot.off.029|                           its button governed by an ordinary taskbar
::X|EN|db.copilot.off.030|                           setting you can toggle with a right-click.
::X|EN|db.copilot.off.031|    SKIP                 : Leave whatever is there, correct where nobody
::X|EN|db.copilot.off.032|                           looks at the taskbar.
::X|EN|db.copilot.off.033|
::X|EN|db.copilot.off.034|  Why these profiles : This table is deliberately thin because the setting
::X|EN|db.copilot.off.035|                       is thin. Only gaming writes 1, and for a visual
::X|EN|db.copilot.off.036|                       reason it is honest about: that profile wants a
::X|EN|db.copilot.off.037|                       bare taskbar and no shell surface it did not
::X|EN|db.copilot.off.038|                       choose. Server skips - a headless box has no
::X|EN|db.copilot.off.039|                       taskbar to tidy and no background cost to reclaim,
::X|EN|db.copilot.off.040|                       so writing a policy value there would be noise in
::X|EN|db.copilot.off.041|                       the registry and nothing else. Office, laptop and
::X|EN|db.copilot.off.042|                       Windows all leave it absent, and yes that means
::X|EN|db.copilot.off.043|                       three identical rows: there is no latency case, no
::X|EN|db.copilot.off.044|                       throughput case and no battery case to be made in
::X|EN|db.copilot.off.045|                       either direction, so the table declines to invent
::X|EN|db.copilot.off.046|                       one. If all you want is the button gone, right-
::X|EN|db.copilot.off.047|                       click the taskbar instead - it achieves the same
::X|EN|db.copilot.off.048|                       visible result without stamping the machine as
::X|EN|db.copilot.off.049|                       policy-managed.
::X|EN|db.copilot.off.050|
::X|EN|db.copilot.off.051|  Unverified      : On 24H2 and 25H2 Copilot is an ordinary Store app
::X|EN|db.copilot.off.052|                    (Microsoft.Copilot). This policy governs the
::X|EN|db.copilot.off.053|                    integrated shell entry point, and I cannot confirm how
::X|EN|db.copilot.off.054|                    much of the current app experience it still reaches -
::X|EN|db.copilot.off.055|                    on a recent build it may amount to little more than
::X|EN|db.copilot.off.056|                    hiding a pinned button.
::X|EN|db.copilot.off.057|
::X|EN|db.copilot.off.058|  Target          : reg add "HKLM\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Windows\Wind
::X|EN|db.copilot.off.059|                    owsCopilot" /v "TurnOffWindowsCopilot" /t REG_DWORD /d
::X|EN|db.copilot.off.060|                    1 /f and reg add "HKCU\Software\Policies\Microsoft\Win
::X|EN|db.copilot.off.061|                    dows\WindowsCopilot" /v "TurnOffWindowsCopilot" /t
::X|EN|db.copilot.off.062|                    REG_DWORD /d 1 /f (OPTY.bat lines 1717-1718)
::X|FR|db.copilot.off.001|  Ce que c est    : Deux valeurs de strategie, machine et utilisateur, qui
::X|FR|db.copilot.off.002|                    coupent le point d entree Copilot integre.
::X|FR|db.copilot.off.003|
::X|FR|db.copilot.off.004|  Effet reel      : Ecrit 1 aux deux. Le bouton Copilot et son raccourci
::X|FR|db.copilot.off.005|                    clavier cessent de fonctionner.
::X|FR|db.copilot.off.006|
::X|FR|db.copilot.off.007|  Gain            : Aucun gain mesurable. Copilot n est pas resident : pas
::X|FR|db.copilot.off.008|                    de memoire liberee, pas de CPU economise, pas de temps
::X|FR|db.copilot.off.009|                    de demarrage recupere, pas d autonomie gagnee. Tout ce
::X|FR|db.copilot.off.010|                    que vous obtenez, c est une chose de moins a lancer
::X|FR|db.copilot.off.011|                    par erreur. Qui vous vend ceci comme un reglage de
::X|FR|db.copilot.off.012|                    performance vous vend du folklore.
::X|FR|db.copilot.off.013|
::X|FR|db.copilot.off.014|  Cout            : Vous perdez le point d entree integre. L application
::X|FR|db.copilot.off.015|                    Copilot autonome, si elle est installee, n est pas
::X|FR|db.copilot.off.016|                    touchee.
::X|FR|db.copilot.off.017|
::X|FR|db.copilot.off.018|  Defaut Windows  : Les deux absentes, Copilot disponible.
::X|FR|db.copilot.off.019|
::X|FR|db.copilot.off.020|  Valeurs possibles :
::X|FR|db.copilot.off.021|    1                    : Le point d entree Copilot integre est desactive
::X|FR|db.copilot.off.022|                           : le bouton de la barre des taches et le
::X|FR|db.copilot.off.023|                           raccourci du shell ne repondent plus. Cela ne
::X|FR|db.copilot.off.024|                           desinstalle pas l application du Store et ne
::X|FR|db.copilot.off.025|                           libere aucune memoire : Copilot n a pas de
::X|FR|db.copilot.off.026|                           processus resident a supprimer.
::X|FR|db.copilot.off.027|    0                    : Explicitement autorise par strategie. Troisieme
::X|FR|db.copilot.off.028|                           etat : le reglage est marque comme gere tout en
::X|FR|db.copilot.off.029|                           etant permis. Ce n est pas la condition
::X|FR|db.copilot.off.030|                           d origine.
::X|FR|db.copilot.off.031|    DELETE               : Absente, l etat d origine. Copilot disponible,
::X|FR|db.copilot.off.032|                           son bouton relevant d un simple reglage de
::X|FR|db.copilot.off.033|                           barre des taches modifiable par un clic droit.
::X|FR|db.copilot.off.034|    SKIP                 : Laisse ce qui est en place, ce qui convient la
::X|FR|db.copilot.off.035|                           ou personne ne regarde la barre des taches.
::X|FR|db.copilot.off.036|
::X|FR|db.copilot.off.037|  Pourquoi ces profils : Ce tableau est maigre parce que le reglage l est.
::X|FR|db.copilot.off.038|                         Seul le profil gaming ecrit 1, pour une raison
::X|FR|db.copilot.off.039|                         visuelle qu il assume : il veut une barre des
::X|FR|db.copilot.off.040|                         taches nue, sans element impose. Le serveur passe
::X|FR|db.copilot.off.041|                         son tour - une machine sans ecran n a ni barre a
::X|FR|db.copilot.off.042|                         ranger ni cout de fond a recuperer, donc y ecrire
::X|FR|db.copilot.off.043|                         une strategie serait du bruit dans le registre,
::X|FR|db.copilot.off.044|                         rien de plus. Bureautique, portable et Windows
