:: ---- rad.maintenance.killswitch (repair) ------------------------
::P|rad.maintenance.killswitch|DELETE|DELETE|DELETE|DELETE|DELETE|
::T|EN|rad.maintenance.killswitch.001|RE-ENABLE AUTOMATIC MAINTENANCE
::T|EN|rad.maintenance.killswitch.002|Removes a hidden switch, invisible anywhere in the Windows UI, that some debloat tools use to silently stop all scheduled disk and system upkeep - if it was set, this is one of the most impactful single fixes in the whole script.
::T|FR|rad.maintenance.killswitch.001|REACTIVER LA MAINTENANCE AUTOMATIQUE
::T|FR|rad.maintenance.killswitch.002|Supprime un interrupteur cache, invisible partout dans l interface Windows, que certains outils de debloat utilisent pour arreter en silence tout l entretien planifie du disque et du systeme - s il etait actif, c est l une des corrections les plus importantes de tout le script.
::X|EN|rad.maintenance.killswitch.001|  What it is      : A single DWORD that silently switches off the whole
::X|EN|rad.maintenance.killswitch.002|                    Automatic Maintenance window. It is a favourite of debloat
::X|EN|rad.maintenance.killswitch.003|                    scripts because it makes a machine look quiet, and it is
::X|EN|rad.maintenance.killswitch.004|                    one of the very few settings in Windows with no GUI
::X|EN|rad.maintenance.killswitch.005|                    representation at all.
::X|EN|rad.maintenance.killswitch.006|
::X|EN|rad.maintenance.killswitch.007|  Actual effect   : Deletes the value if present, so scheduled TRIM or defrag,
::X|EN|rad.maintenance.killswitch.008|                    proactive chkdsk, index compaction and WinSxS cleanup are
::X|EN|rad.maintenance.killswitch.009|                    allowed to run again during idle time. Deleting is the
::X|EN|rad.maintenance.killswitch.010|                    correct restore here because the shipped default is the
::X|EN|rad.maintenance.killswitch.011|                    value not existing.
::X|EN|rad.maintenance.killswitch.012|
::X|EN|rad.maintenance.killswitch.013|  Gain            : Nothing on a machine where it was never set - and that is
::X|EN|rad.maintenance.killswitch.014|                    most machines, so do not expect a report line. On a
::X|EN|rad.maintenance.killswitch.015|                    machine where a tweak tool set it, this is the highest-
::X|EN|rad.maintenance.killswitch.016|                    leverage single value in the whole script: months of
::X|EN|rad.maintenance.killswitch.017|                    skipped TRIM, an index that never compacts and a WinSxS
::X|EN|rad.maintenance.killswitch.018|                    store that only ever grows, all while Task Scheduler shows
::X|EN|rad.maintenance.killswitch.019|                    everything Ready.
::X|EN|rad.maintenance.killswitch.020|
::X|EN|rad.maintenance.killswitch.021|  Cost            : Maintenance uses the disk and CPU while the machine is
::X|EN|rad.maintenance.killswitch.022|                    idle and backs off as soon as you touch it. On a laptop,
::X|EN|rad.maintenance.killswitch.023|                    that idle work is real battery when the lid is open and
::X|EN|rad.maintenance.killswitch.024|                    the machine is plugged in - Windows already restricts the
::X|EN|rad.maintenance.killswitch.025|                    window on battery.
::X|EN|rad.maintenance.killswitch.026|
::X|EN|rad.maintenance.killswitch.027|  Windows default : Absent, maintenance runs.
::X|EN|rad.maintenance.killswitch.028|
::X|EN|rad.maintenance.killswitch.029|  Possible values:
::X|EN|rad.maintenance.killswitch.030|    DELETE : The shipped state. The Automatic Maintenance window runs when the
::X|EN|rad.maintenance.killswitch.031|             machine is idle: scheduled defrag or TRIM depending on the media,
::X|EN|rad.maintenance.killswitch.032|             chkdsk ProactiveScan, search-index compaction, WinSxS component
::X|EN|rad.maintenance.killswitch.033|             cleanup, and the system-restore and update housekeeping tasks. It
::X|EN|rad.maintenance.killswitch.034|             yields the moment you touch the keyboard.
::X|EN|rad.maintenance.killswitch.035|    1      : Stops the entire maintenance window. The individual tasks are NOT
::X|EN|rad.maintenance.killswitch.036|             disabled - every one of them still shows Ready in Task Scheduler
::X|EN|rad.maintenance.killswitch.037|             and its next-run time still advances - the maintenance scheduler
::X|EN|rad.maintenance.killswitch.038|             simply never launches them. That combination is why this is
::X|EN|rad.maintenance.killswitch.039|             invisible: there is no GUI anywhere in Windows that reveals it,
::X|EN|rad.maintenance.killswitch.040|             and every diagnostic you would run looks healthy.
::X|EN|rad.maintenance.killswitch.041|    0      : Maintenance enabled, written explicitly. Behaviourally the same
::X|EN|rad.maintenance.killswitch.042|             as the value being absent. It is not wrong, it just leaves a
::X|EN|rad.maintenance.killswitch.043|             value in the registry that the OS never wrote, which is why this
::X|EN|rad.maintenance.killswitch.044|             step deletes rather than writing 0.
::X|EN|rad.maintenance.killswitch.045|
::X|EN|rad.maintenance.killswitch.046|  Why these profiles : Five identical answers and no honest way to
::X|EN|rad.maintenance.killswitch.047|                       differentiate. TRIM, chkdsk and component cleanup are
::X|EN|rad.maintenance.killswitch.048|                       not a taste - a gaming SSD that never gets TRIM
::X|EN|rad.maintenance.killswitch.049|                       degrades exactly like an office one, and a host box
::X|EN|rad.maintenance.killswitch.050|                       that is idle most of the day is the ideal case for a
::X|EN|rad.maintenance.killswitch.051|                       maintenance window, not an argument against it.
::X|EN|rad.maintenance.killswitch.052|
::X|EN|rad.maintenance.killswitch.053|  Target             : HKLM\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows
