:: ---- usoclient.scaninstall (risky) -----------------------------
::P|usoclient.scaninstall|SKIP|RUN|RUN|SKIP|SKIP|
::T|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.001|INSTALL PENDING WINDOWS UPDATES NOW
::T|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.002|This forces Windows Update to scan, download and install everything pending right now instead of waiting for its own schedule, which patches you faster but risks an unwanted driver swap or a reboot prompt mid-session.
::T|FR|usoclient.scaninstall.001|INSTALLER MAINTENANT LES MISES A JOUR WINDOWS EN ATTENTE
::T|FR|usoclient.scaninstall.002|Ceci force Windows Update a rechercher, telecharger et installer immediatement tout ce qui est en attente, au lieu d attendre son propre calendrier, ce qui protege plus vite mais risque un pilote indesirable ou une demande de redemarrage en pleine session.
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.001|  What it is      : Triggers Windows Update to scan, download and install
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.002|                    everything pending, without going through the Settings
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.003|                    window and without asking again once it has started.
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.004|
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.005|  Actual effect   : Starts the same update session the Windows Update page
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.006|                    starts. Because the call is asynchronous, OPTY logs
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.007|                    'executed' and moves on while the install is still
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.008|                    running - and if OPTY is chained to a shutdown, the
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.009|                    install finishes at the next boot on its own schedule.
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.010|
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.011|  Gain            : The machine ends up patched. Security patches are the
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.012|                    single highest-value thing in this whole script;
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.013|                    nothing else in OPTY protects you from anything.
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.014|
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.015|  Cost            : Genuine risk of surprise. It can install a driver you
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.016|                    did not want, it will usually leave the machine
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.017|                    needing a reboot, and it can pull a feature update on
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.018|                    a machine you meant to keep on its current build.
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.019|                    usoclient is undocumented by Microsoft and its
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.020|                    behaviour has changed between builds, so on some
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.021|                    versions it queues a scan and never reaches the
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.022|                    install stage - and OPTY cannot tell the difference.
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.023|
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.024|  Windows default : Not applicable in the usual sense: Windows already
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.025|                    scans and installs on its own schedule. This only
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.026|                    forces it to happen now, which is not a shipped state.
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.027|
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.028|  Possible values:
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.029|    RUN                  : usoclient scaninstallwait asks the Update
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.030|                           Orchestrator to scan, download and install
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.031|                           everything currently offered. It is
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.032|                           asynchronous: the command returns almost
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.033|                           immediately while the session runs in the
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.034|                           background, so OPTY's exit code says nothing
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.035|                           about whether anything installed. Whatever is
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.036|                           offered gets installed - quality updates,
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.037|                           drivers if your settings allow them, sometimes
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.038|                           a feature update - and the machine is usually
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.039|                           left with a reboot pending.
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.040|    SKIP                 : Nothing is triggered. Windows Update keeps its
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.041|                           own schedule: it scans roughly daily, downloads
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.042|                           and installs during idle time, and reboots
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.043|                           inside your active hours window. You are not
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.044|                           left unpatched by skipping this - you are left
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.045|                           on Microsoft's timing instead of forcing it
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.046|                           now.
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.047|
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.048|  Why these profiles : SERVER and OFFICE run it, and for the same reason:
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.049|                       a box that is exposed to the network and looked
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.050|                       after by someone who can let it reboot should be
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.051|                       current, and this is the one step in OPTY that
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.052|                       actually protects the machine. GAMING skips it on
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.053|                       timing, not principle - the concrete cost is
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.054|                       Windows Update replacing a hand-picked GPU driver
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.055|                       and a restart-required nag arriving mid-session;
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.056|                       run it deliberately on a day you are not playing.
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.057|                       LAPTOP skips it because a full update session is
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.058|                       the heaviest sustained CPU and disk load Windows
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.059|                       will ever schedule, which is exactly what the
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.060|                       battery-first profile refuses; Windows itself
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.061|                       already defers this on battery and on metered
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.062|                       links, and that deferral is the behaviour the
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.063|                       profile wants respected. WINDOWS skips because
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.064|                       forcing a scan now is not a shipped default.
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.065|
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.066|  Known problems  : Two concrete ones. Windows Update can replace a
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.067|                    manually installed GPU driver with the WHQL build it
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.068|                    carries: the symptom is a display driver version that
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.069|                    silently goes backwards after a reboot, taking custom
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.070|                    Adrenalin or NVIDIA Control Panel profiles with it.
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.071|                    And because usoclient returns immediately, OPTY's log
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.072|                    line 'Executed usoclient scaninstallwait
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.073|                    (scan+download+install)' is written whether or not a
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.074|                    single update installed - on builds where
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.075|                    scaninstallwait only queues a scan, the log is
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.076|                    confidently wrong.
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.077|
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.078|  Unverified      : usoclient is not documented by Microsoft. On some
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.079|                    Windows 11 builds scaninstallwait triggers a scan but
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.080|                    not an install; this was not re-tested on 25H2, and
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.081|                    OPTY reports success either way.
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.082|
::X|EN|usoclient.scaninstall.083|  Target          : OPTY.bat :wupdate, line 672: usoclient scaninstallwait
::X|FR|usoclient.scaninstall.001|  Ce que c est    : Declenche la recherche, le telechargement et
::X|FR|usoclient.scaninstall.002|                    l installation de tout ce qui est en attente dans
::X|FR|usoclient.scaninstall.003|                    Windows Update, sans passer par la fenetre Parametres
::X|FR|usoclient.scaninstall.004|                    et sans redemander une fois lance.
::X|FR|usoclient.scaninstall.005|
::X|FR|usoclient.scaninstall.006|  Effet reel      : Ouvre la meme session de mise a jour que la page
::X|FR|usoclient.scaninstall.007|                    Windows Update. Comme l appel est asynchrone, OPTY
::X|FR|usoclient.scaninstall.008|                    note « execute » et passe a la suite pendant que
::X|FR|usoclient.scaninstall.009|                    l installation tourne encore - et si OPTY enchaine sur
::X|FR|usoclient.scaninstall.010|                    un arret, l installation se termine au prochain
::X|FR|usoclient.scaninstall.011|                    demarrage, a son propre rythme.
::X|FR|usoclient.scaninstall.012|
::X|FR|usoclient.scaninstall.013|  Gain            : La machine finit a jour. Les correctifs de securite
::X|FR|usoclient.scaninstall.014|                    sont ce que ce script apporte de plus precieux ; rien
::X|FR|usoclient.scaninstall.015|                    d autre dans OPTY ne vous protege de quoi que ce soit.
::X|FR|usoclient.scaninstall.016|
::X|FR|usoclient.scaninstall.017|  Cout            : Vraie possibilite de mauvaise surprise. Ca peut
::X|FR|usoclient.scaninstall.018|                    installer un pilote dont vous ne vouliez pas, ca
