::P|storagesense.tempfiles|1|1|1|1|1|
::T|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.001|STORAGE SENSE RULE: DELETE TEMP FILES
::T|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.002|This turns on the specific Storage Sense rule that actually deletes old temporary files, reclaiming a few hundred MB to a couple of GB a month, with no real risk beyond software that wrongly stores long-term data in the temp folder.
::T|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.001|REGLE DE L ASSISTANT STOCKAGE : SUPPRIMER LES FICHIERS TEMPORAIRES
::T|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.002|Ceci active la regle precise de l Assistant Stockage qui supprime vraiment les vieux fichiers temporaires, recuperant de quelques centaines de Mo a deux Go par mois, sans risque reel hormis un logiciel qui stocke a tort des donnees durables dans le dossier temporaire.
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.001|  What it is      : The single checkbox inside Storage Sense labelled
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.002|                    'Keep Windows running smoothly by automatically
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.003|                    cleaning up temporary system and app files'. Without
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.004|                    it, turning Storage Sense on does almost nothing
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.005|                    useful.
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.006|
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.007|  Actual effect   : Sets StoragePolicy value 04 to 1. Windows empties the
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.008|                    standard temp locations during its scheduled pass,
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.009|                    with its own age filters applied.
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.010|
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.011|  Gain            : This is the rule that actually reclaims space. On a
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.012|                    machine used daily it is typically a few hundred MB to
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.013|                    a couple of GB per month that would otherwise just
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.014|                    accumulate. It is space, not speed - no throughput or
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.015|                    latency changes.
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.016|
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.017|  Cost            : An application that parks working data in %TEMP% and
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.018|                    expects it to survive for weeks could lose it. That is
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.019|                    rare and badly-behaved software, and Storage Sense
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.020|                    applies age and in-use filters rather than emptying
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.021|                    the folder outright.
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.022|
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.023|  Windows default : 1 - the checkbox ships ticked on Windows 11, and 1 is
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.024|                    the same value the Settings UI itself writes, so this
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.025|                    is a re-assert of the shipped state and not a third
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.026|                    position.
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.027|
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.028|  Possible values:
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.029|    1                    : The temp-file rule is on. During its scheduled
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.030|                           pass Storage Sense empties the standard
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.031|                           temporary locations - %TEMP%, Windows\Temp, the
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.032|                           Delivery Optimization cache, thumbnail and
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.033|                           Windows Update cleanup targets - applying its
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.034|                           own age and in-use filters rather than deleting
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.035|                           blindly. This is the rule that actually
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.036|                           reclaims space; the master switch alone
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.037|                           reclaims almost nothing.
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.038|    0                    : The temp-file rule is off. Storage Sense still
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.039|                           runs on its schedule but only handles the
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.040|                           Recycle Bin, Downloads and cloud-dehydration
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.041|                           rules, so on a machine with the Downloads rule
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.042|                           pinned off it does close to nothing. Turning
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.043|                           the master switch on with 04 at 0 is the
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.044|                           configuration that makes people say Storage
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.045|                           Sense is useless.
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.046|    DELETE               : Value absent. The Settings checkbox still reads
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.047|                           ticked and Windows behaves as if it were 1, so
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.048|                           removing it changes nothing observable. Writing
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.049|                           1 therefore reproduces the shipped behaviour
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.050|                           exactly, unlike the 0-versus-absent cases
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.051|                           elsewhere in this script.
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.052|
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.053|  Why these profiles : Five identical answers, which is the correct table
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.054|                       rather than a lazy one: this is the shipped Windows
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.055|                       behaviour and the entire point of Storage Sense,
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.056|                       and there is no profile for which accumulating temp
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.057|                       files is desirable. A server benefits as much as a
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.058|                       gaming desktop, a laptop as much as an office PC,
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.059|                       and WINDOWS agrees because 1 is what Windows ships.
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.060|                       The only person who should say no is someone using
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.061|                       %TEMP% as a personal scratch folder.
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.062|
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.063|  Unverified      : Whether StoragePolicy value 04 physically exists on a
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.064|                    never-touched 25H2 install, or is only materialised
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.065|                    the first time the Settings page is opened, was not
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.066|                    verified. Behaviourally it makes no difference: absent
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.067|                    and 1 both mean the box is ticked.
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.068|
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.069|  Target          : HKCU\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Storage
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.070|                    Sense\Parameters\StoragePolicy /v "04" /t REG_DWORD -
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.071|                    OPTY.bat line 891, call :regset "%SSP%" "04" REG_DWORD
::X|EN|storagesense.tempfiles.072|                    1 "clean temp files"
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.001|  Ce que c est    : La case a cocher de l Assistant Stockage intitulee «
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.002|                    Maintenir le bon fonctionnement de Windows en
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.003|                    nettoyant automatiquement les fichiers temporaires du
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.004|                    systeme et des applications ». Sans elle, activer
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.005|                    l Assistant Stockage ne sert quasiment a rien.
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.006|
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.007|  Effet reel      : Met la valeur 04 de StoragePolicy a 1. Windows vide
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.008|                    les emplacements temporaires standard pendant son
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.009|                    passage planifie, avec ses propres filtres d age.
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.010|
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.011|  Gain            : C est la regle qui recupere reellement de la place.
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.012|                    Sur une machine utilisee tous les jours, on parle en
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.013|                    general de quelques centaines de Mo a deux Go par mois
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.014|                    qui, sinon, s empilent. C est de l espace, pas de la
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.015|                    vitesse : ni le debit ni la latence ne bougent.
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.016|
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.017|  Cout            : Une application qui stocke des donnees de travail dans
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.018|                    %TEMP% en esperant les retrouver des semaines plus
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.019|                    tard pourrait les perdre. C est rare et c est un
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.020|                    logiciel mal ecrit, et l Assistant Stockage applique
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.021|                    des filtres d age et d utilisation plutot que de vider
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.022|                    le dossier d un bloc.
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.023|
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.024|  Defaut Windows  : 1 - la case est cochee par defaut sur Windows 11, et 1
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.025|                    est exactement la valeur que l interface des
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.026|                    Parametres ecrit elle-meme : c est donc une
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.027|                    reaffirmation de l etat d origine, pas une troisieme
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.028|                    position.
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.029|
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.030|  Valeurs possibles :
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.031|    1                    : La regle « fichiers temporaires » est active.
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.032|                           Pendant son passage planifie, l Assistant
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.033|                           Stockage vide les emplacements temporaires
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.034|                           standard - %TEMP%, Windows\Temp, le cache
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.035|                           Delivery Optimization, les miniatures et les
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.036|                           cibles de nettoyage Windows Update - en
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.037|                           appliquant ses propres filtres d age et
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.038|                           d utilisation plutot qu en supprimant
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.039|                           aveuglement. C est la regle qui recupere
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.040|                           reellement de la place ; l interrupteur
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.041|                           principal seul ne recupere presque rien.
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.042|    0                    : La regle « fichiers temporaires » est
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.043|                           desactivee. L Assistant Stockage tourne
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.044|                           toujours selon sa frequence, mais ne traite
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.045|                           plus que la Corbeille, les Telechargements et
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.046|                           la deshydratation du cloud : sur une machine ou
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.047|                           la regle Telechargements est verrouillee sur
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.048|                           OFF, il ne fait donc quasiment rien. Activer
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.049|                           l interrupteur principal avec 04 a 0, c est
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.050|                           exactement la configuration qui fait dire que
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.051|                           l Assistant Stockage ne sert a rien.
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.052|    DELETE               : Valeur absente. La case des Parametres reste
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.053|                           cochee et Windows se comporte comme si elle
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.054|                           valait 1 : la retirer ne change rien
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.055|                           d observable. Ecrire 1 reproduit donc
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.056|                           exactement le comportement d origine,
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.057|                           contrairement aux cas 0-contre-absence ailleurs
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.058|                           dans ce script.
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.059|
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.060|  Pourquoi ces profils : Cinq reponses identiques, et c est le bon
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.061|                         tableau, pas un tableau paresseux : c est le
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.062|                         comportement livre par Windows et la raison
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.063|                         d etre de l Assistant Stockage, et il n existe
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.064|                         aucun profil pour lequel accumuler des fichiers
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.065|                         temporaires soit souhaitable. Un serveur y gagne
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.066|                         autant qu une machine de jeu, un portable autant
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.067|                         qu un poste bureautique, et WINDOWS est d accord
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.068|                         parce que 1 est la valeur livree. Le seul a
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.069|                         devoir refuser, c est celui qui utilise %TEMP%
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.070|                         comme dossier de travail personnel.
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.071|
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.072|  Non verifie (en)  : Whether StoragePolicy value 04 physically exists on
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.073|                      a never-touched 25H2 install, or is only
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.074|                      materialised the first time the Settings page is
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.075|                      opened, was not verified. Behaviourally it makes no
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.076|                      difference: absent and 1 both mean the box is
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.077|                      ticked.
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.078|
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.079|  Cible           : HKCU\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Storage
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.080|                    Sense\Parameters\StoragePolicy /v "04" /t REG_DWORD -
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.081|                    OPTY.bat line 891, call :regset "%SSP%" "04" REG_DWORD
::X|FR|storagesense.tempfiles.082|                    1 "clean temp files"
