:: ---- rad.wu.driversearch (repair) -------------------------------
::P|rad.wu.driversearch|1|1|1|1|1|
::T|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.001|RE-ALLOW DRIVER DELIVERY FROM WINDOWS UPDATE
::T|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.002|This is the more complete driver fix: it re-enables Windows Update as a driver source and clears three policy blocks that could silently keep drivers off even when the main switch looked correct.
::T|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.001|REAUTORISER LA LIVRAISON DES PILOTES PAR WINDOWS UPDATE
::T|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.002|C est le correctif pilotes le plus complet : il reactive Windows Update comme source de pilotes et supprime trois blocages de strategie qui pouvaient les empecher discretement meme quand l interrupteur principal semblait correct.
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.001|  What it is      : The RESTORE-menu version of the driver fix. It writes
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.002|                    the same SearchOrderConfig=1 as the other driver card,
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.003|                    and additionally removes the three policy values that
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.004|                    can block driver delivery even when SearchOrderConfig
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.005|                    is correct.
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.006|
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.007|  Actual effect   : Writes SearchOrderConfig=1, the shipped value, then
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.008|                    deletes ExcludeWUDriversInQualityUpdate,
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.009|                    DontSearchWindowsUpdate and
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.010|                    PreventDeviceMetadataFromNetwork if they exist.
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.011|                    Deletion rather than zeroing, because the default for
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.012|                    all three is that the value does not exist.
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.013|
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.014|  Gain            : A device you plug in tomorrow gets a driver instead of
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.015|                    sitting in Device Manager with an error and no clue
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.016|                    why. This version is the more complete one:
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.017|                    SearchOrderConfig=1 alone is not enough if
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.018|                    DontSearchWindowsUpdate is still present, because the
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.019|                    policy wins.
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.020|
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.021|  Cost            : Windows may occasionally install a generic driver over
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.022|                    a vendor one. If you pin your own GPU driver, note
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.023|                    that ExcludeWUDriversInQualityUpdate is deleted here -
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.024|                    re-set it to 1 yourself afterwards if that protection
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.025|                    is something you actually want.
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.026|
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.027|  Windows default : SearchOrderConfig=1, present. All three policy values
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.028|                    absent.
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.029|
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.030|  Possible values:
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.031|    1                    : SearchOrderConfig=1, the shipped value: Windows
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.032|                           may look on Windows Update for a driver a
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.033|                           device needs. Written unconditionally, and the
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.034|                           three policy leftovers below are deleted
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.035|                           alongside it, because any one of them alone is
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.036|                           enough to keep drivers blocked.
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.037|    0                    : SearchOrderConfig=0: Windows never looks on
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.038|                           Windows Update. Combined with
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.039|                           ExcludeWUDriversInQualityUpdate=1 this stops
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.040|                           ANY driver or firmware ever arriving, which is
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.041|                           the state this step exists to undo.
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.042|    2                    : SearchOrderConfig=2, the legacy Windows 7 'only
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.043|                           if not found locally' branch. No current
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.044|                           Windows UI writes it.
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.045|    ExcludeWUDriversInQualityUpdate=1 -> DELETE :
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.046|        While present and set to 1, quality updates never carry drivers or
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.047|        firmware. Its true default is ABSENT, so it is deleted rather than
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.048|        set to 0 - writing 0 would leave a policy key behind and keep the
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.049|        'managed by your organization' marker in Settings.
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.050|    DontSearchWindowsUpdate=1 -> DELETE :
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.051|        The Group Policy 'Specify search order for device driver source
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.052|        locations' set to 'Do not search Windows Update'. It overrides
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.053|        SearchOrderConfig, so fixing SearchOrderConfig alone while leaving
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.054|        this in place changes nothing. Default is absent.
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.055|    PreventDeviceMetadataFromNetwork=1 -> DELETE :
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.056|        Blocks the device metadata download - the icons, friendly names
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.057|        and manufacturer info that make a printer show as its model
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.058|        instead of a generic box. It does not block drivers, and no gain
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.059|        is claimed for removing it beyond devices being named properly
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.060|        again. Default is absent.
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.061|
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.062|  Why these profiles : Five identical answers for the same reason as the
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.063|                       other driver card: a device either gets a driver or
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.064|                       it does not, and no machine role benefits from the
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.065|                       second outcome. The extra content of this card -
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.066|                       the three policy deletes - does not change the
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.067|                       calculus either; all three defaults are absence, so
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.068|                       DELETE is simultaneously the repair and the shipped
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.069|                       state. The gaming exception people reach for (pin
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.070|                       the GPU driver) is a deliberate opt-in to be made
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.071|                       afterwards, not a reason to leave three blocking
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.072|                       policies in place.
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.073|
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.074|  Known problems  : Fixing SearchOrderConfig without removing
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.075|                    DontSearchWindowsUpdate is a silent no-op: the Group
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.076|                    Policy value takes precedence, so the machine still
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.077|                    refuses to fetch drivers while the registry looks
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.078|                    correct and OPTY reports the write as successful. That
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.079|                    is exactly the failure mode this step's extra deletes
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.080|                    prevent, and it is why the two driver cards are not
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.081|                    interchangeable.
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.082|
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.083|  Target          : OPTY.bat lines 1815-1818: call :regset "HKLM\SOFTWARE\
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.084|                    Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\DriverSearching"
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.085|                    "SearchOrderConfig" REG_DWORD 1, then :killkey on HKLM
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.086|                    \SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Windows\WindowsUpdate\Exc
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.087|                    ludeWUDriversInQualityUpdate, HKLM\SOFTWARE\Policies\M
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.088|                    icrosoft\Windows\DriverSearching\DontSearchWindowsUpda
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.089|                    te and HKLM\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Windows\Device
::X|EN|rad.wu.driversearch.090|                    Metadata\PreventDeviceMetadataFromNetwork
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.001|  Ce que c est    : La version « menu RESTORE » du correctif pilotes. Elle
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.002|                    ecrit le meme SearchOrderConfig=1 que l autre fiche
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.003|                    pilotes, et supprime en plus les trois valeurs de
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.004|                    strategie capables de bloquer la livraison meme quand
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.005|                    SearchOrderConfig est correct.
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.006|
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.007|  Effet reel      : Ecrit SearchOrderConfig=1, la valeur d origine, puis
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.008|                    supprime ExcludeWUDriversInQualityUpdate,
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.009|                    DontSearchWindowsUpdate et
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.010|                    PreventDeviceMetadataFromNetwork si elles existent.
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.011|                    Suppression et non mise a zero, parce que la valeur
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.012|                    par defaut des trois est l absence.
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.013|
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.014|  Gain            : Un peripherique branche demain obtient son pilote au
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.015|                    lieu de rester en erreur dans le Gestionnaire de
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.016|                    peripheriques. C est la version la plus complete :
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.017|                    SearchOrderConfig=1 seul ne suffit pas si
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.018|                    DontSearchWindowsUpdate est encore la, puisque la
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.019|                    strategie l emporte.
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.020|
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.021|  Cout            : Windows peut parfois poser un pilote generique par-
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.022|                    dessus celui du fabricant. Si vous figez votre pilote
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.023|                    graphique, notez qu ExcludeWUDriversInQualityUpdate
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.024|                    est supprimee ici : remettez-la a 1 vous-meme ensuite
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.025|                    si cette protection vous tient reellement a coeur.
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.026|
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.027|  Defaut Windows  : SearchOrderConfig=1, presente. Les trois valeurs de
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.028|                    strategie absentes.
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.029|
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.030|  Valeurs possibles :
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.031|    1                    : SearchOrderConfig=1, la valeur d origine :
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.032|                           Windows peut chercher sur Windows Update le
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.033|                           pilote dont un peripherique a besoin. Ecrite
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.034|                           sans condition, et les trois residus de
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.035|                           strategie ci-dessous sont supprimes en meme
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.036|                           temps, car un seul d entre eux suffit a
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.037|                           maintenir les pilotes bloques.
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.038|    0                    : SearchOrderConfig=0 : Windows ne regarde jamais
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.039|                           sur Windows Update. Combine a
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.040|                           ExcludeWUDriversInQualityUpdate=1, cela empeche
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.041|                           l arrivee de tout pilote ou firmware, et c est
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.042|                           l etat que cette etape existe pour defaire.
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.043|    2                    : SearchOrderConfig=2, l ancienne branche Windows
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.044|                           7 « seulement si introuvable localement ».
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.045|                           Aucune interface Windows actuelle ne l ecrit.
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.046|    ExcludeWUDriversInQualityUpdate=1 -> DELETE :
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.047|        Tant qu elle est presente et a 1, les mises a jour de qualite ne
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.048|        transportent plus ni pilote ni firmware. Sa vraie valeur par
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.049|        defaut est l ABSENCE : elle est donc supprimee plutot que mise a 0
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.050|        - ecrire 0 laisserait une cle de strategie et conserverait la
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.051|        mention « gere par votre organisation » dans les Parametres.
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.052|    DontSearchWindowsUpdate=1 -> DELETE :
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.053|        La strategie de groupe « Specifier l ordre de recherche des
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.054|        emplacements sources des pilotes » reglee sur « Ne pas rechercher
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.055|        sur Windows Update ». Elle prime sur SearchOrderConfig : corriger
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.056|        SearchOrderConfig seul en laissant celle-ci en place ne change
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.057|        rien. Valeur par defaut : absente.
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.058|    PreventDeviceMetadataFromNetwork=1 -> DELETE :
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.059|        Bloque le telechargement des metadonnees de peripherique - icones,
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.060|        noms lisibles et informations constructeur qui font apparaitre une
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.061|        imprimante sous son modele plutot qu en boitier generique. Elle ne
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.062|        bloque pas les pilotes, et aucun gain n est revendique pour sa
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.063|        suppression au-dela de peripheriques a nouveau correctement
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.064|        nommes. Valeur par defaut : absente.
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.065|
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.066|  Pourquoi ces profils : Cinq reponses identiques, pour la meme raison que
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.067|                         l autre fiche pilotes : un peripherique obtient
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.068|                         son pilote ou ne l obtient pas, et aucun role de
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.069|                         machine ne gagne au second cas. Le contenu
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.070|                         supplementaire de cette fiche - les trois
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.071|                         suppressions de strategie - ne change rien au
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.072|                         calcul : leur valeur par defaut a toutes les
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.073|                         trois est l absence, donc DELETE est a la fois la
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.074|                         reparation et l etat d origine. L exception
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.075|                         gaming qu on invoque volontiers (figer le pilote
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.076|                         graphique) est un choix deliberé a poser ensuite,
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.077|                         pas une raison de laisser trois strategies
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.078|                         bloquantes en place.
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.079|
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.080|  Problemes connus : Corriger SearchOrderConfig sans supprimer
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.081|                     DontSearchWindowsUpdate est une operation sans effet,
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.082|                     et silencieuse : la valeur de strategie de groupe
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.083|                     prime, donc la machine refuse toujours de chercher
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.084|                     des pilotes alors que le registre a l air correct et
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.085|                     qu OPTY annonce l ecriture reussie. C est precisement
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.086|                     le scenario que les suppressions supplementaires de
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.087|                     cette etape evitent, et c est pour cela que les deux
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.088|                     fiches pilotes ne sont pas interchangeables.
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.089|
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.090|  Cible           : OPTY.bat lines 1815-1818: call :regset "HKLM\SOFTWARE\
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.091|                    Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\DriverSearching"
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.092|                    "SearchOrderConfig" REG_DWORD 1, then :killkey on HKLM
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.093|                    \SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Windows\WindowsUpdate\Exc
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.094|                    ludeWUDriversInQualityUpdate, HKLM\SOFTWARE\Policies\M
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.095|                    icrosoft\Windows\DriverSearching\DontSearchWindowsUpda
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.096|                    te and HKLM\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Windows\Device
::X|FR|rad.wu.driversearch.097|                    Metadata\PreventDeviceMetadataFromNetwork
