:: ---- usb.selective.suspend.off (preference) -------------------------
::P|usb.selective.suspend.off|1|1|DELETE|DELETE|DELETE|
::T|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.001|DISABLE USB SELECTIVE SUSPEND (WHOLE MACHINE)
::T|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.002|Keeps every USB port powered at all times, which can fix a mouse, headset or controller that stutters or drops out after sitting idle - but it draws more power, which mainly matters on laptop battery life.
::T|FR|usb.selective.suspend.off.001|SUSPENSION SELECTIVE USB (REGLAGE VALABLE POUR TOUTE LA MACHINE)
::T|FR|usb.selective.suspend.off.002|Maintient chaque port USB sous pleine puissance en permanence, ce qui peut corriger une souris, un casque ou une manette qui saccade ou se coupe apres un moment d inactivite - mais ca consomme plus, ce qui compte surtout pour l autonomie d un portable.
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.001|  What it is      : USB selective suspend lets the hub driver idle out a
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.002|                    single inactive USB port and wake it on the next
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.003|                    transfer. It is normally controlled per power plan,
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.004|                    through the AC/DC "USB selective suspend setting"
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.005|                    under Power Options. DisableSelectiveSuspend is a
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.006|                    different knob: a machine-wide override read by the
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.007|                    USB hub driver itself, outside any power plan.
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.008|
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.009|  Actual effect   : Writes DisableSelectiveSuspend=1 directly under HKLM
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.010|                    \SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Services\USB, or removes
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.011|                    the value. This is a service parameter, not a power-
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.012|                    plan setting: it targets no single scheme, needs no
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.013|                    powercfg /setactive to take effect, and is not lost
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.014|                    when you switch power plans afterwards.
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.015|
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.016|  Gain            : The same fix as the per-plan setting, applied
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.017|                    harder: a mouse, headset, controller, webcam, DAC or
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.018|                    audio interface that hitches, crackles, or takes a
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.019|                    beat to respond after sitting idle - or one that
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.020|                    disappears from Device Manager and comes back.
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.021|                    Without that symptom, be clear about what you are
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.022|                    buying: nothing you can perceive, and no measurable
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.023|                    gain of any kind.
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.024|
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.025|  Cost            : USB devices stay powered continuously, on every
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.026|                    power plan, on both AC and DC. Trivial idle wattage
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.027|                    on a desktop; a real, measurable shortening of
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.028|                    battery life on a laptop, plus the risk of blocking
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.029|                    the deeper sleep states.
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.030|
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.031|  Windows default : The value is absent. Selective suspend then follows
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.032|                    whatever the USB setting on the active power plan
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.033|                    says - normally enabled on both AC and DC in the
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.034|                    shipped Balanced plan.
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.035|
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.036|  Possible values:
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.037|    1                    : Selective suspend force-disabled for every USB
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.038|                           hub, on every power plan, all the time. No
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.039|                           port ever suspends: full power and
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.040|                           enumeration always, on mains or on battery,
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.041|                           whichever plan is active.
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.042|    DELETE               : Value absent - the shipped state. The USB
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.043|                           setting carried by the active power plan
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.044|                           governs again, normally enabled, so idle
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.045|                           ports still suspend and wake on demand.
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.046|
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.047|  Why these profiles : This is one switch for the whole machine, with
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.048|                       no AC/DC split of its own, so it can only ever
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.049|                       be all or nothing. Gaming: 1, cheap insurance -
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.050|                       a controller or headset that needs a moment to
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.051|                       wake mid-session is exactly the symptom this
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.052|                       prevents, and a desktop pays nothing for it.
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.053|                       Server: 1, because a 24/7 box tends to have a USB
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.054|                       external drive, a UPS data cable or a tuner
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.055|                       dongle hanging off it, and those are exactly the
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.056|                       devices that come back badly from a suspend; it
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.057|                       runs on mains and nothing there is meant to
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.058|                       sleep anyway. Office: DELETE, a quiet family PC
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.059|                       has no symptom to fix and no reason to force
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.060|                       every USB port to full power all the time.
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.061|                       Laptop: DELETE, never forced - writing 1 here
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.062|                       would hold every USB port at full power even on
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.063|                       battery, with no way back to the AC-aware setting
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.064|                       carried by the plan itself; that is the opposite
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.065|                       of the Laptop mandate, so the power plan is left
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.066|                       to do its own job. Windows: DELETE, the value
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.067|                       ships absent.
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.068|
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.069|  Target          : HKLM\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Services\USB /v
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.070|                    DisableSelectiveSuspend (REG_DWORD), one machine-wide
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.071|                    value - not the per-plan powercfg GUID chain
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.072|                    (2a737441-... / 48e6b7a6-...) used elsewhere in this
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.073|                    script for other USB power settings - see :askreg
::X|EN|usb.selective.suspend.off.074|                    "usb.selective.suspend.off" in the System section.
::X|FR|usb.selective.suspend.off.001|  Ce que c est    : La suspension selective USB permet au pilote de hub
::X|FR|usb.selective.suspend.off.002|                    de mettre un port USB inactif en veille basse
::X|FR|usb.selective.suspend.off.003|                    consommation et de le reveiller au transfert suivant.
::X|FR|usb.selective.suspend.off.004|                    Elle est normalement pilotee par mode d alimentation,
::X|FR|usb.selective.suspend.off.005|                    via le reglage secteur/batterie "Parametres USB" des
::X|FR|usb.selective.suspend.off.006|                    options d alimentation. DisableSelectiveSuspend est un
::X|FR|usb.selective.suspend.off.007|                    reglage different : une surcharge valable pour toute
::X|FR|usb.selective.suspend.off.008|                    la machine, lue par le pilote de hub USB lui meme, en
::X|FR|usb.selective.suspend.off.009|                    dehors de tout mode d alimentation.
::X|FR|usb.selective.suspend.off.010|
::X|FR|usb.selective.suspend.off.011|  Effet reel      : Ecrit DisableSelectiveSuspend=1 directement sous HKLM
::X|FR|usb.selective.suspend.off.012|                    \SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Services\USB, ou supprime
::X|FR|usb.selective.suspend.off.013|                    la valeur. C est un parametre de service, pas un
::X|FR|usb.selective.suspend.off.014|                    reglage de mode d alimentation : il ne vise aucun mode
::X|FR|usb.selective.suspend.off.015|                    en particulier, n a besoin d aucun powercfg
::X|FR|usb.selective.suspend.off.016|                    /setactive pour s appliquer, et ne se perd pas si
::X|FR|usb.selective.suspend.off.017|                    vous changez de mode d alimentation ensuite.
::X|FR|usb.selective.suspend.off.018|
::X|FR|usb.selective.suspend.off.019|  Gain            : Le meme remede que le reglage par mode, applique
::X|FR|usb.selective.suspend.off.020|                    plus largement : une souris, un casque, une manette,
::X|FR|usb.selective.suspend.off.021|                    une webcam, un DAC ou une interface audio qui
::X|FR|usb.selective.suspend.off.022|                    saccade, gresille ou met un temps a repondre apres un
::X|FR|usb.selective.suspend.off.023|                    moment d inactivite - ou qui disparait du
::X|FR|usb.selective.suspend.off.024|                    Gestionnaire de peripheriques puis revient. Sans ce
::X|FR|usb.selective.suspend.off.025|                    symptome, rien de perceptible, et aucun gain
::X|FR|usb.selective.suspend.off.026|                    mesurable d aucune sorte.
::X|FR|usb.selective.suspend.off.027|
::X|FR|usb.selective.suspend.off.028|  Cout            : Les peripheriques USB restent alimentes en
::X|FR|usb.selective.suspend.off.029|                    permanence, sur tous les modes d alimentation,
::X|FR|usb.selective.suspend.off.030|                    secteur comme batterie. Consommation au repos
::X|FR|usb.selective.suspend.off.031|                    negligeable sur un fixe ; reduction reelle et
::X|FR|usb.selective.suspend.off.032|                    mesurable de l autonomie sur un portable, plus le
::X|FR|usb.selective.suspend.off.033|                    risque de bloquer les etats de veille profonds.
::X|FR|usb.selective.suspend.off.034|
::X|FR|usb.selective.suspend.off.035|  Defaut Windows  : La valeur est absente. La suspension selective suit
::X|FR|usb.selective.suspend.off.036|                    alors ce que dit le reglage USB du mode d alimentation
::X|FR|usb.selective.suspend.off.037|                    actif - normalement activee sur secteur comme sur
::X|FR|usb.selective.suspend.off.038|                    batterie dans le mode Utilisation normale d origine.
::X|FR|usb.selective.suspend.off.039|
::X|FR|usb.selective.suspend.off.040|  Valeurs possibles :
::X|FR|usb.selective.suspend.off.041|    1                    : Suspension selective forcee a l arret pour
::X|FR|usb.selective.suspend.off.042|                           chaque hub USB, sur tous les modes
::X|FR|usb.selective.suspend.off.043|                           d alimentation, tout le temps. Aucun port
::X|FR|usb.selective.suspend.off.044|                           n est jamais suspendu : pleine puissance et
::X|FR|usb.selective.suspend.off.045|                           enumeration en permanence, sur secteur comme
::X|FR|usb.selective.suspend.off.046|                           sur batterie, quel que soit le mode actif.
::X|FR|usb.selective.suspend.off.047|    DELETE               : Valeur absente - l etat d origine. Le
::X|FR|usb.selective.suspend.off.048|                           reglage USB porte par chaque mode
::X|FR|usb.selective.suspend.off.049|                           d alimentation s applique de nouveau,
::X|FR|usb.selective.suspend.off.050|                           normalement active, donc les ports inactifs
::X|FR|usb.selective.suspend.off.051|                           se suspendent et se reveillent toujours a la
