:: ---- rad.pwr.idledisable (repair) -------------------------------
::P|rad.pwr.idledisable|0|0|0|0|DELETE|
::T|EN|rad.pwr.idledisable.001|ALLOW CPU IDLE STATES (C-STATES)
::T|EN|rad.pwr.idledisable.002|Lets idle CPU cores power down again, undoing an old audio-latency tweak that forced them to stay awake - this is neutral to positive for performance too, since a cooler chip has more room to boost, and it always cuts power and fan noise.
::T|FR|rad.pwr.idledisable.001|ETATS DE REPOS DU CPU (C-STATES)
::T|FR|rad.pwr.idledisable.002|Laisse les coeurs CPU inactifs se reposer de nouveau, en annulant un vieux reglage de latence audio qui les forcait a rester eveilles - c est neutre a positif pour les performances aussi, un processeur plus frais ayant plus de marge pour booster, et ca reduit toujours la consommation et le bruit.
::X|EN|rad.pwr.idledisable.001|  What it is      : IDLEDISABLE=1 forbids the CPU from entering low-power
::X|EN|rad.pwr.idledisable.002|                    idle states. It comes from old real-time-audio and
::X|EN|rad.pwr.idledisable.003|                    latency guides written when C-state exit latency was
::X|EN|rad.pwr.idledisable.004|                    worth worrying about and boost algorithms did not
::X|EN|rad.pwr.idledisable.005|                    exist.
::X|EN|rad.pwr.idledisable.006|
::X|EN|rad.pwr.idledisable.007|  Actual effect   : OPTY writes 0 - idle allowed - and only when an
::X|EN|rad.pwr.idledisable.008|                    override exists on the active scheme and is not
::X|EN|rad.pwr.idledisable.009|                    already 0. If nothing is set, it reports that and does
::X|EN|rad.pwr.idledisable.010|                    nothing.
::X|EN|rad.pwr.idledisable.011|
::X|EN|rad.pwr.idledisable.012|  Gain            : Counter-intuitive but the mechanism is
::X|EN|rad.pwr.idledisable.013|                    straightforward: idle cores in a C-state stop
::X|EN|rad.pwr.idledisable.014|                    producing heat and stop drawing current, and modern
::X|EN|rad.pwr.idledisable.015|                    boost algorithms hand out clock speed in proportion to
::X|EN|rad.pwr.idledisable.016|                    exactly that thermal and current headroom. Blocking
::X|EN|rad.pwr.idledisable.017|                    idle keeps the whole package warm, so the cores doing
::X|EN|rad.pwr.idledisable.018|                    real work get less headroom to boost into. Undoing the
::X|EN|rad.pwr.idledisable.019|                    tweak is therefore neutral-to-positive for
::X|EN|rad.pwr.idledisable.020|                    performance, and clearly positive for power and noise.
::X|EN|rad.pwr.idledisable.021|
::X|EN|rad.pwr.idledisable.022|  Cost            : Exiting a deep C-state costs a wake latency measured
::X|EN|rad.pwr.idledisable.023|                    in microseconds. On a machine built for hard real-time
::X|EN|rad.pwr.idledisable.024|                    audio at very small ASIO buffers that is a defensible
::X|EN|rad.pwr.idledisable.025|                    thing to care about; in a game, in a browser, in a
::X|EN|rad.pwr.idledisable.026|                    compile, it is far below anything you could perceive
::X|EN|rad.pwr.idledisable.027|                    or measure.
::X|EN|rad.pwr.idledisable.028|
::X|EN|rad.pwr.idledisable.029|  Windows default : No override at all, and the effective behaviour is
::X|EN|rad.pwr.idledisable.030|                    idle states enabled.
::X|EN|rad.pwr.idledisable.031|
::X|EN|rad.pwr.idledisable.032|  Possible values:
::X|EN|rad.pwr.idledisable.033|    0                    : Idle states enabled - the default and the
::X|EN|rad.pwr.idledisable.034|                           correct value. When a core has nothing to do it
::X|EN|rad.pwr.idledisable.035|                           enters a C-state: clocks stopped, and in the
::X|EN|rad.pwr.idledisable.036|                           deeper states power gated off entirely. That is
::X|EN|rad.pwr.idledisable.037|                           what frees the thermal and current budget the
::X|EN|rad.pwr.idledisable.038|                           boost algorithm spends on the cores that are
::X|EN|rad.pwr.idledisable.039|                           actually working.
::X|EN|rad.pwr.idledisable.040|    1                    : Idle states disabled. The idle thread stops
::X|EN|rad.pwr.idledisable.041|                           halting the core and spins instead, so every
::X|EN|rad.pwr.idledisable.042|                           core stays awake and drawing power around the
::X|EN|rad.pwr.idledisable.043|                           clock. On any modern part this is the wrong
::X|EN|rad.pwr.idledisable.044|                           direction: boost on Zen 3/4/5 and on Raptor
::X|EN|rad.pwr.idledisable.045|                           Lake is granted out of thermal and current
::X|EN|rad.pwr.idledisable.046|                           headroom, and a package kept permanently warm
::X|EN|rad.pwr.idledisable.047|                           by idle cores has less of both to spend. You
::X|EN|rad.pwr.idledisable.048|                           pay continuous idle wattage and constant fan
::X|EN|rad.pwr.idledisable.049|                           noise to buy back a wake latency that is
::X|EN|rad.pwr.idledisable.050|                           measured in microseconds.
::X|EN|rad.pwr.idledisable.051|    DELETE               : Remove the override so the plan inherits. On a
::X|EN|rad.pwr.idledisable.052|                           clean install there is no override on this GUID
::X|EN|rad.pwr.idledisable.053|                           at all and idle states are simply enabled.
::X|EN|rad.pwr.idledisable.054|                           Byte-for-byte factory state; writing 0 behaves
::X|EN|rad.pwr.idledisable.055|                           the same but leaves a value that Windows never
::X|EN|rad.pwr.idledisable.056|                           wrote.
::X|EN|rad.pwr.idledisable.057|
::X|EN|rad.pwr.idledisable.058|  Why these profiles : All four working profiles write 0 and there is no
::X|EN|rad.pwr.idledisable.059|                       case among them for anything else - not even
::X|EN|rad.pwr.idledisable.060|                       gaming, which is the profile this tweak was
