:: ---- rp.throttle.window (repair) --------------------------------
::P|rp.throttle.window|DELETE|DELETE|DELETE|DELETE|DELETE|
::T|EN|rp.throttle.window.001|24-HOUR RESTORE POINT LIMIT (SETUP/REPAIR PATH)
::T|EN|rp.throttle.window.002|The same reliability fix as the setup step: briefly lifts Windows built-in 24-hour cooldown so a restore point can actually be created before the setup or repair path changes anything - a safety measure, not a performance change.
::T|FR|rp.throttle.window.001|LA FENETRE DE 24 H DES POINTS DE RESTAURATION (CHEMIN SETUP/REPARATION)
::T|FR|rp.throttle.window.002|Le meme correctif de fiabilite que l etape de configuration : leve brievement le delai de 24 h de Windows pour qu un point de restauration soit vraiment cree avant que le chemin de configuration ou de reparation ne change quoi que ce soit - une mesure de securite, pas de performance.
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.001|  What it is      : Windows refuses a second System Restore point within
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.002|                    1440 minutes of the previous one.
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.003|                    SystemRestorePointCreationFrequency holds that window
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.004|                    in minutes. OPTY lifts it to 0 for the duration of its
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.005|                    own checkpoint and puts it back afterwards.
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.006|
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.007|  Actual effect   : With the throttle at 0, OPTY's restore point is
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.008|                    created even if Windows Update or another tool already
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.009|                    made one today. What you decide here is only what is
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.010|                    left behind after the checkpoint: an explicit 1440, or
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.011|                    nothing at all.
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.012|
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.013|  Gain            : The checkpoint is reliable instead of a coin flip.
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.014|                    Without it, the restore point fails silently on
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.015|                    exactly the days you run the script twice - which are
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.016|                    the days you most want a way back.
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.017|
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.018|  Cost            : Nothing behavioural. At 1440 the value has no effect
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.019|                    whatsoever; absent, it has no effect either. The only
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.020|                    real risk is the value being left at 0 if the run is
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.021|                    interrupted between the two lines, which disables
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.022|                    System Protection's 24-hour guard for everything on
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.023|                    the machine, not just OPTY.
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.024|
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.025|  Windows default : The value is absent, and Windows then applies a
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.026|                    1440-minute window.
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.027|
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.028|  Possible values:
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.029|    0                    : No throttle. Any caller can create a restore
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.030|                           point at any time. This is the state OPTY needs
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.031|                           for the two seconds around its Checkpoint-
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.032|                           Computer call, and the state you do not want it
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.033|                           left in.
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.034|    1440                 : The 24-hour window, written explicitly.
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.035|                           Identical behaviour to the shipped state, but a
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.036|                           value present where a factory machine has
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.037|                           nothing.
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.038|    DELETE               : Value absent, which is the factory state and
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.039|                           which Windows treats as 1440 minutes. Same
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.040|                           behaviour, no residue.
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.041|    any integer N        : A custom window in minutes. Only ever written
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.042|                           by a script or by hand - no Windows dialog
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.043|                           offers it.
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.044|
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.045|  Why these profiles : Five identical answers, because there is genuinely
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.046|                       nothing profile-dependent about a restore point.
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.047|                       DELETE rather than 1440 for the same reason as reg-
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.048|                       srp-creation-frequency: absent already means 1440,
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.049|                       so deleting gives the shipped behaviour with
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.050|                       nothing left in the registry. Implementation note
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.051|                       that matters more than the answer itself: this card
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.052|                       and reg-srp-creation-frequency describe the same
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.053|                       DWORD written by the same two adjacent lines of
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.054|                       :restore_point. They should be one question. Asking
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.055|                       twice invites two different answers for one value,
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.056|                       and the second write silently wins.
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.057|
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.058|  Known problems  : On this machine the value currently reads 0, so a
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.059|                    previous run wrote 0 and never restored the throttle.
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.060|                    Every application that creates restore points has been
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.061|                    unthrottled here ever since.
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.062|
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.063|  Target          : HKLM\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.064|                    NT\CurrentVersion\SystemRestore /v
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.065|                    SystemRestorePointCreationFrequency (REG_DWORD) - the
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.066|                    SAME value and the SAME two lines as reg-srp-creation-
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.067|                    frequency: OPTY.bat line 3622 writes 0, line 3631
::X|EN|rp.throttle.window.068|                    writes the throttle back, both inside :restore_point
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.001|  Ce que c est    : Windows refuse un deuxieme point de restauration dans
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.002|                    les 1440 minutes qui suivent le precedent.
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.003|                    SystemRestorePointCreationFrequency contient cette
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.004|                    fenetre en minutes. OPTY la leve a 0 le temps de son
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.005|                    propre point, puis la remet.
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.006|
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.007| Effet reel : Avec le verrou a 0, le point d OPTY est cree meme si
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.008|                    Windows Update ou un autre outil en a deja fait un
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.009| aujourd hui. Ce que vous decidez ici, c est uniquement
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.010|                    ce qui reste apres le point : un 1440 explicite, ou
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.011|                    rien du tout.
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.012|
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.013| Gain : Le point devient fiable au lieu d etre un coup de des.
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.014|                    Sans ca, il echoue en silence exactement les jours ou
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.015| vous lancez le script deux fois - c est-a-dire les
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.016| jours ou vous avez le plus besoin d un retour en
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.017|                    arriere.
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.018|
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.019|  Cout            : Aucun effet sur le comportement. A 1440 la valeur ne
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.020|                    fait rien ; absente, elle ne fait rien non plus. Le
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.021| seul vrai risque, c est qu elle reste a 0 si
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.022| l execution est interrompue entre les deux lignes, ce
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.023|                    qui desactive le garde-fou de 24 h de la Protection du
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.024|                    systeme pour toute la machine, pas seulement pour
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.025|                    OPTY.
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.026|
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.027|  Defaut Windows  : La valeur est absente, et Windows applique alors une
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.028|                    fenetre de 1440 minutes.
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.029|
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.030|  Valeurs possibles :
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.031| 0 : Aucun verrou. N importe quel appelant peut
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.032|                           creer un point de restauration a tout moment.
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.033| C est l etat dont OPTY a besoin pendant les
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.034|                           deux secondes qui entourent son appel a
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.035| Checkpoint-Computer, et l etat dans lequel il
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.036|                           ne faut pas le laisser.
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.037|    1440                 : La fenetre de 24 h, ecrite explicitement.
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.038| Comportement identique a l etat livre, mais une
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.039| valeur presente la ou une machine d usine n a
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.040|                           rien.
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.041| DELETE : Valeur absente, c est-a-dire l etat d usine,
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.042|                           que Windows traite comme 1440 minutes. Meme
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.043|                           comportement, aucun residu.
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.044|    any integer N        : Une fenetre personnalisee en minutes. Ecrite
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.045|                           uniquement par un script ou a la main - aucune
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.046|                           boite de dialogue Windows ne la propose.
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.047|
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.048| Pourquoi ces profils : Cinq reponses identiques, parce qu il n y a
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.049|                         vraiment rien de dependant du profil dans un
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.050|                         point de restauration. DELETE plutot que 1440
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.051|                         pour la meme raison que dans reg-srp-creation-
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.052|                         frequency : absente signifie deja 1440, donc
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.053| supprimer donne le comportement d origine sans
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.054|                         rien laisser dans le registre. Note
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.055| d implementation plus importante que la reponse
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.056|                         elle-meme : cette carte et reg-srp-creation-
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.057|                         frequency decrivent le meme DWORD, ecrit par les
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.058|                         deux memes lignes voisines de :restore_point. Il
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.059| faut une seule question. En poser deux, c est
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.060|                         inviter deux reponses differentes pour une seule
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.061| valeur, et c est la seconde ecriture qui
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.062| l emporte en silence.
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.063|
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.064|  Problemes connus : Sur cette machine, la valeur vaut actuellement 0 :
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.065|                     une execution precedente a ecrit 0 sans jamais
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.066|                     retablir le verrou. Toutes les applications qui
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.067|                     creent des points de restauration sont dereglementees
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.068|                     ici depuis.
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.069|
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.070|  Cible           : HKLM\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.071|                    NT\CurrentVersion\SystemRestore /v
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.072|                    SystemRestorePointCreationFrequency (REG_DWORD) - the
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.073|                    SAME value and the SAME two lines as reg-srp-creation-
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.074|                    frequency: OPTY.bat line 3622 writes 0, line 3631
::X|FR|rp.throttle.window.075|                    writes the throttle back, both inside :restore_point
