:: ---- mmcss.network.throttling (preference) --------------------------
::P|mmcss.network.throttling|10|0xffffffff|10|10|10|
::T|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.001|NETWORK SPEED CAP DURING AUDIO PLAYBACK
::T|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.002|Windows secretly caps your network speed to about 100 Mbit/s whenever audio is playing, to protect against crackling - lifting the cap only helps if your connection is faster than that and you move big files while listening, and it very slightly raises the risk of audio dropouts.
::T|FR|mmcss.network.throttling.001|LE PLAFOND RESEAU MMCSS PENDANT LA LECTURE AUDIO
::T|FR|mmcss.network.throttling.002|Windows plafonne en secret votre debit reseau a environ 100 Mbit/s des qu un son joue, pour eviter les craquements - lever ce plafond n aide que si votre connexion est plus rapide et que vous transferez de gros fichiers en ecoutant, et ca augmente tres legerement le risque de coupures audio.
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.001|  What it is      : NetworkThrottlingIndex caps how many network packets
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.002|                    per millisecond the system processes - but only while
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.003|                    an MMCSS-registered multimedia or audio stream is
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.004|                    playing. It exists so network interrupt work cannot
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.005|                    starve audio threads and produce crackling. When
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.006|                    nothing is playing, the cap does not apply and your
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.007|                    connection is unaffected.
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.008|
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.009|  Actual effect   : 10 is the shipped value and works out at roughly
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.010|                    100-120 Mbit/s during playback. 4294967295
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.011|                    (0xFFFFFFFF) removes the ceiling entirely, and removes
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.012|                    the protection along with it.
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.013|
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.014|  Gain            : Strictly conditional on two things being true at once:
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.015|                    your link is faster than about 100 Mbit/s, AND you
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.016|                    transfer large amounts of data while audio is playing.
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.017|                    Then lifting the cap gives you your real line rate
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.018|                    instead of a soft ceiling nothing in Windows tells you
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.019|                    about. It is honestly measurable - run a large
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.020|                    download with music playing, before and after. If your
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.021|                    connection is under 100 Mbit/s, or you do not download
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.022|                    during playback, the gain is zero and you keep the
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.023|                    risk.
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.024|
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.025|  Cost            : Audio dropouts and crackling under heavy network load,
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.026|                    which is the exact failure the cap was introduced to
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.027|                    prevent. Nothing else is affected - this is not a
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.028|                    general network setting and it does not touch latency,
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.029|                    gaming traffic or anything that happens while audio is
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.030|                    silent.
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.031|
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.032|  Windows default : 10 (0xa), and unusually for a tuning value it is
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.033|                    genuinely present by default on a clean Windows 11
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.034|                    install - so writing 10 restores the shipped state
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.035|                    exactly, and deleting it does not.
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.036|
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.037|  Possible values:
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.038|    10                   : 0xa, the shipped value. While an MMCSS-
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.039|                           registered multimedia stream is playing, the
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.040|                           system processes roughly 10 network packets per
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.041|                           millisecond; with standard 1500-byte frames
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.042|                           that works out somewhere around 100-120 Mbit/s.
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.043|                           Outside audio playback the cap does not apply
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.044|                           at all and your link runs at full speed. This
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.045|                           is the value that protects audio threads from
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.046|                           being starved by network DPC work.
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.047|    4294967295           : 0xFFFFFFFF - the documented 'no throttling'
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.048|                           sentinel. The cap is removed entirely, and with
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.049|                           it the protection audio threads had against
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.050|                           network interrupt work. Your link runs at full
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.051|                           speed during playback. On a modern multi-core
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.052|                           machine with RSS spreading network DPCs across
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.053|                           cores the starvation risk is much lower than it
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.054|                           was when the cap was designed, but it is not
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.055|                           zero.
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.056|    any integer between 1 and 69 :
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.057|        An intermediate cap: the number is packets per millisecond, so 20
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.058|        is twice the shipped ceiling, 70 is seven times it. Legal, but
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.059|        there is no principled way to choose one - you would be picking a
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.060|        number between 'the value Microsoft tested' and 'off' with no way
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.061|        to measure where you landed. If you are going to move off 10, move
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.062|        to 0xFFFFFFFF and A/B it honestly.
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.063|    DELETE               : Value absent. Unlike most of the settings in
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.064|                           this script, absent is NOT the shipped state
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.065|                           here - a clean Windows 11 install really does
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.066|                           have 10 present. Deleting it is a change, not a
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.067|                           restoration, so write 10 instead.
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.068|
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.069|  Why these profiles : This is a pure throughput-versus-audio-protection
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.070|                       trade, and exactly one of the five profiles is
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.071|                       defined by throughput. Server lifts it: a hosting
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.072|                       box moves large amounts of data and has no
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.073|                       interactive audio worth protecting - on a truly
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.074|                       headless machine the cap may never even engage, so
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.075|                       the gain there is partly theoretical, but nothing
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.076|                       is lost either. Gaming keeps 10 on purpose, against
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.077|                       the folklore: the gaming profile is defined by
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.078|                       latency, audio crackling IS a latency failure, and
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.079|                       game traffic is a trickle of small UDP packets that
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.080|                       never comes near 10 packets per millisecond. Office
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.081|                       and Laptop keep 10 - no throughput case, and a
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.082|                       laptop is the machine most likely to be doing video
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.083|                       calls. Windows keeps 10 because that is the shipped
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.084|                       value.
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.085|
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.086|  Known problems  : The concrete failure at 0xFFFFFFFF is the one the cap
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.087|                    exists to prevent: audio thread starvation under
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.088|                    network DPC load, reported by DAW users as ASIO buffer
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.089|                    underruns and clicks in Reaper and Cubase during large
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.090|                    file transfers. Anyone doing music production should
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.091|                    stay at 10.
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.092|
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.093|  Unverified      : The 100-120 Mbit/s figure follows from 10 packets/ms
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.094|                    at 1500-byte frames, but the effective ceiling depends
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.095|                    on your actual frame size and offload settings, so
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.096|                    treat it as an order of magnitude rather than a
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.097|                    number. I also cannot tell you how often audio
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.098|                    starvation actually occurs at 0xFFFFFFFF on a modern
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.099|                    multi-core machine with RSS enabled - the mechanism is
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.100|                    real and documented, the frequency is not something I
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.101|                    have a measurement for.
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.102|
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.103|  Target          : HKLM\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.104|                    NT\CurrentVersion\Multimedia\SystemProfile /v
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.105|                    NetworkThrottlingIndex (REG_DWORD) - written as 10 at
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.106|                    OPTY.bat lines 1520, 1599, 1787, 2842 and 2854;
::X|EN|mmcss.network.throttling.107|                    written as 4294967295 at line 2860 in :net_prof_thr
::X|FR|mmcss.network.throttling.001|  Ce que c est    : NetworkThrottlingIndex limite le nombre de paquets
::X|FR|mmcss.network.throttling.002|                    reseau traites par milliseconde - mais uniquement tant
::X|FR|mmcss.network.throttling.003| qu un flux multimedia ou audio enregistre aupres de
::X|FR|mmcss.network.throttling.004|                    MMCSS est en lecture. Il existe pour que le travail
::X|FR|mmcss.network.throttling.005| d interruption reseau n affame pas les threads audio
::X|FR|mmcss.network.throttling.006|                    et ne provoque pas de craquements. Quand rien ne joue,
::X|FR|mmcss.network.throttling.007| le plafond ne s applique pas et votre connexion n est
::X|FR|mmcss.network.throttling.008|                    pas concernee.
::X|FR|mmcss.network.throttling.009|
::X|FR|mmcss.network.throttling.010| Effet reel : 10 est la valeur d origine et revient a environ
::X|FR|mmcss.network.throttling.011|                    100-120 Mbit/s pendant la lecture. 4294967295
::X|FR|mmcss.network.throttling.012|                    (0xFFFFFFFF) supprime completement le plafond, et la
::X|FR|mmcss.network.throttling.013|                    protection avec.
::X|FR|mmcss.network.throttling.014|
::X|FR|mmcss.network.throttling.015|  Gain            : Strictement conditionne a deux choses simultanees :
::X|FR|mmcss.network.throttling.016|                    votre lien depasse environ 100 Mbit/s, ET vous
::X|FR|mmcss.network.throttling.017| transferez de gros volumes pendant qu un son joue.
::X|FR|mmcss.network.throttling.018|                    Alors lever le plafond vous rend votre debit reel au
::X|FR|mmcss.network.throttling.019| lieu d un plafond invisible dont Windows ne vous dit
::X|FR|mmcss.network.throttling.020| rien. C est honnetement mesurable : lancez un gros
::X|FR|mmcss.network.throttling.021|                    telechargement avec de la musique, avant et apres. Si
::X|FR|mmcss.network.throttling.022|                    votre connexion est sous 100 Mbit/s, ou si vous ne
::X|FR|mmcss.network.throttling.023|                    telechargez pas pendant la lecture, le gain est nul et
::X|FR|mmcss.network.throttling.024|                    vous gardez le risque.
::X|FR|mmcss.network.throttling.025|
::X|FR|mmcss.network.throttling.026|  Cout            : Des coupures et des craquements audio sous forte
::X|FR|mmcss.network.throttling.027|                    charge reseau, exactement la panne que ce plafond a
::X|FR|mmcss.network.throttling.028| ete introduit pour eviter. Rien d autre n est touche :
::X|FR|mmcss.network.throttling.029| ce n est pas un reglage reseau general, il ne concerne
::X|FR|mmcss.network.throttling.030|                    ni la latence, ni le trafic de jeu, ni quoi que ce
::X|FR|mmcss.network.throttling.031| soit quand l audio est silencieux.
::X|FR|mmcss.network.throttling.032|
::X|FR|mmcss.network.throttling.033|  Defaut Windows  : 10 (0xa), et fait rare pour une valeur de reglage,
::X|FR|mmcss.network.throttling.034|                    elle est reellement presente par defaut sur une
::X|FR|mmcss.network.throttling.035|                    installation propre de Windows 11 - ecrire 10 restaure
::X|FR|mmcss.network.throttling.036| donc exactement l etat livre, la supprimer non.
::X|FR|mmcss.network.throttling.037|
::X|FR|mmcss.network.throttling.038|  Valeurs possibles :
::X|FR|mmcss.network.throttling.039| 10 : 0xa, la valeur d origine. Tant qu un flux
::X|FR|mmcss.network.throttling.040|                           multimedia enregistre aupres de MMCSS est en
::X|FR|mmcss.network.throttling.041|                           lecture, le systeme traite environ 10 paquets
::X|FR|mmcss.network.throttling.042|                           reseau par milliseconde ; avec des trames
::X|FR|mmcss.network.throttling.043|                           standard de 1500 octets, ca revient a peu pres
::X|FR|mmcss.network.throttling.044|                           a 100-120 Mbit/s. En dehors de la lecture
::X|FR|mmcss.network.throttling.045| audio, le plafond ne s applique pas du tout et
::X|FR|mmcss.network.throttling.046| votre lien tourne a plein debit. C est cette
::X|FR|mmcss.network.throttling.047| valeur qui protege les threads audio d etre
