:: ---- rad.hwschmode (preference) -------------------------------------
::P|rad.hwschmode|2|2|2|2|2|
::T|EN|rad.hwschmode.001|TURN ON HARDWARE GPU SCHEDULING (HAGS)
::T|EN|rad.hwschmode.002|Turns on Hardware-Accelerated GPU Scheduling - not a real FPS gain, the difference measured stays inside normal run-to-run noise, but some features like NVIDIA DLSS Frame Generation refuse to run without it.
::T|FR|rad.hwschmode.001|ACTIVER LA PLANIFICATION GPU MATERIELLE (HAGS)
::T|FR|rad.hwschmode.002|Active la planification GPU materielle (HAGS) - ce n est pas un vrai gain de FPS, l ecart mesure reste dans le bruit normal d une execution a l autre, mais certaines fonctions comme NVIDIA DLSS Frame Generation refusent de fonctionner sans elle.
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.001|  What it is      : HwSchMode decides who owns the GPU's work queue: the
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.002|                    CPU-side driver (1) or a scheduling processor on the
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.003|                    GPU itself (2).
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.004|
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.005|  Actual effect   : Writes 2 unconditionally, after reading the current
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.006|                    value so the report can distinguish a repair from a
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.007|                    no-op. Takes effect after a reboot, and only on a GPU
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.008|                    and driver that report support.
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.009|
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.010|  Gain            : Not FPS - independent testing puts the difference
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.011|                    inside run-to-run noise on most systems, and any guide
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.012|                    promising frames from this is selling you nothing. The
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.013|                    substantiated reason to have it on is feature support:
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.014|                    NVIDIA DLSS Frame Generation will not run with
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.015|                    hardware-accelerated GPU scheduling off, and current
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.016|                    AMD and NVIDIA drivers are developed and validated
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.017|                    with it enabled. If a specific feature on your card
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.018|                    lists HAGS as a requirement, that feature's own
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.019|                    release notes are the authority - this card does not
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.020|                    claim one on AMD's behalf.
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.021|
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.022|  Cost            : A reboot. Drivers from the 2020-2021 era were
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.023|                    associated with stutter and with capture software
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.024|                    losing track of the game window; those reports have
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.025|                    largely stopped. On a GPU or driver without hardware
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.026|                    scheduling support, writing 2 is inert rather than
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.027|                    harmful - dxgkrnl checks the driver's capability and
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.028|                    ignores the value.
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.029|
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.030|  Windows default : 2 wherever the GPU and driver support hardware
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.031|                    scheduling, 1 where they do not. The value is present
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.032|                    on a stock machine, so the default here is a value,
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.033|                    not an absence.
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.034|
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.035|  Possible values:
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.036|    2                    : Hardware scheduling. A scheduling processor on
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.037|                           the GPU owns the work queue; the CPU-side
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.038|                           driver only hands work over instead of batching
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.039|                           and pacing every submission itself. Removes
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.040|                           some per-submission CPU work and a layer of
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.041|                           buffering. Requires a WDDM 2.7 or newer driver
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.042|                           that reports the capability - on hardware that
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.043|                           does not, dxgkrnl ignores the value entirely
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.044|                           and the Graphics settings toggle is not even
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.045|                           shown. Reboot to take effect.
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.046|    1                    : Software scheduling - the pre-WDDM-2.7
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.047|                           arrangement, where the driver's kernel-mode
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.048|                           component on the CPU batches command buffers
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.049|                           and decides when they go to the GPU. This is
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.050|                           what Windows leaves on hardware that cannot do
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.051|                           more, and it is the value the A/B diagnostic
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.052|                           writes. It is not the Windows default on a
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.053|                           modern GPU.
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.054|    DELETE               : Not a restore here, unlike the overlay values.
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.055|                           HwSchMode is a value Windows and the driver
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.056|                           installer write themselves, so a stock machine
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.057|                           has it present. Deleting it leaves dxgkrnl on
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.058|                           its built-in fallback and the Graphics settings
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.059|                           page with nothing selected - a state a fresh
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.060|                           install does not produce. OPTY writes 2 rather
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.061|                           than deleting for exactly this reason.
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.062|
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.063|  Why these profiles : All five write 2, and that is a finding rather than
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.064|                       a shrug. Two is what a supported machine ships
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.065|                       with, and on unsupported hardware the value is
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.066|                       ignored, so there is no profile where having 2 on
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.067|                       disk is wrong. Nobody has published a power or
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.068|                       battery delta for hardware scheduling in either
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.069|                       direction, so the laptop profile gets the same
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.070|                       answer instead of an invented one - claiming a
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.071|                       battery cost here would be exactly the folklore
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.072|                       this rewrite exists to remove. Server writes it
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.073|                       too: a box transcoding in Plex runs the same driver
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.074|                       stack that ships validated with it on. The only
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.075|                       real reason to hold 1 is a stutter or capture bug
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.076|                       you have bisected yourself, and that lives on the
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.077|                       A/B card.
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.078|
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.079|  Known problems  : Nothing current. The historical report worth knowing:
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.080|                    on early HAGS drivers, OBS and similar capture tools
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.081|                    could lose the game capture source after enabling it.
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.082|                    If you hit that today, the A/B card is how you confirm
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.083|                    it before blaming anything else.
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.084|
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.085|  Unverified      : Two things worth fixing in the source, not in the
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.086|                    card. First, this write sits in the repair-and-
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.087|                    defaults path, but choosing a GPU scheduling mode is a
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.088|                    preference by the project's own rule and should be
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.089|                    asked rather than asserted there. Second, the comment
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.090|                    above line 1808 in OPTY.bat still reads 'HAGS is
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.091|                    driver-assumed on RDNA3 since Adrenalin 23.12.1 and
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.092|                    Anti-Lag 2 needs it' - that is the exact claim the
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.093|                    audit refuted and it should be replaced with the DLSS
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.094|                    Frame Generation wording. Separately, I have not
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.095|                    verified byte-for-byte that HwSchMode is present on a
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.096|                    fresh 25H2 install before any vendor driver is
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.097|                    installed, and machines do turn up with HwSchMode=0,
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.098|                    whose meaning I could not confirm; OPTY should never
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.099|                    write 0.
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.100|
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.101|  Target          : call :regset
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.102|                    HKLM\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\GraphicsDrivers
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.103|                    HwSchMode REG_DWORD 2 - OPTY.bat line 1808, repair-
::X|EN|rad.hwschmode.104|                    and-defaults path
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.001|  Ce que c est    : HwSchMode designe qui possede la file de travail du
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.002|                    GPU : le pilote cote CPU (1) ou un processeur
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.003|                    d ordonnancement sur le GPU lui-meme (2).
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.004|
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.005|  Effet reel      : Ecrit 2 sans condition, apres avoir lu la valeur en
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.006|                    place pour que le rapport puisse distinguer une
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.007|                    reparation d une non-operation. Effectif apres
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.008|                    redemarrage, et uniquement si le GPU et le pilote
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.009|                    declarent la capacite.
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.010|
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.011|  Gain            : Pas des images par seconde : les tests independants
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.012|                    placent l ecart dans le bruit d une execution a
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.013|                    l autre sur la plupart des machines, et tout guide qui
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.014|                    vous promet des FPS ici ne vend rien. La raison etayee
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.015|                    de l activer, c est le support des fonctionnalites :
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.016|                    NVIDIA DLSS Frame Generation refuse de fonctionner si
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.017|                    la planification GPU materielle est desactivee, et les
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.018|                    pilotes AMD et NVIDIA actuels sont developpes et
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.019|                    valides avec elle active. Si une fonction precise de
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.020|                    votre carte exige HAGS, ce sont ses propres notes de
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.021|                    version qui font foi : cette carte n invente rien au
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.022|                    nom d AMD.
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.023|
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.024|  Cout            : Un redemarrage. Les pilotes de la periode 2020-2021
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.025|                    ont ete associes a des saccades et a des logiciels de
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.026|                    capture qui perdaient la fenetre du jeu ; ces
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.027|                    signalements ont largement cesse. Sur un GPU ou un
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.028|                    pilote sans support de la planification materielle,
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.029|                    ecrire 2 est inerte plutot que nuisible : dxgkrnl
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.030|                    consulte la capacite du pilote et ignore la valeur.
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.031|
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.032|  Defaut Windows  : 2 partout ou le GPU et le pilote gerent la
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.033|                    planification materielle, 1 la ou ils ne la gerent
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.034|                    pas. La valeur est presente sur une machine d origine
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.035|                    : ici le defaut est une valeur, pas une absence.
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.036|
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.037|  Valeurs possibles :
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.038|    2                    : Planification materielle. Un processeur
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.039|                           d ordonnancement sur le GPU possede la file de
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.040|                           travail ; le pilote cote CPU se contente de lui
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.041|                           passer le travail au lieu de regrouper et de
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.042|                           cadencer lui-meme chaque soumission. Cela
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.043|                           retire un peu de travail CPU par soumission et
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.044|                           un etage de tampon. Il faut un pilote WDDM 2.7
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.045|                           ou plus recent qui declare la capacite : sur un
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.046|                           materiel qui ne la declare pas, dxgkrnl ignore
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.047|                           purement et simplement la valeur et
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.048|                           l interrupteur des Parametres graphiques
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.049|                           n apparait meme pas. Redemarrage requis.
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.050|    1                    : Planification logicielle : l organisation
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.051|                           d avant WDDM 2.7, ou le composant noyau du
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.052|                           pilote, cote CPU, regroupe les tampons de
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.053|                           commandes et decide quand ils partent vers le
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.054|                           GPU. C est ce que Windows laisse sur un
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.055|                           materiel incapable de mieux, et c est la valeur
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.056|                           qu ecrit le test A/B. Ce n est pas le defaut
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.057|                           Windows sur un GPU moderne.
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.058|    DELETE               : Ici, contrairement aux valeurs d overlay, ce
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.059|                           n est pas un retour a l origine. HwSchMode est
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.060|                           une valeur que Windows et l installateur du
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.061|                           pilote ecrivent eux-memes : une machine
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.062|                           d origine la possede. La supprimer laisse
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.063|                           dxgkrnl sur son repli interne et la page des
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.064|                           Parametres graphiques sans rien de selectionne,
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.065|                           un etat qu une installation neuve ne produit
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.066|                           pas. C est precisement pour cela qu OPTY ecrit
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.067|                           2 plutot que de supprimer.
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.068|
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.069|  Pourquoi ces profils : Les cinq ecrivent 2, et c est un constat, pas un
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.070|                         haussement d epaules. 2 est ce qu embarque une
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.071|                         machine compatible, et sur un materiel
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.072|                         incompatible la valeur est ignoree : il n existe
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.073|                         aucun profil pour lequel avoir 2 sur le disque
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.074|                         soit une erreur. Personne n a publie d ecart de
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.075|                         consommation ou d autonomie lie a la
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.076|                         planification materielle, dans un sens ou dans
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.077|                         l autre : le profil portable recoit donc la meme
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.078|                         reponse plutot qu une reponse inventee -
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.079|                         pretendre a un cout en batterie ici serait
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.080|                         exactement le folklore que cette reecriture
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.081|                         cherche a eliminer. Le serveur l ecrit aussi :
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.082|                         une machine qui transcode sous Plex fait tourner
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.083|                         la meme pile de pilotes, livree validee avec
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.084|                         l option active. La seule vraie raison de rester
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.085|                         a 1, c est une saccade ou un bug de capture que
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.086|                         vous avez vous-meme isole, et cela releve de la
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.087|                         carte de test A/B.
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.088|
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.089|  Problemes connus : Rien d actuel. Le signalement historique a connaitre
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.090|                     : sur les premiers pilotes HAGS, OBS et les outils de
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.091|                     capture equivalents pouvaient perdre la source de
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.092|                     capture du jeu apres activation. Si cela vous arrive
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.093|                     aujourd hui, la carte de test A/B est le moyen de le
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.094|                     confirmer avant d accuser autre chose.
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.095|
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.096|  Non verifie (en)  : Two things worth fixing in the source, not in the
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.097|                      card. First, this write sits in the repair-and-
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.098|                      defaults path, but choosing a GPU scheduling mode is
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.099|                      a preference by the project s own rule and should be
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.100|                      asked rather than asserted there. Second, the
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.101|                      comment above line 1808 in OPTY.bat still reads
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.102|                       HAGS is driver-assumed on RDNA3 since Adrenalin
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.103|                      23.12.1 and Anti-Lag 2 needs it  - that is the exact
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.104|                      claim the audit refuted and it should be replaced
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.105|                      with the DLSS Frame Generation wording. Separately,
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.106|                      I have not verified byte-for-byte that HwSchMode is
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.107|                      present on a fresh 25H2 install before any vendor
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.108|                      driver is installed, and machines do turn up with
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.109|                      HwSchMode=0, whose meaning I could not confirm; OPTY
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.110|                      should never write 0.
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.111|
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.112|  Cible           : call :regset
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.113|                    HKLM\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\GraphicsDrivers
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.114|                    HwSchMode REG_DWORD 2 - OPTY.bat line 1808, repair-
::X|FR|rad.hwschmode.115|                    and-defaults path
