::X|EN|reg.gamedvr.enabled.001|  What it is      : The per-user switch under HKCU\System\GameConfigStore.
::X|EN|reg.gamedvr.enabled.002|                    It is one of three separate Game DVR values and it is
::X|EN|reg.gamedvr.enabled.003|                    worth keeping them apart: GameDVR_Enabled decides
::X|EN|reg.gamedvr.enabled.004|                    whether Game Bar registers as a capture target at all,
::X|EN|reg.gamedvr.enabled.005|                    AppCaptureEnabled gates the capture feature in
::X|EN|reg.gamedvr.enabled.006|                    Settings, and HistoricalCaptureEnabled - the one
::X|EN|reg.gamedvr.enabled.007|                    people actually mean when they say 'it records in the
::X|EN|reg.gamedvr.enabled.008|                    background' - ships at 0.
::X|EN|reg.gamedvr.enabled.009|
::X|EN|reg.gamedvr.enabled.010|  Actual effect   : Writes 0 for the account running OPTY. Nothing
::X|EN|reg.gamedvr.enabled.011|                    machine-wide, no policy key, no other account
::X|EN|reg.gamedvr.enabled.012|                    affected.
::X|EN|reg.gamedvr.enabled.013|
::X|EN|reg.gamedvr.enabled.014|  Gain            : No measurable gain. Reported frame-rate differences
::X|EN|reg.gamedvr.enabled.015|                    cluster at 0-3%, which on any modern game is inside
::X|EN|reg.gamedvr.enabled.016|                    run-to-run variance, and the mechanism people cite for
::X|EN|reg.gamedvr.enabled.017|                    it - 'it stops recording in the background' - is
::X|EN|reg.gamedvr.enabled.018|                    simply wrong on a default machine, because background
::X|EN|reg.gamedvr.enabled.019|                    recording is off out of the box. The accurate
::X|EN|reg.gamedvr.enabled.020|                    description is: one fewer capture component arming
::X|EN|reg.gamedvr.enabled.021|                    itself at game start, and a certainty that Game Bar is
::X|EN|reg.gamedvr.enabled.022|                    not going to write video to your drive. Both are
::X|EN|reg.gamedvr.enabled.023|                    reasons someone might want it. Neither is FPS.
