:: ---- mouse.apply.live (diagnostic) ----------------------------------
::P|mouse.apply.live|RUN|SKIP|RUN|RUN|RUN|
::T|EN|mouse.apply.live.001|APPLY MOUSE SETTINGS WITHOUT SIGNING OUT
::T|EN|mouse.apply.live.002|Tells Windows to re-read the mouse settings right now instead of waiting for the next sign-in - no performance effect, it just lets you feel the change immediately instead of forgetting you made it.
::T|FR|mouse.apply.live.001|APPLIQUER LES REGLAGES DE SOURIS SANS FERMER LA SESSION
::T|FR|mouse.apply.live.002|Demande a Windows de relire les reglages de souris tout de suite, sans attendre la prochaine ouverture de session : aucun effet sur les performances, cela permet juste de sentir le changement immediatement au lieu de l oublier.
::X|EN|mouse.apply.live.001|  What it is      : A call to rundll32
::X|EN|mouse.apply.live.002|                    user32.dll,UpdatePerUserSystemParameters. It asks the
::X|EN|mouse.apply.live.003|                    current session to re-read the per-user system
::X|EN|mouse.apply.live.004|                    parameters out of the registry. It is an action rather
::X|EN|mouse.apply.live.005|                    than a report, but it writes and stores nothing.
::X|EN|mouse.apply.live.006|
::X|EN|mouse.apply.live.007|  Actual effect   : Without it, the four Mouse values sit in HKCU and
::X|EN|mouse.apply.live.008|                    change nothing until you sign out and back in. With
::X|EN|mouse.apply.live.009|                    it, the pointer changes under your hand while the
::X|EN|mouse.apply.live.010|                    script is still open.
::X|EN|mouse.apply.live.011|
::X|EN|mouse.apply.live.012|  Gain            : You judge the change now instead of tomorrow — the
::X|EN|mouse.apply.live.013|                    difference between a setting you can actually evaluate
::X|EN|mouse.apply.live.014|                    and one you forget you made. There is no performance
::X|EN|mouse.apply.live.015|                    dimension to this at all.
::X|EN|mouse.apply.live.016|
::X|EN|mouse.apply.live.017|  Cost            : Nothing that persists. Some shells briefly redraw the
::X|EN|mouse.apply.live.018|                    desktop — the wallpaper flicker people report is this
::X|EN|mouse.apply.live.019|                    call — and it is over in an instant.
::X|EN|mouse.apply.live.020|
::X|EN|mouse.apply.live.021|  Windows default : Not a setting. There is no shipped default because
::X|EN|mouse.apply.live.022|                    nothing on disk changes.
::X|EN|mouse.apply.live.023|
::X|EN|mouse.apply.live.024|  Possible values:
::X|EN|mouse.apply.live.025|    RUN                  : Executes the rundll32 call. The session re-
::X|EN|mouse.apply.live.026|                           reads the per-user system parameters from HKCU,
::X|EN|mouse.apply.live.027|                           so the mouse values written a moment earlier
::X|EN|mouse.apply.live.028|                           take effect at once. Nothing is written to disk
::X|EN|mouse.apply.live.029|                           and there is no state to undo.
::X|EN|mouse.apply.live.030|    SKIP                 : The registry values still change; they simply
::X|EN|mouse.apply.live.031|                           do not take effect until the next sign-out and
::X|EN|mouse.apply.live.032|                           sign-in. Nothing is lost, only delayed.
::X|EN|mouse.apply.live.033|
::X|EN|mouse.apply.live.034|  Why these profiles : Run it wherever mouse values were actually written,
::X|EN|mouse.apply.live.035|                       which is four profiles out of five — the table is
::X|EN|mouse.apply.live.036|                       near-uniform and there is no reason to pretend
::X|EN|mouse.apply.live.037|                       otherwise. 2 server is SKIP for exactly one reason:
::X|EN|mouse.apply.live.038|                       it wrote nothing, so there is nothing to apply. 5
::X|EN|mouse.apply.live.039|                       Windows still runs it, because 'the shipped
::X|EN|mouse.apply.live.040|                       default' has no meaning for an API call and the
::X|EN|mouse.apply.live.041|                       stock values it just wrote deserve to be live too.
::X|EN|mouse.apply.live.042|
::X|EN|mouse.apply.live.043|  Unverified      : This call is normally documented with arguments —
::X|EN|mouse.apply.live.044|                    rundll32.exe user32.dll,UpdatePerUserSystemParameters
::X|EN|mouse.apply.live.045|                    1, True. The argument-less form used here is the one
::X|EN|mouse.apply.live.046|                    that circulates widely, and the visible desktop redraw
::X|EN|mouse.apply.live.047|                    shows it does something, but I did not verify that it
::X|EN|mouse.apply.live.048|                    re-reads exactly the same set of parameters as the
::X|EN|mouse.apply.live.049|                    documented form. If a mouse change ever fails to
::X|EN|mouse.apply.live.050|                    appear live, this is the first thing to test.
::X|EN|mouse.apply.live.051|
::X|EN|mouse.apply.live.052|  Target          : rundll32.exe user32.dll,UpdatePerUserSystemParameters
::X|EN|mouse.apply.live.053|                    - the :mouseapply subroutine, called here when
::X|EN|mouse.apply.live.054|                    PROFVAL=RUN, and unconditionally from :gaming_restore
::X|EN|mouse.apply.live.055|                    ("Undo ALL profiles").
::X|FR|mouse.apply.live.001|  Ce que c est    : Un appel à rundll32
::X|FR|mouse.apply.live.002|                    user32.dll,UpdatePerUserSystemParameters. Il demande à
::X|FR|mouse.apply.live.003|                    la session courante de relire les paramètres système
::X|FR|mouse.apply.live.004|                    de l utilisateur depuis le registre. C est une action
::X|FR|mouse.apply.live.005|                    et non un rapport, mais elle n écrit et ne stocke
::X|FR|mouse.apply.live.006|                    rien.
::X|FR|mouse.apply.live.007|
::X|FR|mouse.apply.live.008|  Effet reel      : Sans lui, les quatre valeurs Mouse dorment dans HKCU
::X|FR|mouse.apply.live.009|                    et ne changent rien jusqu à la prochaine fermeture
::X|FR|mouse.apply.live.010|                    puis réouverture de session. Avec lui, le pointeur
::X|FR|mouse.apply.live.011|                    change sous votre main pendant que le script est
::X|FR|mouse.apply.live.012|                    encore ouvert.
::X|FR|mouse.apply.live.013|
::X|FR|mouse.apply.live.014|  Gain            : Vous jugez le changement maintenant plutôt que demain
::X|FR|mouse.apply.live.015|                    — la différence entre un réglage que vous pouvez
::X|FR|mouse.apply.live.016|                    réellement évaluer et un réglage que vous oublierez
::X|FR|mouse.apply.live.017|                    avoir fait. Il n y a ici aucune dimension de
::X|FR|mouse.apply.live.018|                    performance.
::X|FR|mouse.apply.live.019|
::X|FR|mouse.apply.live.020|  Cout            : Rien de persistant. Certains environnements
::X|FR|mouse.apply.live.021|                    redessinent brièvement le bureau — le clignotement de
::X|FR|mouse.apply.live.022|                    fond d écran que les gens rapportent, c est cet appel
::X|FR|mouse.apply.live.023|                    — et c est fini instantanément.
::X|FR|mouse.apply.live.024|
::X|FR|mouse.apply.live.025|  Defaut Windows  : Ce n est pas un réglage. Il n y a pas de valeur
::X|FR|mouse.apply.live.026|                    d usine puisque rien ne change sur le disque.
::X|FR|mouse.apply.live.027|
::X|FR|mouse.apply.live.028|  Valeurs possibles :
::X|FR|mouse.apply.live.029|    RUN                  : Exécute l appel rundll32. La session relit les
::X|FR|mouse.apply.live.030|                           paramètres système de l utilisateur depuis HKCU
::X|FR|mouse.apply.live.031|                           : les valeurs de souris écrites à l instant
::X|FR|mouse.apply.live.032|                           prennent effet immédiatement. Rien n est écrit
::X|FR|mouse.apply.live.033|                           sur le disque et il n y a aucun état à annuler.
::X|FR|mouse.apply.live.034|    SKIP                 : Les valeurs du registre changent quand même :
::X|FR|mouse.apply.live.035|                           elles ne prennent simplement effet qu à la
::X|FR|mouse.apply.live.036|                           prochaine fermeture puis réouverture de
::X|FR|mouse.apply.live.037|                           session. Rien n est perdu, seulement différé.
::X|FR|mouse.apply.live.038|
::X|FR|mouse.apply.live.039|  Pourquoi ces profils : À exécuter partout où des valeurs de souris ont
::X|FR|mouse.apply.live.040|                         réellement été écrites, soit quatre profils sur
::X|FR|mouse.apply.live.041|                         cinq — le tableau est presque uniforme et il n y
::X|FR|mouse.apply.live.042|                         a pas lieu de faire semblant du contraire. Le 2
::X|FR|mouse.apply.live.043|                         serveur est SKIP pour une seule raison : il n a
::X|FR|mouse.apply.live.044|                         rien écrit, il n y a donc rien à appliquer. Le 5
::X|FR|mouse.apply.live.045|                         Windows l exécute quand même, car « la valeur
::X|FR|mouse.apply.live.046|                         d usine » n a aucun sens pour un appel d API, et
::X|FR|mouse.apply.live.047|                         les valeurs d origine qu il vient d écrire
::X|FR|mouse.apply.live.048|                         méritent elles aussi d être actives tout de
::X|FR|mouse.apply.live.049|                         suite.
::X|FR|mouse.apply.live.050|
::X|FR|mouse.apply.live.051|  Non verifie (en)  : This call is normally documented with arguments —
::X|FR|mouse.apply.live.052|                      rundll32.exe
::X|FR|mouse.apply.live.053|                      user32.dll,UpdatePerUserSystemParameters 1, True.
::X|FR|mouse.apply.live.054|                      The argument-less form used here is the one that
::X|FR|mouse.apply.live.055|                      circulates widely, and the visible desktop redraw
::X|FR|mouse.apply.live.056|                      shows it does something, but I did not verify that
::X|FR|mouse.apply.live.057|                      it re-reads exactly the same set of parameters as
::X|FR|mouse.apply.live.058|                      the documented form. If a mouse change ever fails to
::X|FR|mouse.apply.live.059|                      appear live, this is the first thing to test.
::X|FR|mouse.apply.live.060|
::X|FR|mouse.apply.live.061|  Cible           : rundll32.exe user32.dll,UpdatePerUserSystemParameters
::X|FR|mouse.apply.live.062|                    - the :mouseapply subroutine, called here when
::X|FR|mouse.apply.live.063|                    PROFVAL=RUN, and unconditionally from :gaming_restore
::X|FR|mouse.apply.live.064|                    ("Undo ALL profiles").
