:: ---- rad.bcd.residue (risky) -----------------------------------
::P|rad.bcd.residue|DELETE|DELETE|DELETE|DELETE|DELETE|
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.001|REMOVE BOOT CONFIGURATION LEFTOVERS
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.002|Removes ten boot-loader settings that tuning guides and msconfig leave behind - several are real damage in disguise, like a boot entry stuck on 4 of your 16 CPU threads or a forced clock source that makes timing worse, not better.
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.001|RETIRER LES RESIDUS DE CONFIGURATION DE DEMARRAGE
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.002|Retire dix reglages de demarrage laisses par des guides d optimisation ou par msconfig : plusieurs sont de vrais degats deguises en ameliorations, comme une entree de demarrage bloquee sur 4 de vos 16 threads CPU, ou une source d horloge forcee qui degrade la latence au lieu de l ameliorer.
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.001|  What it is      : Ten boot-configuration elements on the current boot
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.002|                    entry that no Windows installer ever writes:
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.003|                    useplatformclock, useplatformtick, disabledynamictick,
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.004|                    tscsyncpolicy, numproc, onecpu, maxproc, groupsize,
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.005|                    truncatememory and removememory. They come from tuning
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.006|                    guides, from msconfig's Boot > Advanced options
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.007|                    dialog, or from a hardware-debugging session somebody
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.008|                    never undid.
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.009|
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.010|  Actual effect   : For each element that is actually present, runs
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.011|                    bcdedit /deletevalue {current} <element>. If the OS
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.012|                    volume is BitLocker-protected - read from HKLM\SYSTEM\
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.013|                    CurrentControlSet\Control\BitLockerStatus\BootStatus,
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.014|                    which is the one locale-proof signal here - it prints
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.015|                    the element and the exact command instead and changes
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.016|                    nothing. Reboot required. usefirmwarepcisettings and
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.017|                    increaseuserva are deliberately left alone: the first
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.018|                    can move PCI resource assignment, the second is a
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.019|                    legitimate 32-bit element and not wreckage.
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.020|
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.021|  Gain            : Two of the ten do real damage and justify the reboot
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.022|                    by themselves. useplatformclock forces the HPET as the
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.023|                    system performance counter, so every timing call
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.024|                    becomes a bus read instead of a register read and
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.025|                    measured DPC latency and frame pacing get worse rather
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.026|                    than better - it is sold as a latency fix and it is a
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.027|                    latency cost. numproc, onecpu and groupsize leave the
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.028|                    kernel running on fewer logical processors than the
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.029|                    CPU has, the classic msconfig leftover where a
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.030|                    sixteen-thread CPU boots on four. truncatememory and
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.031|                    removememory make installed RAM vanish into hardware-
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.032|                    reserved. If none of the ten are present - the common
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.033|                    case on a machine that was never tweaked - this card
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.034|                    does nothing at all, and that is a perfectly good
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.035|                    outcome.
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.036|
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.037|  Cost            : A reboot, and only for the elements that were actually
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.038|                    there. If you set one deliberately - onecpu or numproc
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.039|                    for driver debugging, truncatememory to reproduce a
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.040|                    low-memory condition - you lose it and have to set it
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.041|                    again. Nothing in a normal Windows configuration
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.042|                    requires any of the ten.
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.043|
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.044|  Windows default : All ten absent from {current}. Windows Setup writes
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.045|                    none of them, on any edition.
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.046|
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.047|  Possible values:
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.048|    DELETE               : Remove every one of the ten that is present
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.049|                           from the {current} boot entry, then reboot.
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.050|                           This is what all five profiles do. Elements
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.051|                           that are not present are skipped silently, so
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.052|                           on a machine that was never tweaked this whole
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.053|                           card is a no-op.
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.054|    SKIP                 : Report only, change nothing. This is what the
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.055|                           script forces on its own when BitLocker
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.056|                           protects the OS volume: it prints each element
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.057|                           it found and the exact bcdedit command to run
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.058|                           after suspending BitLocker.
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.059|    useplatformclock yes : Forces the HPET as the system performance
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.060|                           counter source instead of the invariant TSC.
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.061|                           Every QueryPerformanceCounter call becomes an
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.062|                           MMIO read across the bus - hundreds of
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.063|                           nanoseconds - instead of an RDTSC costing a
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.064|                           few. Timing-heavy code, which includes every
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.065|                           game engine and every audio stack, pays that on
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.066|                           each call, and measured DPC latency goes up,
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.067|                           not down. There is no correct value: the
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.068|                           element should not exist.
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.069|    useplatformtick yes  : Same family: forces the platform timer to
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.070|                           generate the periodic tick instead of the per-
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.071|                           core local APIC timer. Every tick becomes a bus
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.072|                           transaction, and the ticks are no longer core-
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.073|                           local. Same verdict, remove it.
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.074|    disabledynamictick yes :
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.075|        Turns off the tickless kernel: the timer interrupt keeps firing at
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.076|        a fixed rate even when the machine has nothing to do, which
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.077|        prevents deep core and package idle states. That means a warmer,
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.078|        noisier, thirstier idle. On a laptop it is straightforwardly
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.079|        battery you are burning. The timing consistency it is supposed to
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.080|        buy has never shown up in a careful measurement.
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.081|    tscsyncpolicy Default / Legacy / Enhanced :
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.082|        Tells the kernel how to synchronise the TSC across cores at boot.
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.083|        Forcing a policy is guide folklore; on a multi-socket machine or a
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.084|        hybrid P-core/E-core CPU, the wrong policy is a way to get time-
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.085|        source oddities you will never diagnose. Absent lets the kernel
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.086|        pick from what the CPU reports.
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.087|    numproc N            : Caps the number of logical processors the
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.088|                           kernel starts at N. This is what msconfig's
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.089|                           Boot > Advanced options > Number of processors
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.090|                           box writes, and people leave it behind
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.091|                           constantly. Symptom: Task Manager shows fewer
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.092|                           logical processors than the CPU has, and
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.093|                           everything is slower for a reason nothing on
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.094|                           screen explains.
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.095|    onecpu yes           : Boots on a single logical processor. A kernel-
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.096|                           debugging element, catastrophic as a leftover.
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.097|    maxproc yes          : Makes the kernel build its structures for the
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.098|                           maximum number of processors the platform could
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.099|                           ever have, for hot-add support. It does not cap
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.100|                           anything and is mostly harmless - a small
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.101|                           amount of wasted non-paged pool. It is on the
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.102|                           list because it is wreckage, not because it
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.103|                           hurts.
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.104|    groupsize N          : Forces the size of processor groups (a power of
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.105|                           two, up to 64). Set to 2 or 4, the machine gets
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.106|                           carved into many tiny groups, and since a
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.107|                           normal application runs inside a single group
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.108|                           it now sees two or four logical processors.
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.109|                           Same visible symptom as numproc, harder to
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.110|                           spot.
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.111|    truncatememory <address in bytes> :
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.112|        Tells the OS to ignore all physical memory above that address.
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.113|        This is msconfig's Maximum memory box. Symptom: System shows
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.114|        "Installed 32.0 GB (16.0 GB usable)" and people go buy RAM.
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.115|    removememory <bytes> : Removes that many bytes from the top of usable
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.116|                           memory. Same family, same symptom, same answer:
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.117|                           it should not be there.
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.118|
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.119|  Why these profiles : All five delete, profile 5 included, because absent
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.120|                       is the shipped state for every single one of these.
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.121|                       This is the clearest case in the set where the
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.122|                       right answer does not depend on what the machine is
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.123|                       for: a boot entry that starts on four of your
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.124|                       sixteen threads is wrong for a gaming rig, a server
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.125|                       and a laptop equally, and there is no role that
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.126|                       benefits from the HPET being forced as the system
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.127|                       clock. The laptop has one extra reason on top:
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.128|                       disabledynamictick keeps the timer interrupt firing
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.129|                       at a fixed rate while the machine idles, which
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.130|                       blocks the deep package idle states and burns
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.131|                       battery for a timing benefit nobody has ever
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.132|                       measured in a game.
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.133|
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.134|  Known problems  : Concrete symptoms these elements cause - not symptoms
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.135|                    of removing them, which has no known breakage. Task
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.136|                    Manager showing fewer logical processors than the CPU
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.137|                    has (numproc, onecpu, groupsize). System reporting
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.138|                    "Installed 32.0 GB (16.0 GB usable)" (truncatememory,
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.139|                    removememory). LatencyMon reporting high ISR/DPC times
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.140|                    with no driver obviously at fault (useplatformclock,
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.141|                    useplatformtick). A laptop that idles hot and drains
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.142|                    overnight with nothing running (disabledynamictick).
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.143|                    The one operational hazard is BitLocker: edit the boot
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.144|                    configuration on a protected volume and you risk a
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.145|                    recovery-key prompt at the next boot, which is why the
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.146|                    script refuses to write in that case.
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.147|
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.148|  Unverified      : The BitLocker guard is deliberately conservative
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.149|                    rather than precise. BitLocker's default TPM-only
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.150|                    protector seals against a documented set of measured
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.151|                    boot settings; I cannot confirm that these ten
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.152|                    specific elements are inside that set, so I cannot
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.153|                    promise deleting one triggers a recovery prompt, nor
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.154|                    that it does not. Reporting instead of writing
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.155|                    whenever BitLocker is on is the right call under that
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.156|                    uncertainty. Suspending BitLocker for one reboot is
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.157|                    the safe way to apply them.
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.158|
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.159|  Target          : bcdedit /deletevalue "{current}" <element> for each
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.160|                    of: useplatformclock useplatformtick
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.161|                    disabledynamictick tscsyncpolicy numproc onecpu
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.162|                    maxproc groupsize truncatememory removememory. Loop at
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.163|                    OPTY.bat line 1986, helper :bcdresidue at lines
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.164|                    1994-2011. Presence is tested with bcdedit /enum
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.165|                    "{current}" / findstr /i /b. BitLocker guard reads
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.166|                    HKLM\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\BitLockerStatus
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.167|                    /v BootStatus (line 1980); non-zero means report only.
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.168|                    Explicitly NOT touched: usefirmwarepcisettings and
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.169|                    increaseuserva.
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.001|  Ce que c est    : Dix elements de configuration de demarrage poses sur
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.002|                    l entree courante et qu aucune installation de Windows
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.003|                    n ecrit jamais : useplatformclock, useplatformtick,
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.004|                    disabledynamictick, tscsyncpolicy, numproc, onecpu,
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.005|                    maxproc, groupsize, truncatememory et removememory.
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.006|                    Ils viennent des guides d optimisation, de la fenetre
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.007|                    msconfig > Demarrer > Options avancees, ou d une
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.008|                    session de diagnostic materiel que personne n a
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.009|                    defaite.
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.010|
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.011|  Effet reel      : Pour chaque element reellement present, lance bcdedit
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.012|                    /deletevalue {current} <element>. Si le volume systeme
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.013|                    est protege par BitLocker - detecte via HKLM\SYSTEM\Cu
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.014|                    rrentControlSet\Control\BitLockerStatus\BootStatus, le
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.015|                    seul signal insensible a la langue ici - il affiche
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.016|                    l element et la commande exacte, et ne change rien.
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.017|                    Redemarrage requis. usefirmwarepcisettings et
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.018|                    increaseuserva sont volontairement laisses tranquilles
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.019|                    : le premier peut deplacer l attribution des
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.020|                    ressources PCI, le second est un element 32 bits
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.021|                    legitime, pas un residu.
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.022|
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.023|  Gain            : Deux des dix font des degats reels et justifient le
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.024|                    redemarrage a eux seuls. useplatformclock impose le
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.025|                    HPET comme compteur de performance systeme : chaque
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.026|                    appel de temps devient une lecture sur le bus au lieu
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.027|                    d une lecture de registre, et la latence DPC mesuree
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.028|                    comme la regularite d affichage empirent au lieu de
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.029|                    s ameliorer - on le vend comme un remede a la latence,
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.030|                    c est un cout de latence. numproc, onecpu et groupsize
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.031|                    laissent le noyau tourner sur moins de processeurs
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.032|                    logiques que le CPU n en a : le classique residu
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.033|                    msconfig ou un CPU a seize threads demarre sur quatre.
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.034|                    truncatememory et removememory font disparaitre de la
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.035|                    RAM installee en « reserve materielle ». Si aucun des
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.036|                    dix n est present - le cas courant sur une machine
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.037|                    jamais bidouillee - cette carte ne fait rien du tout,
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.038|                    et c est un tres bon resultat.
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.039|
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.040|  Cout            : Un redemarrage, et seulement pour les elements qui
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.041|                    etaient reellement la. Si vous en aviez pose un exprès
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.042|                    - onecpu ou numproc pour deboguer un pilote,
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.043|                    truncatememory pour reproduire une machine a faible
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.044|                    memoire - il disparait et il faudra le remettre.
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.045|                    Aucune configuration Windows normale n a besoin d un
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.046|                    seul de ces dix elements.
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.047|
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.048|  Defaut Windows  : Les dix absents de {current}. Le programme
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.049|                    d installation de Windows n en ecrit aucun, sur aucune
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.050|                    edition.
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.051|
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.052|  Valeurs possibles :
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.053|    DELETE               : Retirer de l entree de demarrage {current}
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.054|                           chacun des dix elements presents, puis
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.055|                           redemarrer. C est ce que font les cinq profils.
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.056|                           Les elements absents sont ignores en silence :
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.057|                           sur une machine jamais bidouillee, cette carte
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.058|                           ne fait strictement rien.
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.059|    SKIP                 : Signaler seulement, ne rien changer. C est ce
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.060|                           que le script impose de lui-meme quand
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.061|                           BitLocker protege le volume systeme : il
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.062|                           affiche chaque element trouve et la commande
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.063|                           bcdedit exacte a lancer apres avoir suspendu
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.064|                           BitLocker.
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.065|    useplatformclock yes : Impose le HPET comme source du compteur de
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.066|                           performance systeme a la place du TSC
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.067|                           invariant. Chaque appel a
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.068|                           QueryPerformanceCounter devient une lecture
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.069|                           MMIO sur le bus - des centaines de nanosecondes
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.070|                           - au lieu d un RDTSC qui en coute quelques-
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.071|                           unes. Le code sensible au temps, ce qui inclut
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.072|                           tous les moteurs de jeu et toutes les piles
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.073|                           audio, paie ca a chaque appel, et la latence
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.074|                           DPC mesuree monte au lieu de descendre. Il n y
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.075|                           a pas de bonne valeur : cet element ne devrait
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.076|                           pas exister.
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.077|    useplatformtick yes  : Meme famille : force le timer de plateforme a
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.078|                           generer le tick periodique a la place du timer
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.079|                           APIC local de chaque coeur. Chaque tick devient
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.080|                           une transaction sur le bus, et les ticks ne
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.081|                           sont plus locaux au coeur. Meme verdict, on
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.082|                           l enleve.
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.083|    disabledynamictick yes :
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.084|        Desactive le noyau sans tick : l interruption d horloge continue
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.085|        de tomber a cadence fixe meme quand la machine n a rien a faire,
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.086|        ce qui empeche les etats de repos profonds des coeurs et du
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.087|        package. Resultat : un repos plus chaud, plus bruyant, plus
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.088|        gourmand. Sur un portable, c est de la batterie que vous brulez,
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.089|        tout simplement. La regularite de timing censee compenser n est
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.090|        jamais apparue dans une mesure serieuse.
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.091|    tscsyncpolicy Default / Legacy / Enhanced :
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.092|        Indique au noyau comment synchroniser le TSC entre les coeurs au
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.093|        demarrage. Forcer une politique releve du folklore des guides ;
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.094|        sur une machine multi-socket ou un CPU hybride coeurs P/coeurs E,
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.095|        la mauvaise politique est un bon moyen d obtenir des bizarreries
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.096|        de source de temps que vous ne diagnostiquerez jamais. Absent, le
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.097|        noyau choisit d apres ce que le CPU declare.
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.098|    numproc N            : Limite a N le nombre de processeurs logiques
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.099|                           que le noyau demarre. C est ce qu ecrit la case
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.100|                           Nombre de processeurs dans msconfig, Demarrer >
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.101|                           Options avancees, et les gens l oublient en
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.102|                           permanence. Symptome : le Gestionnaire des
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.103|                           taches affiche moins de processeurs logiques
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.104|                           que le CPU n en a, et tout est plus lent sans
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.105|                           qu aucun ecran ne l explique.
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.106|    onecpu yes           : Demarre sur un seul processeur logique. Un
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.107|                           element de debogage noyau, catastrophique quand
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.108|                           il traine.
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.109|    maxproc yes          : Fait construire au noyau ses structures pour le
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.110|                           nombre maximal de processeurs que la plateforme
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.111|                           pourrait accueillir, en vue d un ajout a chaud.
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.112|                           Ne limite rien et reste globalement inoffensif
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.113|                           : un peu de pool non pagine gaspille. Il est
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.114|                           dans la liste parce que c est un residu, pas
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.115|                           parce qu il fait mal.
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.116|    groupsize N          : Force la taille des groupes de processeurs (une
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.117|                           puissance de deux, jusqu a 64). Regle a 2 ou 4,
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.118|                           la machine est decoupee en une multitude de
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.119|                           petits groupes, et comme une application
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.120|                           normale s execute dans un seul groupe, elle ne
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.121|                           voit plus que deux ou quatre processeurs
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.122|                           logiques. Meme symptome visible que numproc,
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.123|                           mais bien plus difficile a reperer.
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.124|    truncatememory <address in bytes> :
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.125|        Demande au systeme d ignorer toute la memoire physique au-dessus
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.126|        de cette adresse. C est la case Memoire maximale de msconfig.
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.127|        Symptome : la page Systeme affiche « 32,0 Go installes (16,0 Go
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.128|        utilisable) » et les gens vont racheter de la RAM.
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.129|    removememory <bytes> : Retire ce nombre d octets du haut de la memoire
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.130|                           utilisable. Meme famille, meme symptome, meme
