::P|net.tcp.defaults.netdns|APPLY|APPLY|APPLY|APPLY|APPLY|
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.001|RESTORE STANDARD TCP NETWORK SETTINGS
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.002|Rewrites three machine-wide TCP settings to their Windows defaults - no gain on a clean machine, but it undoes a common gaming-guide tweak that pins the receive window at 64 KB and can crush download speed on fast or long connections.
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.001|RETABLIR LES REGLAGES TCP RESEAU STANDARD
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.002|Reecrit trois reglages TCP valables pour toute la machine a leurs valeurs Windows d origine : aucun gain sur une machine propre, mais cela annule un tweak courant des guides gaming qui bloque la fenetre de reception a 64 Ko et peut effondrer le debit sur les connexions rapides ou longues.
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.001|  What it is      : Three machine-wide TCP/IP settings: receive-window
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.002|                    autotuning (how large a window Windows will
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.003|                    negotiate), Window Scaling Heuristics (whether Windows
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.004|                    second-guesses that autotuning per path), and Receive
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.005|                    Side Scaling at the TCP layer, which spreads receive
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.006|                    processing across CPU cores.
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.007|
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.008|  Actual effect   : OPTY writes autotuninglevel=normal,
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.009|                    heuristics=disabled and rss=enabled unconditionally,
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.010|                    without reading the current values first. Machine-
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.011|                    wide, immediate, no reboot.
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.012|
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.013|  Gain            : On an untouched Windows 11 machine, none. All three
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.014|                    are already at these values - verified live here, and
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.015|                    Window Scaling Heuristics has shipped disabled since
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.016|                    Windows 8.1. The step exists to undo damage, not to
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.017|                    improve anything: gaming optimizers and forum guides
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.018|                    routinely write autotuninglevel=disabled, which pins
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.019|                    the receive window at 64 KB and destroys throughput on
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.020|                    any long or fast path. This puts it back.
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.021|
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.022|  Cost            : Nothing on a stock machine. If you had deliberately
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.023|                    tuned TCP for an unusual link - satellite, high-
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.024|                    latency WAN, a lab setup - your setting is overwritten
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.025|                    silently, with no record of what it was.
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.026|
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.027|  Windows default : autotuninglevel=normal, rss=enabled and Window Scaling
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.028|                    Heuristics disabled are all Windows defaults. netsh
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.029|                    int tcp set heuristics default hands the decision back
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.030|                    to Windows and lands on the same behaviour.
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.031|
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.032|  Possible values:
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.033|    autotuninglevel=normal :
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.034|        Windows sizes the TCP receive window automatically, scaling it up
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.035|        to the bandwidth-delay product of the path. Shipped value.
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.036|    autotuninglevel=disabled :
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.037|        The receive window is pinned at 64 KB and window scaling is never
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.038|        negotiated. On a 100 ms path that caps a single TCP stream at
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.039|        roughly 5 Mbit/s. This is the value optimizer guides write.
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.040|    autotuninglevel=highlyrestricted :
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.041|        The window may grow only slightly beyond the 64 KB default.
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.042|    autotuninglevel=restricted :
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.043|        The window grows moderately beyond the default, still well below
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.044|        what a long fast path needs.
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.045|    autotuninglevel=experimental :
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.046|        The window may grow to extreme values, up to a 1 GB scale factor.
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.047|        It wastes non-paged pool and no home path needs it.
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.048|    heuristics=disabled  : Windows stops applying its stored per-path
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.049|                           Window Scaling Heuristics and honours the
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.050|                           autotuning level you set.
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.051|    heuristics=enabled   : Windows may silently reduce the window scale
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.052|                           factor on paths it judges problematic,
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.053|                           overriding your autotuning level without
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.054|                           telling you.
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.055|    heuristics=default   : Stops asserting a value and hands the decision
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.056|                           to the Windows built-in policy, which has been
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.057|                           disabled since Windows 8.1 - so the observable
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.058|                           behaviour matches heuristics=disabled.
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.059|    rss=enabled          : Received-packet processing is spread across
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.060|                           several CPU cores at the TCP layer. Shipped
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.061|                           value.
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.062|    rss=disabled         : All receive processing lands on a single core,
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.063|                           which saturates before the link does on a fast
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.064|                           connection.
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.065|    rss=default          : Stops asserting a value and hands the decision
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.066|                           to Windows, whose policy is enabled.
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.067|
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.068|  Why these profiles : Five identical columns, because there is nothing
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.069|                       here to vary. These three values ARE the shipped
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.070|                       defaults, so gaming, server, office and laptop all
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.071|                       want them, and the Windows column wants them too -
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.072|                       writing them is exactly how a mangled machine gets
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.073|                       back to shipped. The only owner who should decline
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.074|                       is one who knowingly set a non-default autotuning
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.075|                       level for a specific link.
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.076|
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.077|  Unverified      : That Window Scaling Heuristics ships disabled rests on
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.078|                    documented Windows 8.1-and-later behaviour plus one
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.079|                    live Windows 11 25H2 reading. Microsoft does not
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.080|                    restate it per release, so it is not sourced from a
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.081|                    25H2 document.
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.082|
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.083|  Target          : netsh int tcp set global autotuninglevel=normal ;
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.084|                    netsh int tcp set heuristics disabled ; netsh int tcp
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.085|                    set global rss=enabled - the three lines at
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.086|                    :netdns_tcp (OPTY.bat ~590), run unconditionally
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.087|                    during the maintenance pass right after ipconfig
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.088|                    /flushdns
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.001|  Ce que c est    : Trois reglages TCP valables pour toute la machine :
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.002|                    l ajustement automatique de la fenetre de reception
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.003|                    (jusqu ou Windows accepte de la faire grandir), les
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.004|                    heuristiques de mise a l echelle de fenetre (qui
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.005|                    laissent Windows revenir sur cet ajustement chemin par
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.006|                    chemin), et le RSS au niveau TCP, qui repartit le
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.007|                    traitement en reception sur plusieurs coeurs.
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.008|
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.009|  Effet reel      : OPTY ecrit autotuninglevel=normal, heuristics=disabled
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.010|                    et rss=enabled sans condition, sans lire d abord les
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.011|                    valeurs en place. Effet immediat sur toute la machine,
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.012|                    sans redemarrage.
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.013|
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.014|  Gain            : Sur une machine Windows 11 non trafiquee, aucun. Les
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.015|                    trois sont deja a ces valeurs - verifie en direct ici,
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.016|                    et les heuristiques de mise a l echelle sont livrees
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.017|                    desactivees depuis Windows 8.1. L etape ne sert pas a
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.018|                    ameliorer mais a reparer : les optimiseurs de jeu et
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.019|                    les tutos de forum ecrivent regulierement
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.020|                    autotuninglevel=disabled, ce qui bloque la fenetre de
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.021|                    reception a 64 Ko et effondre le debit sur tout chemin
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.022|                    long ou rapide. Ceci le remet en place.
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.023|
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.024|  Cout            : Rien sur une machine d origine. Si vous aviez
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.025|                    volontairement regle TCP pour un lien inhabituel -
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.026|                    satellite, WAN a forte latence, banc de test - votre
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.027|                    reglage est ecrase sans avertissement et sans trace de
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.028|                    ce qu il valait.
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.029|
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.030|  Defaut Windows  : autotuninglevel=normal, rss=enabled et les
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.031|                    heuristiques de mise a l echelle desactivees sont
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.032|                    toutes des valeurs Windows d origine. netsh int tcp
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.033|                    set heuristics default rend la main a Windows et
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.034|                    aboutit au meme comportement.
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.035|
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.036|  Valeurs possibles :
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.037|    autotuninglevel=normal :
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.038|        Windows dimensionne automatiquement la fenetre de reception TCP et
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.039|        la fait grandir jusqu au produit debit x latence du chemin. Valeur
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.040|        d origine.
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.041|    autotuninglevel=disabled :
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.042|        La fenetre de reception est bloquee a 64 Ko et la mise a l echelle
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.043|        n est jamais negociee. Sur un chemin a 100 ms, un seul flux TCP
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.044|        plafonne vers 5 Mbit/s. C est la valeur qu ecrivent les guides
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.045|        d optimisation.
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.046|    autotuninglevel=highlyrestricted :
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.047|        La fenetre ne depasse que tres legerement les 64 Ko par defaut.
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.048|    autotuninglevel=restricted :
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.049|        La fenetre grandit moderement au-dela du defaut, mais reste loin
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.050|        de ce qu exige un chemin long et rapide.
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.051|    autotuninglevel=experimental :
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.052|        La fenetre peut atteindre des valeurs extremes, jusqu a un facteur
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.053|        d echelle de 1 Go. Cela gaspille du pool non pagine et aucun usage
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.054|        domestique n en a besoin.
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.055|    heuristics=disabled  : Windows cesse d appliquer ses heuristiques de
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.056|                           mise a l echelle memorisees par chemin et
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.057|                           respecte le niveau d autotuning que vous avez
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.058|                           fixe.
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.059|    heuristics=enabled   : Windows peut reduire en silence le facteur
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.060|                           d echelle sur les chemins qu il juge
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.061|                           problematiques, passant outre votre niveau
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.062|                           d autotuning sans rien dire.
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.063|    heuristics=default   : Cesse d imposer une valeur et rend la decision
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.064|                           a la politique interne de Windows, desactivee
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.065|                           depuis Windows 8.1 : le comportement observable
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.066|                           est donc le meme que heuristics=disabled.
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.067|    rss=enabled          : Le traitement des paquets recus est reparti sur
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.068|                           plusieurs coeurs au niveau TCP. Valeur
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.069|                           d origine.
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.070|    rss=disabled         : Tout le traitement en reception tombe sur un
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.071|                           seul coeur, qui sature avant le lien sur une
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.072|                           connexion rapide.
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.073|    rss=default          : Cesse d imposer une valeur et rend la decision
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.074|                           a Windows, dont la politique est enabled.
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.075|
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.076|  Pourquoi ces profils : Cinq colonnes identiques, parce qu il n y a rien
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.077|                         a faire varier. Ces trois valeurs SONT les
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.078|                         valeurs d usine : gaming, serveur, bureautique et
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.079|                         portable les veulent toutes, et la colonne
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.080|                         Windows aussi, puisque les ecrire est precisement
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.081|                         la maniere de ramener une machine trafiquee a
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.082|                         l etat livre. Le seul refus legitime vient de
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.083|                         quelqu un qui a choisi sciemment un autre niveau
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.084|                         d autotuning pour un lien precis.
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.085|
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.086|  Non verifie (en)  : That Window Scaling Heuristics ships disabled rests
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.087|                      on documented Windows 8.1-and-later behaviour plus
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.088|                      one live Windows 11 25H2 reading. Microsoft does not
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.089|                      restate it per release, so it is not sourced from a
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.090|                      25H2 document.
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.091|
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.092|  Cible           : netsh int tcp set global autotuninglevel=normal ;
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.093|                    netsh int tcp set heuristics disabled ; netsh int tcp
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.094|                    set global rss=enabled - the three lines at
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.095|                    :netdns_tcp (OPTY.bat ~590), run unconditionally
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.096|                    during the maintenance pass right after ipconfig
