:: ---- net.reset.ip.stack (risky) --------------------------------
::P|net.reset.ip.stack|SKIP|SKIP|SKIP|SKIP|SKIP|
::T|EN|net.reset.ip.stack.001|RESET THE TCP/IP STACK (DESTRUCTIVE REPAIR)
::T|EN|net.reset.ip.stack.002|Wipes every network adapter back to factory DHCP settings to fix deep connection problems nothing else can reach - but it also erases any static IP, custom DNS or VPN route you had set up, with no way to undo it.
::T|FR|net.reset.ip.stack.001|REINITIALISER LA PILE TCP/IP (REPARATION DESTRUCTIVE)
::T|FR|net.reset.ip.stack.002|Remet chaque carte reseau en DHCP d usine pour reparer des pannes profondes que rien d autre ne corrige - mais efface aussi toute IP fixe, tout DNS personnalise ou route VPN que vous aviez configures, sans possibilite de retour en arriere.
::X|EN|net.reset.ip.stack.001|  What it is      : Rewrites the entire TCP/IP stack configuration in the
::X|EN|net.reset.ip.stack.002|                    registry back to factory state. Repair menu only,
::X|EN|net.reset.ip.stack.003|                    behind a typed RESET confirmation.
::X|EN|net.reset.ip.stack.004|
::X|EN|net.reset.ip.stack.005|  Actual effect   : Every per-interface IP configuration is wiped: static
::X|EN|net.reset.ip.stack.006|                    IP addresses, static DNS servers, persistent routes,
::X|EN|net.reset.ip.stack.007|                    custom interface metrics. All adapters go back to
::X|EN|net.reset.ip.stack.008|                    DHCP. A reboot is required. OPTY re-asserts the three
::X|EN|net.reset.ip.stack.009|                    TCP globals immediately afterwards, because the reset
::X|EN|net.reset.ip.stack.010|                    reverts those too.
::X|EN|net.reset.ip.stack.011|
::X|EN|net.reset.ip.stack.012|  Gain            : Fixes stack-level corruption nothing else reaches -
::X|EN|net.reset.ip.stack.013|                    adapters that will not take an address, an interface
::X|EN|net.reset.ip.stack.014|                    still broken after a driver reinstall, a routing table
::X|EN|net.reset.ip.stack.015|                    that is wrong for no visible reason. When that is the
::X|EN|net.reset.ip.stack.016|                    fault, this is what fixes it.
::X|EN|net.reset.ip.stack.017|
::X|EN|net.reset.ip.stack.018|  Cost            : OPTY cannot undo this. On a plain DHCP machine you
::X|EN|net.reset.ip.stack.019|                    will not notice. If you point at Pi-hole or NextDNS,
::X|EN|net.reset.ip.stack.020|                    run a static IP, keep a persistent route to a VPN
::X|EN|net.reset.ip.stack.021|                    subnet or a NAS, or your DNS was pushed by corporate
::X|EN|net.reset.ip.stack.022|                    configuration, all of it is wiped and you re-enter it
::X|EN|net.reset.ip.stack.023|                    by hand. Save the output of ipconfig /all and route
::X|EN|net.reset.ip.stack.024|                    print before you say yes, and check that a restore
::X|EN|net.reset.ip.stack.025|                    point exists.
::X|EN|net.reset.ip.stack.026|
::X|EN|net.reset.ip.stack.027|  Windows default : Not applicable - this restores the factory stack
::X|EN|net.reset.ip.stack.028|                    configuration by definition.
::X|EN|net.reset.ip.stack.029|
::X|EN|net.reset.ip.stack.030|  Possible values:
::X|EN|net.reset.ip.stack.031|    RESET                : The whole per-interface TCP/IP configuration in
::X|EN|net.reset.ip.stack.032|                           the registry is rewritten to factory. Static IP
::X|EN|net.reset.ip.stack.033|                           addresses, static DNS servers, persistent
::X|EN|net.reset.ip.stack.034|                           routes and custom interface metrics are gone,
::X|EN|net.reset.ip.stack.035|                           every adapter returns to DHCP, and a reboot is
::X|EN|net.reset.ip.stack.036|                           required before the machine is usable as
::X|EN|net.reset.ip.stack.037|                           configured.
::X|EN|net.reset.ip.stack.038|    SKIP                 : Nothing is touched. This is what typing
::X|EN|net.reset.ip.stack.039|                           anything other than RESET does.
::X|EN|net.reset.ip.stack.040|
::X|EN|net.reset.ip.stack.041|  Why these profiles : Five SKIP columns, deliberately. No usage profile
::X|EN|net.reset.ip.stack.042|                       is a reason to reset a TCP/IP stack; a reproducible
::X|EN|net.reset.ip.stack.043|                       fault is, and nothing else. The server and laptop
::X|EN|net.reset.ip.stack.044|                       columns are the ones with most to lose, since those
::X|EN|net.reset.ip.stack.045|                       are the machines most likely to carry a static
::X|EN|net.reset.ip.stack.046|                       address, a pinned resolver or a persistent route -
::X|EN|net.reset.ip.stack.047|                       but even the Windows column is SKIP, because
::X|EN|net.reset.ip.stack.048|                       Windows does not do this to itself either.
::X|EN|net.reset.ip.stack.049|
::X|EN|net.reset.ip.stack.050|  Known problems  : The deck carried two copies of this card with
::X|EN|net.reset.ip.stack.051|                    different default answers and different cost text. The
::X|EN|net.reset.ip.stack.052|                    stricter one is kept: there is no default answer here
::X|EN|net.reset.ip.stack.053|                    - the step requires typing RESET.
::X|EN|net.reset.ip.stack.054|
::X|EN|net.reset.ip.stack.055|  Target          : netsh int ip reset, inside :netreset - reached only
::X|EN|net.reset.ip.stack.056|                    from the Repair menu, behind a typed RESET
::X|EN|net.reset.ip.stack.057|                    confirmation and a call :restore_point (OPTY.bat
::X|EN|net.reset.ip.stack.058|                    ~2723-2742)
::X|FR|net.reset.ip.stack.001|  Ce que c est    : Reecrit toute la configuration de la pile TCP/IP dans
::X|FR|net.reset.ip.stack.002| le registre a l etat d usine. Menu Reparation
::X|FR|net.reset.ip.stack.003|                    uniquement, derriere une confirmation a taper (RESET).
::X|FR|net.reset.ip.stack.004|
::X|FR|net.reset.ip.stack.005|  Effet reel      : Toute la configuration IP de chaque interface est
::X|FR|net.reset.ip.stack.006|                    effacee : adresses IP fixes, serveurs DNS fixes,
::X|FR|net.reset.ip.stack.007|                    routes persistantes, metriques personnalisees. Toutes
::X|FR|net.reset.ip.stack.008|                    les cartes repassent en DHCP. Un redemarrage est
::X|FR|net.reset.ip.stack.009|                    obligatoire. OPTY reaffirme les trois reglages TCP
::X|FR|net.reset.ip.stack.010|                    globaux juste apres, parce que la reinitialisation les
::X|FR|net.reset.ip.stack.011|                    efface aussi.
::X|FR|net.reset.ip.stack.012|
::X|FR|net.reset.ip.stack.013|  Gain            : Repare une corruption au niveau de la pile que rien
::X|FR|net.reset.ip.stack.014| d autre n atteint : cartes qui refusent de prendre une
::X|FR|net.reset.ip.stack.015|                    adresse, interface toujours cassee apres
::X|FR|net.reset.ip.stack.016|                    reinstallation du pilote, table de routage fausse sans
::X|FR|net.reset.ip.stack.017| raison visible. Quand c est bien cela la panne, c est
::X|FR|net.reset.ip.stack.018|                    ce qui la corrige.
::X|FR|net.reset.ip.stack.019|
::X|FR|net.reset.ip.stack.020|  Cout            : OPTY ne peut pas annuler cela. Sur une machine
::X|FR|net.reset.ip.stack.021|                    simplement en DHCP, vous ne verrez rien. Si vous
::X|FR|net.reset.ip.stack.022|                    pointez vers un Pi-hole ou NextDNS, si vous avez une
::X|FR|net.reset.ip.stack.023|                    IP fixe, une route persistante vers un sous-reseau VPN
::X|FR|net.reset.ip.stack.024|                    ou un NAS, ou un DNS impose par une configuration
::X|FR|net.reset.ip.stack.025| d entreprise, tout est efface et il faudra tout
::X|FR|net.reset.ip.stack.026| ressaisir a la main. Sauvegardez la sortie d ipconfig
::X|FR|net.reset.ip.stack.027|                    /all et de route print avant de dire oui, et verifiez
::X|FR|net.reset.ip.stack.028| qu un point de restauration existe.
::X|FR|net.reset.ip.stack.029|
::X|FR|net.reset.ip.stack.030|  Defaut Windows  : Sans objet - par definition, cela retablit la
::X|FR|net.reset.ip.stack.031| configuration de pile d usine.
::X|FR|net.reset.ip.stack.032|
::X|FR|net.reset.ip.stack.033|  Valeurs possibles :
::X|FR|net.reset.ip.stack.034|    RESET                : Toute la configuration TCP/IP par interface
::X|FR|net.reset.ip.stack.035| dans le registre est reecrite a l etat d usine.
::X|FR|net.reset.ip.stack.036|                           Adresses IP fixes, serveurs DNS fixes, routes
::X|FR|net.reset.ip.stack.037| persistantes et metriques d interface
::X|FR|net.reset.ip.stack.038|                           personnalisees disparaissent, chaque carte
::X|FR|net.reset.ip.stack.039|                           repasse en DHCP, et un redemarrage est
::X|FR|net.reset.ip.stack.040|                           obligatoire avant que la machine soit
::X|FR|net.reset.ip.stack.041|                           utilisable comme configuree.
::X|FR|net.reset.ip.stack.042| SKIP : Rien n est touche. C est ce que produit toute
::X|FR|net.reset.ip.stack.043|                           saisie autre que RESET.
::X|FR|net.reset.ip.stack.044|
::X|FR|net.reset.ip.stack.045|  Pourquoi ces profils : Cinq colonnes a SKIP, deliberement. Aucun profil
::X|FR|net.reset.ip.stack.046| d usage n est une raison de reinitialiser une
::X|FR|net.reset.ip.stack.047|                         pile TCP/IP ; une panne reproductible en est une,
::X|FR|net.reset.ip.stack.048| et rien d autre. Les colonnes serveur et portable
::X|FR|net.reset.ip.stack.049|                         sont celles qui ont le plus a perdre, car ce sont
::X|FR|net.reset.ip.stack.050|                         les machines les plus susceptibles de porter une
::X|FR|net.reset.ip.stack.051|                         adresse fixe, un resolveur impose ou une route
::X|FR|net.reset.ip.stack.052|                         persistante - mais meme la colonne Windows est a
::X|FR|net.reset.ip.stack.053|                         SKIP, parce que Windows ne se fait pas cela a
