:: ---- net.reset.winsock.catalog (risky) -------------------------
::P|net.reset.winsock.catalog|SKIP|SKIP|SKIP|SKIP|SKIP|
::T|EN|net.reset.winsock.catalog.001|RESET THE WINSOCK CATALOG (DESTRUCTIVE REPAIR)
::T|EN|net.reset.winsock.catalog.002|Clears out network software drivers (VPN clients, some firewalls, security suites) that may be blocking apps from connecting even though the network itself looks fine - fixes that specific problem, but you will likely need to reinstall that software afterward.
::T|FR|net.reset.winsock.catalog.001|REINITIALISER LE CATALOGUE WINSOCK (REPARATION DESTRUCTIVE)
::T|FR|net.reset.winsock.catalog.002|Efface les logiciels reseau tiers (client VPN, certains pare-feu, suites de securite) qui peuvent empecher les applications de se connecter meme quand le reseau semble fonctionner - regle ce probleme precis, mais il faudra sans doute reinstaller ces logiciels ensuite.
::X|EN|net.reset.winsock.catalog.001|  What it is      : Resets the Winsock catalog to its default entries.
::X|EN|net.reset.winsock.catalog.002|                    Same typed RESET gate as the IP reset, and OPTY runs
::X|EN|net.reset.winsock.catalog.003|                    the two together in one step.
::X|EN|net.reset.winsock.catalog.004|
::X|EN|net.reset.winsock.catalog.005|  Actual effect   : Third-party LSPs are removed from the chain. VPN
::X|EN|net.reset.winsock.catalog.006|                    clients, some firewalls, older security suites and a
::X|EN|net.reset.winsock.catalog.007|                    few parental-control tools install LSPs and may need
::X|EN|net.reset.winsock.catalog.008|                    reinstalling before they work again. A reboot is
::X|EN|net.reset.winsock.catalog.009|                    required.
::X|EN|net.reset.winsock.catalog.010|
::X|EN|net.reset.winsock.catalog.011|  Gain            : Removes a broken or orphaned LSP - the classic cause
::X|EN|net.reset.winsock.catalog.012|                    of the symptom where the network is up and ping works
::X|EN|net.reset.winsock.catalog.013|                    but no application can connect. When that is the
::X|EN|net.reset.winsock.catalog.014|                    fault, nothing else fixes it.
::X|EN|net.reset.winsock.catalog.015|
::X|EN|net.reset.winsock.catalog.016|  Cost            : OPTY cannot undo this. Expect to reinstall your VPN
::X|EN|net.reset.winsock.catalog.017|                    client or security suite. And note that OPTY runs this
::X|EN|net.reset.winsock.catalog.018|                    in the same step as netsh int ip reset, so everything
::X|EN|net.reset.winsock.catalog.019|                    that step wipes goes with it: static IP, static DNS
::X|EN|net.reset.winsock.catalog.020|                    including a Pi-hole or NextDNS address, DNS pushed by
::X|EN|net.reset.winsock.catalog.021|                    corporate configuration, persistent routes and
::X|EN|net.reset.winsock.catalog.022|                    interface metrics. Save the output of ipconfig /all
::X|EN|net.reset.winsock.catalog.023|                    and route print first. On a machine with no such
::X|EN|net.reset.winsock.catalog.024|                    software, the practical cost is a reboot.
::X|EN|net.reset.winsock.catalog.025|
::X|EN|net.reset.winsock.catalog.026|  Windows default : Not applicable - it restores the default catalog by
::X|EN|net.reset.winsock.catalog.027|                    definition.
::X|EN|net.reset.winsock.catalog.028|
::X|EN|net.reset.winsock.catalog.029|  Possible values:
::X|EN|net.reset.winsock.catalog.030|    RESET                : The Winsock catalog - the list of layered
::X|EN|net.reset.winsock.catalog.031|                           service providers every socket call passes
::X|EN|net.reset.winsock.catalog.032|                           through - is rewritten to its default entries.
::X|EN|net.reset.winsock.catalog.033|                           Third-party LSPs are removed from the chain and
::X|EN|net.reset.winsock.catalog.034|                           a reboot is required.
::X|EN|net.reset.winsock.catalog.035|    SKIP                 : Nothing is touched, and the LSP chain stays as
::X|EN|net.reset.winsock.catalog.036|                           it is.
::X|EN|net.reset.winsock.catalog.037|
::X|EN|net.reset.winsock.catalog.038|  Why these profiles : Five SKIP columns. This is for one specific symptom
::X|EN|net.reset.winsock.catalog.039|                       - connectivity present but applications unable to
::X|EN|net.reset.winsock.catalog.040|                       reach the network - after the simple steps have
::X|EN|net.reset.winsock.catalog.041|                       failed, and no usage profile makes it more or less
::X|EN|net.reset.winsock.catalog.042|                       appropriate. The server profile is the one most
::X|EN|net.reset.winsock.catalog.043|                       likely to have a VPN client or a security suite
::X|EN|net.reset.winsock.catalog.044|                       whose LSPs need reinstalling afterwards, which is a
::X|EN|net.reset.winsock.catalog.045|                       reason for more caution, not a reason to differ.
::X|EN|net.reset.winsock.catalog.046|
::X|EN|net.reset.winsock.catalog.047|  Known problems  : The deck carried two copies of this card with
::X|EN|net.reset.winsock.catalog.048|                    different default answers. The stricter one is kept:
::X|EN|net.reset.winsock.catalog.049|                    there is no default answer - the step requires typing
::X|EN|net.reset.winsock.catalog.050|                    RESET, and it is inseparable from the IP reset that
::X|EN|net.reset.winsock.catalog.051|                    runs alongside it.
::X|EN|net.reset.winsock.catalog.052|
::X|EN|net.reset.winsock.catalog.053|  Target          : netsh winsock reset, inside :netreset - runs in the
::X|EN|net.reset.winsock.catalog.054|                    same step as netsh int ip reset, behind the same typed
::X|EN|net.reset.winsock.catalog.055|                    RESET confirmation and restore point (OPTY.bat
::X|EN|net.reset.winsock.catalog.056|                    ~2743-2744)
::X|FR|net.reset.winsock.catalog.001| Ce que c est : Remet le catalogue Winsock a ses entrees d origine.
::X|FR|net.reset.winsock.catalog.002|                    Meme verrou que la reinitialisation IP - il faut taper
::X|FR|net.reset.winsock.catalog.003|                    RESET - et OPTY execute les deux dans la meme etape.
::X|FR|net.reset.winsock.catalog.004|
::X|FR|net.reset.winsock.catalog.005|  Effet reel      : Les LSP tiers sont retires de la chaine. Les clients
::X|FR|net.reset.winsock.catalog.006|                    VPN, certains pare-feu, les anciennes suites de
