::T|EN|net.tcp.globals.assert.postreset.001|RE-APPLY TCP SETTINGS AFTER A STACK RESET
::T|EN|net.tcp.globals.assert.postreset.002|Automatically restores Windows normal network auto-tuning settings right after a stack reset clears them, so the repair finishes in the standard state instead of whatever the reset happened to leave behind.
::T|FR|net.tcp.globals.assert.postreset.001|REAPPLIQUER LES REGLAGES TCP APRES UNE REINITIALISATION
::T|FR|net.tcp.globals.assert.postreset.002|Retablit automatiquement les reglages d auto-tuning reseau normaux de Windows juste apres qu une reinitialisation de pile les a effaces, pour que la reparation se termine dans l etat standard plutot que dans un etat indetermine.
::X|EN|net.tcp.globals.assert.postreset.001|  What it is      : The same three machine-wide TCP settings, written
::X|EN|net.tcp.globals.assert.postreset.002|                    again inside the reset step because netsh int ip reset
::X|EN|net.tcp.globals.assert.postreset.003|                    takes the stack back to a state where they have to be
::X|EN|net.tcp.globals.assert.postreset.004|                    re-established.
::X|EN|net.tcp.globals.assert.postreset.005|
::X|EN|net.tcp.globals.assert.postreset.006|  Actual effect   : Three netsh calls run immediately after the reset.
::X|EN|net.tcp.globals.assert.postreset.007|                    Without them the machine would come back from a repair
::X|EN|net.tcp.globals.assert.postreset.008|                    with its TCP globals in whatever state the reset
::X|EN|net.tcp.globals.assert.postreset.009|                    produced, which is not necessarily where you left
::X|EN|net.tcp.globals.assert.postreset.010|                    them.
::X|EN|net.tcp.globals.assert.postreset.011|
::X|EN|net.tcp.globals.assert.postreset.012|  Gain            : It closes the reset step properly: the machine reboots
::X|EN|net.tcp.globals.assert.postreset.013|                    with autotuning at normal and RSS on rather than with
::X|EN|net.tcp.globals.assert.postreset.014|                    whatever the reset left behind. On its own it changes
::X|EN|net.tcp.globals.assert.postreset.015|                    nothing on a stock machine.
::X|EN|net.tcp.globals.assert.postreset.016|
::X|EN|net.tcp.globals.assert.postreset.017|  Cost            : None. All three are the shipped values, so this cannot
::X|EN|net.tcp.globals.assert.postreset.018|                    leave the stack in a worse place than the reset did.
::X|EN|net.tcp.globals.assert.postreset.019|
::X|EN|net.tcp.globals.assert.postreset.020|  Windows default : autotuninglevel=normal, rss=enabled and Window Scaling
::X|EN|net.tcp.globals.assert.postreset.021|                    Heuristics disabled are all Windows defaults - WSH has
