::P|recycle.bin.all.drives|DELETE|DELETE|DELETE|DELETE|SKIP|
::T|EN|recycle.bin.all.drives.001|RECYCLE BIN ON EVERY FIXED DRIVE, EVERY USER
::T|EN|recycle.bin.all.drives.002|Permanently empties every user's deleted files on every fixed drive to free up space - once this runs there is no way to get any of it back, so check your own bin first.
::T|FR|recycle.bin.all.drives.001|CORBEILLE DE CHAQUE DISQUE INTERNE, TOUS UTILISATEURS
::T|FR|recycle.bin.all.drives.002|Supprime definitivement les fichiers supprimes de tout le monde sur chaque disque interne pour liberer de la place - une fois lance, aucun retour en arriere possible, alors videz d abord votre propre corbeille.
::X|EN|recycle.bin.all.drives.001|  What it is      : $Recycle.Bin at the root of each drive is where
::X|EN|recycle.bin.all.drives.002|                    deleted files wait until the bin is emptied. It holds
::X|EN|recycle.bin.all.drives.003|                    one subfolder per user account on the machine. This
::X|EN|recycle.bin.all.drives.004|                    step removes the whole store on every fixed drive with
::X|EN|recycle.bin.all.drives.005|                    rd /S /Q.
::X|EN|recycle.bin.all.drives.006|
::X|EN|recycle.bin.all.drives.007|  Actual effect   : Permanently destroys everything every account on this
::X|EN|recycle.bin.all.drives.008|                    machine had deleted but not yet purged. It bypasses
::X|EN|recycle.bin.all.drives.009|                    the shell API entirely, so this is not Empty Recycle
::X|EN|recycle.bin.all.drives.010|                    Bin for you - it is Empty Recycle Bin for everybody,
::X|EN|recycle.bin.all.drives.011|                    on C: and on every other fixed drive.
::X|EN|recycle.bin.all.drives.012|
::X|EN|recycle.bin.all.drives.013|  Gain            : Disk space, and sometimes a great deal of it: a bin
::X|EN|recycle.bin.all.drives.014|                    nobody has emptied for a year can hold tens of GB.
::X|EN|recycle.bin.all.drives.015|                    There is no performance benefit of any kind - a full
::X|EN|recycle.bin.all.drives.016|                    Recycle Bin does not slow anything down.
::X|EN|recycle.bin.all.drives.017|
::X|EN|recycle.bin.all.drives.018|  Cost            : Every deleted file becomes unrecoverable, including
::X|EN|recycle.bin.all.drives.019|                    files another user of this machine deleted five
::X|EN|recycle.bin.all.drives.020|                    minutes ago and may still want back. Regeneration time
::X|EN|recycle.bin.all.drives.021|                    for this data is infinite: it never comes back, which
::X|EN|recycle.bin.all.drives.022|                    is exactly what makes it the odd one out among the
