::X|EN|defrag.all.volumes.061|                       for the same reason in reverse: gaming, office and
::X|EN|defrag.all.volumes.062|                       laptop machines here are SSD-backed and go idle
::X|EN|defrag.all.volumes.063|                       regularly, so the weekly task has already done
::X|EN|defrag.all.volumes.064|                       everything a manual run would do, and on the laptop
::X|EN|defrag.all.volumes.065|                       it would also be minutes of full-rate disk activity
::X|EN|defrag.all.volumes.066|                       on battery. The Windows column is SKIP because a
::X|EN|defrag.all.volumes.067|                       manual, unthrottled run is not something Windows
::X|EN|defrag.all.volumes.068|                       ever does to itself.
::X|EN|defrag.all.volumes.069|
