:: ---- chkdsk.full.repair (risky) --------------------------------
::P|chkdsk.full.repair|SKIP|SKIP|SKIP|SKIP|SKIP|
::T|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.001|FULL DISK REPAIR SCAN (CHKDSK /F /R)
::T|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.002|Reads every sector of the disk to find and repair real damage - it can take many hours and cannot be canceled once started, so only run it if you actually suspect disk corruption, not as routine maintenance.
::T|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.001|REPARATION COMPLETE DU DISQUE (CHKDSK /F /R)
::T|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.002|Lit chaque secteur du disque pour trouver et reparer de vrais degats - cela peut durer des heures et ne peut plus etre annule une fois lance, a reserver donc aux cas ou vous soupconnez vraiment une corruption, pas a l entretien courant.
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.001|  What it is      : CHKDSK /f fixes filesystem errors; /r additionally
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.002|                    reads every sector on the disk looking for bad ones
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.003|                    and relocating whatever data is still readable out of
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.004|                    them.
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.005|
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.006|  Actual effect   : Depends on which volume it lands on. If the volume can
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.007|                    be locked it runs there and then, holding it for the
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.008|                    whole scan. If it cannot - the system drive, while
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.009|                    Windows is running - it offers to schedule the check
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.010|                    for the next restart, and the check then runs before
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.011|                    Windows loads with no way to use the machine
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.012|                    meanwhile.
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.013|
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.014|  Gain            : On a mechanical drive with real errors, this is the
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.015|                    tool that repairs the filesystem and maps out failing
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.016|                    sectors. If your problem is genuine disk corruption,
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.017|                    nothing else in this menu will fix it. On a healthy
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.018|                    machine, or on an SSD, /r produces no finding and no
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.019|                    benefit.
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.020|
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.021|  Cost            : On a large or slow disk it can run for many hours, and
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.022|                    it cannot be cancelled once it has started. The
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.023|                    surface scan hammers a drive that is already dying and
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.024|                    can be the push that finishes it - on a failing disk
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.025|                    you should be imaging your data, not scanning it. /r
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.026|                    is designed for spinning rust and has no place on an
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.027|                    SSD, where the controller's own remapping is invisible
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.028|                    to chkdsk anyway. You can cancel a scheduled boot-time
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.029|                    check with chkntfs /x C: before rebooting.
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.030|
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.031|  Windows default : Not scheduled by default. Windows only runs autochk on
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.032|                    a volume it has flagged dirty.
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.033|
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.034|  Possible values:
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.035|    RUN                  : chkdsk /f /r on the target volume. /f fixes
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.036|                           filesystem errors and needs an exclusive lock.
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.037|                           /r adds a full surface scan: every sector is
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.038|                           read, and any data still readable in a failing
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.039|                           sector is copied elsewhere and the sector
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.040|                           marked bad. On a volume Windows can lock, it
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.041|                           starts immediately and holds the volume for the
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.042|                           duration. On a volume it cannot lock, such as
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.043|                           the system drive, it offers to schedule the
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.044|                           check for the next restart, and autochk runs it
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.045|                           before Windows loads.
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.046|    RUN /F ONLY          : chkdsk /f without /r. Repairs the filesystem
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.047|                           structures but skips the sector-by-sector
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.048|                           surface scan. This is the appropriate form on
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.049|                           an SSD, where reading every sector tells you
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.050|                           nothing useful about the flash underneath and
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.051|                           the controller has already remapped what it
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.052|                           needed to.
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.053|    SKIP                 : Nothing is scheduled and nothing runs. Windows
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.054|                           only invokes autochk on a volume it has itself
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.055|                           flagged dirty, which is a state it sets after a
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.056|                           specific failure, not as routine.
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.057|
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.058|  Why these profiles : All five columns say SKIP, and that is a decision
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.059|                       rather than an evasion. The trigger for this tool
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.060|                       is not a use case, it is a symptom on rotational
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.061|                       media: file corruption, CRC errors in the event
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.062|                       log, freezes on read. None of the four use profiles
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.063|                       implies either of those - a gaming desktop, a Plex
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.064|                       server, an office PC and a laptop are all equally
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.065|                       likely to be fine, and this project's machines are
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.066|                       SSD-backed, where /r cannot help at all. Anyone
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.067|                       with the symptom takes it deliberately, after a
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.068|                       backup, and does not need a profile to tell them.
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.069|
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.070|  Known problems  : Line 1268 is CHKDSK /f /r with no volume argument,
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.071|                    while the online scan on line 1256 correctly passes
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.072|                    %SystemDrive%. With no argument chkdsk operates on the
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.073|                    current directory's drive, which is whatever volume
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.074|                    OPTY.bat was launched from - on this machine that is
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.075|                    E:, not C:. Two consequences follow. The card's whole
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.076|                    premise, that it must schedule itself for the next
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.077|                    reboot because the system drive cannot be locked, only
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.078|                    holds for C:; on a data volume chkdsk locks it and
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.079|                    starts a multi-hour surface scan immediately, with no
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.080|                    reboot and no second chance to back out. And the user
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.081|                    who chose this menu item to check their system drive
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.082|                    did not check their system drive. Line 1268 should
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.083|                    read: CHKDSK %SystemDrive% /f /r.
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.084|
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.085|  Unverified      : The bug above is read directly from the source line,
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.086|                    not observed at runtime, because running it to find
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.087|                    out is precisely the thing this card advises against.
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.088|
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.089|  Target          : CHKDSK /f /r - OPTY.bat line 1268, inside the
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.090|                    :chkdsk_full label, reached from the :mchkdsk menu
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.091|                    option 2. Note there is NO volume argument on that
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.092|                    line, unlike the online scan at line 1256 which passes
::X|EN|chkdsk.full.repair.093|                    %SystemDrive%.
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.001|  Ce que c est    : CHKDSK /f corrige les erreurs du systeme de fichiers ;
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.002|                    /r lit en plus chaque secteur du disque pour reperer
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.003|                    les secteurs defectueux et deplacer les donnees encore
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.004|                    lisibles qui s y trouvent.
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.005|
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.006|  Effet reel      : Depend du volume vise. Si le volume peut etre
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.007|                    verrouille, il s execute sur-le-champ et le garde
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.008|                    pendant toute l analyse. S il ne le peut pas - le
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.009|                    disque systeme, pendant que Windows tourne - il
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.010|                    propose de planifier la verification au prochain
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.011|                    redemarrage, et celle-ci s execute alors avant le
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.012|                    chargement de Windows, sans possibilite d utiliser la
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.013|                    machine entre-temps.
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.014|
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.015|  Gain            : Sur un disque mecanique reellement en erreur, c est
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.016|                    l outil qui repare le systeme de fichiers et met de
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.017|                    cote les secteurs defaillants. Si votre probleme est
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.018|                    une vraie corruption disque, rien d autre dans ce menu
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.019|                    ne le corrigera. Sur une machine saine, ou sur un SSD,
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.020|                    /r ne trouve rien et n apporte rien.
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.021|
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.022|  Cout            : Sur un disque gros ou lent, cela peut durer des
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.023|                    heures, et on ne peut plus l annuler une fois lance.
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.024|                    L analyse de surface malmene un disque deja mourant et
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.025|                    peut l achever : sur un disque en fin de vie, il faut
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.026|                    copier vos donnees, pas les scanner. /r est concu pour
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.027|                    les disques a plateaux et n a pas sa place sur un SSD,
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.028|                    ou le remappage effectue par le controleur reste de
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.029|                    toute facon invisible pour chkdsk. On annule une
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.030|                    verification planifiee au demarrage avec chkntfs /x C:
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.031|                    avant de redemarrer.
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.032|
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.033|  Defaut Windows  : Non planifie par defaut. Windows ne lance autochk que
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.034|                    sur un volume qu il a marque comme sale.
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.035|
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.036|  Valeurs possibles :
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.037|    RUN                  : chkdsk /f /r sur le volume vise. /f corrige les
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.038|                           erreurs du systeme de fichiers et exige un
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.039|                           verrou exclusif. /r ajoute une analyse de
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.040|                           surface complete : chaque secteur est lu, et
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.041|                           toute donnee encore lisible dans un secteur
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.042|                           defaillant est recopiee ailleurs avant que le
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.043|                           secteur soit marque comme mauvais. Sur un
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.044|                           volume que Windows peut verrouiller, il demarre
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.045|                           immediatement et garde le volume pendant toute
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.046|                           la duree. Sur un volume qu il ne peut pas
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.047|                           verrouiller, comme le disque systeme, il
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.048|                           propose de planifier la verification au
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.049|                           prochain redemarrage, et autochk l execute
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.050|                           avant le chargement de Windows.
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.051|    RUN /F ONLY          : chkdsk /f sans /r. Repare les structures du
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.052|                           systeme de fichiers mais saute l analyse
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.053|                           secteur par secteur. C est la forme appropriee
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.054|                           sur un SSD, ou lire chaque secteur n apprend
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.055|                           rien d utile sur la memoire flash sous-jacente
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.056|                           et ou le controleur a deja remappe ce qu il
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.057|                           devait.
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.058|    SKIP                 : Rien n est planifie et rien ne s execute.
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.059|                           Windows n invoque autochk que sur un volume
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.060|                           qu il a lui-meme marque comme sale, un etat
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.061|                           qu il pose apres une defaillance precise et non
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.062|                           en routine.
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.063|
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.064|  Pourquoi ces profils : Les cinq colonnes repondent SKIP, et c est une
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.065|                         decision, pas une esquive. Le declencheur de cet
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.066|                         outil n est pas un usage mais un symptome sur
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.067|                         support a plateaux : fichiers corrompus, erreurs
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.068|                         CRC dans le journal d evenements, gels en
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.069|                         lecture. Aucun des quatre profils d usage
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.070|                         n implique l un ou l autre - un PC de jeu, un
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.071|                         serveur Plex, un poste bureautique et un portable
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.072|                         ont exactement autant de chances d aller bien, et
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.073|                         les machines de ce projet sont sur SSD, ou /r ne
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.074|                         peut rien apporter. Celui qui a le symptome le
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.075|                         lance deliberement, apres sauvegarde, et n a pas
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.076|                         besoin d un profil pour le lui dire.
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.077|
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.078|  Problemes connus : La ligne 1268 est CHKDSK /f /r sans argument de
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.079|                     volume, alors que l analyse en ligne de la ligne 1256
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.080|                     passe correctement %SystemDrive%. Sans argument,
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.081|                     chkdsk agit sur le disque du repertoire courant,
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.082|                     c est-a-dire le volume depuis lequel OPTY.bat a ete
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.083|                     lance - sur cette machine, E: et non C:. Deux
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.084|                     consequences. Toute la premisse de la fiche, a savoir
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.085|                     qu il doit se planifier au prochain redemarrage parce
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.086|                     que le disque systeme ne peut pas etre verrouille, ne
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.087|                     vaut que pour C: ; sur un volume de donnees, chkdsk
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.088|                     le verrouille et demarre immediatement une analyse de
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.089|                     surface de plusieurs heures, sans redemarrage et sans
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.090|                     seconde chance de se raviser. Et l utilisateur qui a
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.091|                     choisi cette entree de menu pour verifier son disque
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.092|                     systeme n a pas verifie son disque systeme. La ligne
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.093|                     1268 devrait etre : CHKDSK %SystemDrive% /f /r.
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.094|
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.095|  Non verifie (en)  : The bug above is read directly from the source line,
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.096|                      not observed at runtime, because running it to find
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.097|                      out is precisely the thing this card advises
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.098|                      against.
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.099|
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.100|  Cible           : CHKDSK /f /r - OPTY.bat line 1268, inside the
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.101|                    :chkdsk_full label, reached from the :mchkdsk menu
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.102|                    option 2. Note there is NO volume argument on that
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.103|                    line, unlike the online scan at line 1256 which passes
::X|FR|chkdsk.full.repair.104|                    %SystemDrive%.
