:: ---- gr.8dot3.default (repair) ----------------------------------
::P|gr.8dot3.default|2|2|2|2|2|
::T|EN|gr.8dot3.default.001|8.3 SHORT NAMES BACK TO PER-VOLUME
::T|EN|gr.8dot3.default.002|The restore-menu twin of the same repair: undoes a global short-filename override left behind by another tuning tool, with no speed change of any kind, just fewer old-installer breakages.
::T|FR|gr.8dot3.default.001|NOMS COURTS 8.3 REMIS EN MODE PAR VOLUME
::T|FR|gr.8dot3.default.002|La version restauration de la meme reparation : annule un forcage global des noms courts laisse par un autre outil de reglage, sans aucun changement de vitesse, juste moins de casse sur les vieux installeurs.
::X|EN|gr.8dot3.default.001|  What it is      : Whether NTFS also creates an old DOS-style 8.3 name
::X|EN|gr.8dot3.default.002|                    for each file. This is the restore-menu version: same
::X|EN|gr.8dot3.default.003|                    write, reached when you are undoing someone else's
::X|EN|gr.8dot3.default.004|                    tuning rather than setting up.
::X|EN|gr.8dot3.default.005|
::X|EN|gr.8dot3.default.006|  Actual effect   : Sets mode 2 - each volume decides, instead of a global
::X|EN|gr.8dot3.default.007|                    on or off. Applies to names created from now on only;
::X|EN|gr.8dot3.default.008|                    short names that already exist stay, and short names
::X|EN|gr.8dot3.default.009|                    that were never created during a period at value 1 do
::X|EN|gr.8dot3.default.010|                    not appear retroactively.
::X|EN|gr.8dot3.default.011|
::X|EN|gr.8dot3.default.012|  Gain            : No measurable speed gain, and this card does not
::X|EN|gr.8dot3.default.013|                    pretend otherwise. What it removes is a global
::X|EN|gr.8dot3.default.014|                    override that can break old installers and
::X|EN|gr.8dot3.default.015|                    uninstallers relying on short paths. That is the
::X|EN|gr.8dot3.default.016|                    entire benefit and it is a real one.
::X|EN|gr.8dot3.default.017|
::X|EN|gr.8dot3.default.018|  Cost            : Nothing. This is a pure repair back to the shipped
::X|EN|gr.8dot3.default.019|                    value.
::X|EN|gr.8dot3.default.020|
::X|EN|gr.8dot3.default.021|  Windows default : 2.
::X|EN|gr.8dot3.default.022|
::X|EN|gr.8dot3.default.023|  Possible values:
::X|EN|gr.8dot3.default.024|    0                    : Short names created on every volume. More
::X|EN|gr.8dot3.default.025|                           metadata per file, maximum compatibility with
::X|EN|gr.8dot3.default.026|                           pre-1995 software conventions.
::X|EN|gr.8dot3.default.027|    1                    : Short names disabled everywhere, system volume
::X|EN|gr.8dot3.default.028|                           included. This is the value the restore path
::X|EN|gr.8dot3.default.029|                           exists to undo - a global override written by a
::X|EN|gr.8dot3.default.030|                           tuning script, which no Windows installer or
::X|EN|gr.8dot3.default.031|                           Settings page ever sets.
::X|EN|gr.8dot3.default.032|    2                    : Per-volume. Windows decides per volume, which
::X|EN|gr.8dot3.default.033|                           is the shipped policy and what this step
::X|EN|gr.8dot3.default.034|                           writes.
::X|EN|gr.8dot3.default.035|    3                    : Disabled everywhere except the system volume. A
::X|EN|gr.8dot3.default.036|                           deliberate compromise, not a default, and not
::X|EN|gr.8dot3.default.037|                           what a restore should produce.
::X|EN|gr.8dot3.default.038|
::X|EN|gr.8dot3.default.039|  Why these profiles : Five identical twos, for the same reason as the
::X|EN|gr.8dot3.default.040|                       setup-path card: the value is a compatibility
::X|EN|gr.8dot3.default.041|                       policy, not a performance dial, so no use case
::X|EN|gr.8dot3.default.042|                       pulls it in a different direction. Worth knowing
::X|EN|gr.8dot3.default.043|                       that these two cards perform the identical write
::X|EN|gr.8dot3.default.044|                       and differ only in which menu you reached them from
::X|EN|gr.8dot3.default.045|                       - if you have already run the setup path, this one
::X|EN|gr.8dot3.default.046|                       will report that the value was already correct,
::X|EN|gr.8dot3.default.047|                       which is exactly what it should say.
::X|EN|gr.8dot3.default.048|
::X|EN|gr.8dot3.default.049|  Target          : fsutil behavior set disable8dot3 2 - OPTY.bat line
::X|EN|gr.8dot3.default.050|                    1635, in the RESTORE path (Restoring 8.3 short names
::X|EN|gr.8dot3.default.051|                    (default)). Same write and same backing value as the
::X|EN|gr.8dot3.default.052|                    setup-path card:
::X|EN|gr.8dot3.default.053|                    HKLM\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\FileSystem /v
::X|EN|gr.8dot3.default.054|                    NtfsDisable8dot3NameCreation.
::X|FR|gr.8dot3.default.001|  Ce que c est    : Indique si NTFS cree aussi un nom court facon DOS pour
::X|FR|gr.8dot3.default.002|                    chaque fichier. Voici la version du menu de
