:: ---- rad.trim.on (repair) ---------------------------------------
::P|rad.trim.on|0|0|0|0|0|
::T|EN|rad.trim.on.001|RE-ENABLE TRIM FOR SSDS
::T|EN|rad.trim.on.002|The restore-menu version of the same TRIM fix: a real, lasting benefit only if TRIM had actually been switched off on this machine, otherwise a harmless no-op since Windows already ships with it on.
::T|FR|rad.trim.on.001|REACTIVER LE TRIM POUR LES SSD
::T|FR|rad.trim.on.002|La version restauration de la meme reparation TRIM : un vrai benefice durable seulement si le TRIM avait vraiment ete coupe sur cette machine, sinon une ecriture sans effet puisque Windows le livre deja actif.
::X|EN|rad.trim.on.001|  What it is      : TRIM tells an SSD which blocks are no longer in use so
::X|EN|rad.trim.on.002|                    it can erase them ahead of time. This is the restore-
::X|EN|rad.trim.on.003|                    menu version of the same repair.
::X|EN|rad.trim.on.004|
::X|EN|rad.trim.on.005|  Actual effect   : Sets the delete-notify behaviour to 0, so delete
::X|EN|rad.trim.on.006|                    notifications are sent again on both NTFS and ReFS
::X|EN|rad.trim.on.007|                    volumes.
::X|EN|rad.trim.on.008|
::X|EN|rad.trim.on.009|  Gain            : Real and cumulative on an SSD, but only where TRIM had
::X|EN|rad.trim.on.010|                    actually been turned off. Without TRIM, write
::X|EN|rad.trim.on.011|                    performance degrades over months as the drive runs out
::X|EN|rad.trim.on.012|                    of pre-erased blocks; restoring it lets the drive
::X|EN|rad.trim.on.013|                    rebuild that pool as blocks get rewritten. On the
::X|EN|rad.trim.on.014|                    overwhelmingly more common machine, where TRIM was
::X|EN|rad.trim.on.015|                    already on, this write changes nothing and claims
::X|EN|rad.trim.on.016|                    nothing.
::X|EN|rad.trim.on.017|
::X|EN|rad.trim.on.018|  Cost            : Nothing. One consequence worth stating plainly rather
::X|EN|rad.trim.on.019|                    than hiding: deleted data becomes genuinely
::X|EN|rad.trim.on.020|                    unrecoverable much sooner, so if you are in the middle
::X|EN|rad.trim.on.021|                    of trying to recover a deleted file, finish that
::X|EN|rad.trim.on.022|                    first.
::X|EN|rad.trim.on.023|
::X|EN|rad.trim.on.024|  Windows default : 0 - TRIM on.
::X|EN|rad.trim.on.025|
::X|EN|rad.trim.on.026|  Possible values:
::X|EN|rad.trim.on.027|    0                    : Delete notifications sent. Deleting a file
::X|EN|rad.trim.on.028|                           issues TRIM or UNMAP for its blocks, so the
::X|EN|rad.trim.on.029|                           controller erases those flash pages during idle
::X|EN|rad.trim.on.030|                           time and your next write goes into a ready
::X|EN|rad.trim.on.031|                           page. Shipped value.
::X|EN|rad.trim.on.032|    1                    : Delete notifications suppressed. The drive
::X|EN|rad.trim.on.033|                           never learns that blocks are free, its stock of
::X|EN|rad.trim.on.034|                           pre-erased pages drains, and each write
::X|EN|rad.trim.on.035|                           increasingly costs a read-modify-erase-write
::X|EN|rad.trim.on.036|                           cycle. The damage accumulates over months and
::X|EN|rad.trim.on.037|                           is only cleared by rewriting or secure-erasing
::X|EN|rad.trim.on.038|                           the drive.
::X|EN|rad.trim.on.039|
::X|EN|rad.trim.on.040|  Why these profiles : Five identical zeroes. Flash erase behaviour does
::X|EN|rad.trim.on.041|                       not care whether the machine games, serves or sits
::X|EN|rad.trim.on.042|                       on a desk, and 0 is the shipped value, so the
::X|EN|rad.trim.on.043|                       Windows column agrees with the other four rather
::X|EN|rad.trim.on.044|                       than dissenting. This card and the setup-path TRIM
::X|EN|rad.trim.on.045|                       card issue the identical command from two different
::X|EN|rad.trim.on.046|                       menus - running one after the other is harmless and
::X|EN|rad.trim.on.047|                       will simply report that the value was already
::X|EN|rad.trim.on.048|                       correct.
::X|EN|rad.trim.on.049|
::X|EN|rad.trim.on.050|  Target          : fsutil behavior set disabledeletenotify 0 - OPTY.bat
::X|EN|rad.trim.on.051|                    line 1870, in the RESTORE path (System perf defaults:
::X|EN|rad.trim.on.052|                    TRIM on, SysMain/Prefetch on, system-managed
::X|EN|rad.trim.on.053|                    pagefile). Same write and same backing values as the
::X|EN|rad.trim.on.054|                    setup-path TRIM card:
::X|EN|rad.trim.on.055|                    HKLM\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\FileSystem /v
::X|EN|rad.trim.on.056|                    NtfsDisableDeleteNotify and /v
::X|EN|rad.trim.on.057|                    RefsDisableDeleteNotify.
::X|FR|rad.trim.on.001|  Ce que c est    : Le TRIM indique au SSD quels blocs ne servent plus,
::X|FR|rad.trim.on.002|                    pour qu il les efface a l avance. Voici la version du
::X|FR|rad.trim.on.003|                    menu de restauration de la meme reparation.
::X|FR|rad.trim.on.004|
::X|FR|rad.trim.on.005|  Effet reel      : Met le comportement de notification de suppression a 0
::X|FR|rad.trim.on.006|                    : les notifications repartent, sur les volumes NTFS
::X|FR|rad.trim.on.007|                    comme ReFS.
::X|FR|rad.trim.on.008|
::X|FR|rad.trim.on.009|  Gain            : Reel et cumulatif sur SSD, mais uniquement la ou le
::X|FR|rad.trim.on.010|                    TRIM avait effectivement ete coupe. Sans TRIM, les
::X|FR|rad.trim.on.011|                    ecritures ralentissent au fil des mois faute de blocs
::X|FR|rad.trim.on.012|                    pre-effaces ; le retablir laisse le disque
::X|FR|rad.trim.on.013|                    reconstituer cette reserve a mesure que les blocs sont
::X|FR|rad.trim.on.014|                    reecrits. Sur la machine bien plus courante ou le TRIM
::X|FR|rad.trim.on.015|                    etait deja actif, cette ecriture ne change rien et ne
::X|FR|rad.trim.on.016|                    revendique rien.
::X|FR|rad.trim.on.017|
::X|FR|rad.trim.on.018|  Cout            : Rien. Une consequence merite d etre dite franchement
::X|FR|rad.trim.on.019|                    plutot que tue : les donnees supprimees deviennent
::X|FR|rad.trim.on.020|                    vraiment irrecuperables bien plus tot. Si vous etes en
::X|FR|rad.trim.on.021|                    pleine tentative de recuperation d un fichier,
::X|FR|rad.trim.on.022|                    terminez-la d abord.
::X|FR|rad.trim.on.023|
::X|FR|rad.trim.on.024|  Defaut Windows  : 0, TRIM actif.
::X|FR|rad.trim.on.025|
::X|FR|rad.trim.on.026|  Valeurs possibles :
::X|FR|rad.trim.on.027|    0                    : Notifications de suppression emises. Supprimer
::X|FR|rad.trim.on.028|                           un fichier declenche un TRIM ou un UNMAP sur
::X|FR|rad.trim.on.029|                           ses blocs : le controleur efface alors ces
::X|FR|rad.trim.on.030|                           pages de flash pendant ses temps morts et votre
::X|FR|rad.trim.on.031|                           prochaine ecriture entre dans une page prete.
::X|FR|rad.trim.on.032|                           Valeur livree.
::X|FR|rad.trim.on.033|    1                    : Notifications de suppression supprimees. Le
::X|FR|rad.trim.on.034|                           disque n apprend jamais que des blocs sont
::X|FR|rad.trim.on.035|                           libres, sa reserve de pages pre-effacees
::X|FR|rad.trim.on.036|                           s epuise, et chaque ecriture coute de plus en
::X|FR|rad.trim.on.037|                           plus souvent un cycle lecture-modification-
::X|FR|rad.trim.on.038|                           effacement-ecriture. Les degats s accumulent
::X|FR|rad.trim.on.039|                           sur des mois et ne se resorbent qu en
::X|FR|rad.trim.on.040|                           reecrivant ou en effacant securement le disque.
::X|FR|rad.trim.on.041|
::X|FR|rad.trim.on.042|  Pourquoi ces profils : Cinq zeros identiques. Le comportement
::X|FR|rad.trim.on.043|                         d effacement de la flash se moque de savoir si la
::X|FR|rad.trim.on.044|                         machine joue, heberge ou dort sur un bureau, et 0
::X|FR|rad.trim.on.045|                         est la valeur livree : la colonne Windows rejoint
::X|FR|rad.trim.on.046|                         donc les quatre autres au lieu de s en
::X|FR|rad.trim.on.047|                         distinguer. Cette fiche et celle du chemin de
::X|FR|rad.trim.on.048|                         configuration emettent la meme commande depuis
::X|FR|rad.trim.on.049|                         deux menus differents - enchainer les deux est
::X|FR|rad.trim.on.050|                         sans danger et signalera simplement que la valeur
::X|FR|rad.trim.on.051|                         etait deja correcte.
::X|FR|rad.trim.on.052|
::X|FR|rad.trim.on.053|  Cible           : fsutil behavior set disabledeletenotify 0 - OPTY.bat
::X|FR|rad.trim.on.054|                    line 1870, in the RESTORE path (System perf defaults:
::X|FR|rad.trim.on.055|                    TRIM on, SysMain/Prefetch on, system-managed
::X|FR|rad.trim.on.056|                    pagefile). Same write and same backing values as the
::X|FR|rad.trim.on.057|                    setup-path TRIM card:
::X|FR|rad.trim.on.058|                    HKLM\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\FileSystem /v
::X|FR|rad.trim.on.059|                    NtfsDisableDeleteNotify and /v
::X|FR|rad.trim.on.060|                    RefsDisableDeleteNotify.
::
:: ---- rad.vuln.driver.blocklist (repair) -------------------------
::P|rad.vuln.driver.blocklist|1|1|1|1|1|
::T|EN|rad.vuln.driver.blocklist.001|BLOCK KNOWN-VULNERABLE DRIVERS
::T|EN|rad.vuln.driver.blocklist.002|Turns back on Microsoft's list of signed-but-exploitable drivers that Windows should refuse to load - a real security fix against a common ransomware trick, with no performance cost at all.
::T|FR|rad.vuln.driver.blocklist.001|BLOQUER LES PILOTES CONNUS COMME VULNERABLES
::T|FR|rad.vuln.driver.blocklist.002|Reactive la liste de Microsoft des pilotes signes mais exploitables que Windows doit refuser de charger - une vraie protection contre une technique courante des rancongiciels, sans aucun cout de performance.
::X|EN|rad.vuln.driver.blocklist.001|  What it is      : A Microsoft-maintained list of signed but exploitable
::X|EN|rad.vuln.driver.blocklist.002|                    kernel drivers that Windows refuses to load. It is
::X|EN|rad.vuln.driver.blocklist.003|                    updated through Windows Update along with the rest of
::X|EN|rad.vuln.driver.blocklist.004|                    Code Integrity.
::X|EN|rad.vuln.driver.blocklist.005|
::X|EN|rad.vuln.driver.blocklist.006|  Actual effect   : Writes VulnerableDriverBlocklistEnable=1 under
::X|EN|rad.vuln.driver.blocklist.007|                    CI\Config. Takes effect at boot, and applies at each
::X|EN|rad.vuln.driver.blocklist.008|                    driver load thereafter.
::X|EN|rad.vuln.driver.blocklist.009|
::X|EN|rad.vuln.driver.blocklist.010|  Gain            : Blocks the bring-your-own-vulnerable-driver technique,
::X|EN|rad.vuln.driver.blocklist.011|                    which is how a great deal of ransomware disables
::X|EN|rad.vuln.driver.blocklist.012|                    antivirus before doing anything else. The cost side of
::X|EN|rad.vuln.driver.blocklist.013|                    this is genuinely zero: the check is a lookup
::X|EN|rad.vuln.driver.blocklist.014|                    performed once per driver load, not something in any
::X|EN|rad.vuln.driver.blocklist.015|                    hot path, so unlike most security features there is no
::X|EN|rad.vuln.driver.blocklist.016|                    performance argument on the other side of the scale.
::X|EN|rad.vuln.driver.blocklist.017|
::X|EN|rad.vuln.driver.blocklist.018|  Cost            : A very old utility or overclocking tool that ships a
::X|EN|rad.vuln.driver.blocklist.019|                    blocklisted driver stops working. That is the entire
