::X|FR|rad.driververifier.killkey.058|                         l intention : si vous n avez pas lance Verifier,
::X|FR|rad.driververifier.killkey.059|                         il ne devrait pas tourner ; et si vous l avez
::X|FR|rad.driververifier.killkey.060|                         lance, vous n avez pas besoin de cette fiche.
::X|FR|rad.driververifier.killkey.061|
::X|FR|rad.driververifier.killkey.062|  Non verifie (en)  : The previous version of this card claimed Verifier
::X|FR|rad.driververifier.killkey.063|                      can roughly halve I/O throughput. I could not
::X|FR|rad.driververifier.killkey.064|                      substantiate that figure, and it cannot be right as
::X|FR|rad.driververifier.killkey.065|                      a constant: the cost is a function of the
::X|FR|rad.driververifier.killkey.066|                      VerifyDriverLevel bitmask and of how many drivers
::X|FR|rad.driververifier.killkey.067|                      VerifyDrivers covers, so it ranges from modest to
::X|FR|rad.driververifier.killkey.068|                      severe. The card now states the mechanism and drops
::X|FR|rad.driververifier.killkey.069|                      the number. The claim that survives is the one that
::X|FR|rad.driververifier.killkey.070|                      matters and is checkable: nothing in the Windows
::X|FR|rad.driververifier.killkey.071|                      interface tells you Verifier is on.
::X|FR|rad.driververifier.killkey.072|
::X|FR|rad.driververifier.killkey.073|  Cible           : Two :killkey calls at OPTY.bat lines 1927 and 1928
::X|FR|rad.driververifier.killkey.074|                    against %MMK%, which is set at OPTY.bat line 1899 to
::X|FR|rad.driververifier.killkey.075|                    HKLM\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\Session
::X|FR|rad.driververifier.killkey.076|                    Manager\Memory Management - value names VerifyDrivers
::X|FR|rad.driververifier.killkey.077|                    (REG_SZ) and VerifyDriverLevel (REG_DWORD).
