:: ---- rad.sysmain.auto (preference) ----------------------------------
::P|rad.sysmain.auto|auto|auto|auto|auto|auto|
::T|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.001|SYSMAIN: KEEP IT ON AUTOMATIC
::T|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.002|Keeps SysMain (Superfetch) automatic and running so the prefetch settings actually do something; the gain is small on SSD, but this is the state Windows is tested to run in.
::T|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.001|SYSMAIN : GARDER EN AUTOMATIQUE
::T|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.002|Garde SysMain (Superfetch) en automatique et actif pour que les reglages de prechargement servent a quelque chose ; le gain est faible sur SSD, mais c est l etat dans lequel Windows est teste.
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.001|  What it is      : SysMain, the service formerly called Superfetch, does
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.002|                    prefetching and standby-list management. It is what
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.003|                    actually makes the EnablePrefetcher value do anything
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.004|                    - the registry value alone is inert without the
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.005|                    service.
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.006|
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.007|  Actual effect   : Sets start type to auto and starts the service now, in
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.008|                    the same block that re-asserts TRIM and the prefetcher
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.009|                    value, so the three parts of that story are written
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.010|                    together.
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.011|
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.012|  Gain            : On a machine with a mechanical hard disk, noticeably
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.013|                    faster app launches. On an SSD or NVMe the difference
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.014|                    is small and often inside measurement noise - the real
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.015|                    reason to have it running is that Windows 11 is
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.016|                    designed and tested with it on, not a stopwatch
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.017|                    result.
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.018|
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.019|  Cost            : Some disk activity in the first minutes after boot,
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.020|                    and a memory footprint you will see in Task Manager as
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.021|                    standby memory. Standby memory is cache, not usage:
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.022|                    any process that asks for it gets it back immediately.
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.023|
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.024|  Windows default : 2 (Automatic), running.
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.025|
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.026|  Possible values:
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.027|    auto                 : Start=2 and the service is started immediately.
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.028|                           SysMain resumes tracking which executables you
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.029|                           launch, pre-populates the standby list with
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.030|                           pages it expects you to need, and writes the
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.031|                           prefetch and layout files under
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.032|                           C:\Windows\Prefetch that EnablePrefetcher
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.033|                           points at. This is the shipped value on every
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.034|                           Windows 11 SKU.
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.035|    demand               : Start=3. This is the value that matters most to
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.036|                           understand: nothing demand-starts SysMain.
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.037|                           There is no trigger, no dependency and no COM
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.038|                           activation that wakes it, so Manual is
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.039|                           functionally the same as off - the service
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.040|                           simply never runs, and EnablePrefetcher has
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.041|                           nobody left to act on it.
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.042|    disabled             : Start=4. Same practical outcome as Manual, but
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.043|                           explicit: the Service Control Manager refuses
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.044|                           any start request. The standby list still
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.045|                           exists, it is just no longer pre-populated by
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.046|                           anyone.
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.047|    delayed-auto         : Start=2 plus DelayedAutostart=1. Starts a
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.048|                           couple of minutes after logon instead of during
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.049|                           boot. Nothing in Windows ships SysMain this
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.050|                           way, and it defeats part of the point, since
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.051|                           the boot prefetch work is what it is meant to
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.052|                           be doing early.
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.053|
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.054|  Why these profiles : All five columns write auto because this card is in
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.055|                       the re-assert-defaults block, which exists to write
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.056|                       the shipped value as a safety net on a machine
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.057|                       whose history you do not know. Automatic is the
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.058|                       shipped value on every SKU, so there is nothing to
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.059|                       vary. The one machine where leaving SysMain off is
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.060|                       defensible - an old mechanical-drive laptop where
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.061|                       the post-boot grinding is audible - is a hardware
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.062|                       case, not a profile, and it is handled by answering
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.063|                       skip.
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.064|
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.065|  Target          : OPTY.bat line 1892, :reassert_defaults - sc config
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.066|                    SysMain start= auto followed by sc start SysMain.
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.067|                    Registry equivalent:
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.068|                    HKLM\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Services\SysMain\Start =
::X|EN|rad.sysmain.auto.069|                    2
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.001|  Ce que c est    : SysMain, l ancien Superfetch, assure le prefetch et la
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.002|                    gestion de la liste de veille. C est lui qui donne un
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.003|                    sens à la valeur EnablePrefetcher : sans le service,
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.004|                    cette valeur de registre est inerte.
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.005|
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.006|  Effet reel      : Passe le démarrage en automatique et lance le service
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.007|                    tout de suite, dans le même bloc qui réaffirme le TRIM
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.008|                    et la valeur du préchargeur - les trois morceaux de la
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.009|                    même histoire sont écrits ensemble.
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.010|
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.011|  Gain            : Sur une machine à disque mécanique, lancements
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.012|                    d applications nettement plus rapides. Sur SSD ou
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.013|                    NVMe, l écart est faible et souvent dans le bruit de
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.014|                    mesure : la vraie raison de le laisser tourner, c est
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.015|                    que Windows 11 est conçu et testé avec lui actif, pas
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.016|                    un résultat au chronomètre.
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.017|
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.018|  Cout            : De l activité disque dans les premières minutes après
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.019|                    le démarrage, et une empreinte mémoire visible au
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.020|                    Gestionnaire des tâches sous forme de mémoire en
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.021|                    veille. Cette mémoire est du cache, pas de
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.022|                    l occupation : tout processus qui la réclame la
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.023|                    récupère immédiatement.
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.024|
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.025|  Defaut Windows  : 2 (Automatique), en cours d exécution.
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.026|
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.027|  Valeurs possibles :
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.028|    auto                 : Start=2 et le service est lancé immédiatement.
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.029|                           SysMain se remet à suivre les exécutables que
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.030|                           vous lancez, préremplit la liste de veille avec
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.031|                           les pages qu il pense utiles, et écrit les
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.032|                           fichiers de prefetch et de layout sous
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.033|                           C:\Windows\Prefetch que vise EnablePrefetcher.
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.034|                           C est la valeur livrée sur toutes les éditions
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.035|                           de Windows 11.
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.036|    demand               : Start=3. C est la valeur la plus importante à
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.037|                           comprendre : rien ne démarre SysMain à la
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.038|                           demande. Aucun déclencheur, aucune dépendance,
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.039|                           aucune activation COM ne le réveille : Manuel
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.040|                           équivaut donc à coupé - le service ne tourne
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.041|                           jamais, et EnablePrefetcher n a plus personne
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.042|                           pour l appliquer.
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.043|    disabled             : Start=4. Même résultat pratique que Manuel,
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.044|                           mais explicite : le gestionnaire de services
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.045|                           refuse toute demande de démarrage. La liste de
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.046|                           veille existe toujours, elle n est simplement
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.047|                           plus préremplie par personne.
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.048|    delayed-auto         : Start=2 avec DelayedAutostart=1. Démarre une ou
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.049|                           deux minutes après l ouverture de session au
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.050|                           lieu de pendant le boot. Windows ne livre
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.051|                           jamais SysMain ainsi, et cela va à l encontre
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.052|                           du but : c est justement tôt que le travail de
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.053|                           prefetch de démarrage doit se faire.
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.054|
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.055|  Pourquoi ces profils : Les cinq colonnes écrivent auto parce que cette
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.056|                         carte fait partie du bloc de réaffirmation des
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.057|                         défauts, dont le rôle est d écrire la valeur
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.058|                         d usine comme filet de sécurité sur une machine
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.059|                         dont on ignore l histoire. Automatique est la
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.060|                         valeur livrée sur toutes les éditions : il n y a
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.061|                         rien à faire varier. Le seul cas où laisser
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.062|                         SysMain coupé se défend - un vieux portable à
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.063|                         disque mécanique où l on entend le disque après
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.064|                         le démarrage - est un cas matériel, pas un
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.065|                         profil, et il se traite en répondant passer.
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.066|
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.067|  Cible           : OPTY.bat line 1892, :reassert_defaults - sc config
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.068|                    SysMain start= auto followed by sc start SysMain.
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.069|                    Registry equivalent:
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.070|                    HKLM\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Services\SysMain\Start =
::X|FR|rad.sysmain.auto.071|                    2
::
:: ---- rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled (repair) ---------------------
::P|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled|REPAIR|REPAIR|REPAIR|REPAIR|REPAIR|
::T|EN|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.001|REPAIR WINDOWS UPDATE SERVICES FOUND DISABLED
::T|EN|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.002|Turns eleven Windows Update related services back on wherever they were found fully disabled, fixing stuck downloads and update errors at no real cost.
::T|FR|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.001|REPARER LES SERVICES WINDOWS UPDATE DESACTIVES
::T|FR|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.002|Reactive onze services lies a Windows Update partout ou ils etaient trouves desactives, ce qui corrige les telechargements bloques et les erreurs de mise a jour, sans cout reel.
::X|EN|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.001|  What it is      : Eleven services updates depend on: wuauserv, UsoSvc,
::X|EN|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.002|                    DoSvc, BITS, CryptSvc, TrustedInstaller, msiserver,
::X|EN|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.003|                    InstallService, AppIDSvc, wlidsvc and mpssvc. DoSvc is
::X|EN|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.004|                    the primary downloader on Windows 11; BITS is only the
::X|EN|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.005|                    fallback.
::X|EN|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.006|
::X|EN|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.007|  Actual effect   : Rewrites the start type only for services currently
::X|EN|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.008|                    set to Disabled. Anything at Manual or Automatic is
::X|EN|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.009|                    left exactly as it is - a service you deliberately set
::X|EN|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.010|                    to Manual is not touched, by design.
::X|EN|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.011|
::X|EN|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.012|  Gain            : Fixes error 0x80070426 and downloads stuck at 0
::X|EN|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.013|                    percent - failures that give no readable explanation
::X|EN|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.014|                    and are almost always the residue of a debloat script.
::X|EN|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.015|                    wlidsvc disabled is the classic cause of the first;
::X|EN|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.016|                    mpssvc disabled is the classic cause of the second.
::X|EN|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.017|
::X|EN|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.018|  Cost            : Nothing, this is a pure repair. Disabled is the one
::X|EN|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.019|                    state nothing can demand-start out of, so it is the
::X|EN|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.020|                    only state that is unambiguously broken rather than
::X|EN|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.021|                    merely a preference.
::X|EN|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.022|
::X|EN|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.023|  Windows default : Mostly Manual or Manual (Trigger Start), with CryptSvc
::X|EN|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.024|                    and mpssvc Automatic, and DoSvc and UsoSvc Automatic
::X|EN|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.025|                    (Delayed Start). Each service is repaired to its own
::X|EN|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.026|                    value, not to a blanket Manual.
::X|EN|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.027|
::X|EN|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.028|  Possible values:
::X|EN|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.029|    REPAIR               : For each of the eleven services,
::X|EN|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.030|                           :svcfixifdisabled reads HKLM\SYSTEM\CurrentCont
::X|EN|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.031|                           rolSet\Services\<name>\Start. If the value is
::X|EN|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.032|                           anything other than 4 it does nothing and moves
::X|EN|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.033|                           on. Only a service genuinely set to Disabled is
::X|EN|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.034|                           rewritten, and it is rewritten to its own
::X|EN|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.035|                           shipped value: demand for wuauserv, BITS,
::X|EN|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.036|                           TrustedInstaller, msiserver, InstallService,
::X|EN|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.037|                           AppIDSvc and wlidsvc; auto for CryptSvc and
::X|EN|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.038|                           mpssvc; delayed-auto for DoSvc and UsoSvc.
::X|EN|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.039|    SKIP                 : Leaves every disabled service disabled. Windows
::X|EN|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.040|                           Update keeps failing with 0x80070426 or hanging
::X|EN|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.041|                           at 0 percent, and MSI installers keep failing
::X|EN|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.042|                           for the same reason, with no message that
::X|EN|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.043|                           points at a service.
::X|EN|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.044|
::X|EN|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.045|  Why these profiles : Identical everywhere, and it should be. A disabled
::X|EN|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.046|                       CryptSvc is not a gaming preference and a disabled
::X|EN|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.047|                       mpssvc is not a server preference - both are simply
::X|EN|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.048|                       a machine that cannot patch itself. Even someone
::X|EN|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.049|                       who deliberately avoids Windows Update wants these
::X|EN|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.050|                       back, because the same services carry MSI installs
::X|EN|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.051|                       and the Store.
::X|EN|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.052|
::X|EN|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.053|  Target          : OPTY.bat lines 1988-2007 - call :svcfixifdisabled for
::X|EN|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.054|                    wuauserv BITS TrustedInstaller msiserver
::X|EN|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.055|                    InstallService AppIDSvc wlidsvc (demand), CryptSvc
::X|EN|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.056|                    (auto), mpssvc (auto), DoSvc (delayed-auto), UsoSvc
::X|EN|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.057|                    (delayed-auto)
::X|FR|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.001|  Ce que c est    : Onze services dont dépendent les mises à jour :
::X|FR|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.002|                    wuauserv, UsoSvc, DoSvc, BITS, CryptSvc,
::X|FR|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.003|                    TrustedInstaller, msiserver, InstallService, AppIDSvc,
::X|FR|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.004|                    wlidsvc et mpssvc. DoSvc est le téléchargeur principal
::X|FR|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.005|                    sous Windows 11 ; BITS n est que la solution de repli.
::X|FR|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.006|
::X|FR|rad.wu.services.fixifdisabled.007|  Effet reel      : Ne réécrit le type de démarrage que pour les services
