:: ---- svc.wsearch (preference) ---------------------------------------
::P|svc.wsearch|demand|demand|delayed-auto|delayed-auto|delayed-auto|
::T|EN|svc.wsearch.001|WINDOWS SEARCH INDEXER: AUTOMATIC (DELAYED)
::T|EN|svc.wsearch.002|Keeps the Windows Search indexer running so Explorer, Start menu and Outlook search stay accurate and current, at the cost of some background disk and CPU use after login.
::T|FR|svc.wsearch.001|INDEXEUR DE RECHERCHE WINDOWS : AUTOMATIQUE (DIFFERE)
::T|FR|svc.wsearch.002|Garde l indexeur de recherche Windows actif pour que la recherche dans l Explorateur, le menu Demarrer et Outlook reste exacte et a jour, au prix d un peu de disque et de CPU en fond apres l ouverture de session.
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.001|  What it is      : WSearch runs SearchIndexer.exe, which builds the
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.002|                    content index behind Explorer search, file results in
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.003|                    the Start menu, and Outlook instant search. The index
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.004|                    lives in C:\ProgramData\Microsoft\Search and grows to
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.005|                    a few hundred MB on a normal machine.
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.006|
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.007|  Actual effect   : sc config WSearch start= delayed-auto is the shipped
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.008|                    configuration: the indexer starts on its own a minute
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.009|                    or two after logon and keeps the index current instead
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.010|                    of waiting to be woken. start= demand leaves it to
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.011|                    whatever demand-starts it.
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.012|
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.013|  Gain            : Predictable, up-to-date indexing. Important
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.014|                    correction: on this machine WSearch at Manual was
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.015|                    still RUNNING with SearchIndexer.exe alive and search
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.016|                    working, so 'Manual kills Start menu search' is false.
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.017|                    The gain is indexing reliability, not search existing
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.018|                    at all.
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.019|
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.020|  Cost            : Background indexing I/O and CPU after logon, and an
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.021|                    index file that grows to a few hundred MB. On a laptop
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.022|                    the first full index build is the one time it
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.023|                    noticeably costs battery; after that it is
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.024|                    incremental. Nothing breaks either way.
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.025|
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.026|  Windows default : 2 with DelayedAutostart=1 (Automatic, Delayed Start).
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.027|
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.028|  Possible values:
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.029|    delayed-auto         : Start=2 with DelayedAutostart=1, the shipped
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.030|                           configuration. SearchIndexer.exe comes up on
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.031|                           its own a minute or two after logon, outside
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.032|                           the boot rush, and then keeps the index in
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.033|                           C:\ProgramData\Microsoft\Search current as
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.034|                           files change. Content search, Outlook instant
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.035|                           search and file results in the Start menu are
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.036|                           all served from that index.
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.037|    demand               : Start=3. Tested live on this machine: WSearch
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.038|                           at Manual was still RUNNING, SearchIndexer.exe
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.039|                           was alive and search worked, so 'Manual kills
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.040|                           Start menu search' is false. Something demand-
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.041|                           starts it. What you lose is the guarantee:
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.042|                           indexing happens when something wakes the
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.043|                           service rather than continuously, so a freshly
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.044|                           written file can take longer to appear in
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.045|                           results.
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.046|    auto                 : Start=2 without the delayed flag. Same
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.047|                           behaviour as delayed-auto except the indexer
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.048|                           starts during boot instead of after it,
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.049|                           competing with everything else for disk. There
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.050|                           is no upside over delayed-auto, which is why
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.051|                           Windows ships the delayed form.
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.052|    disabled             : Start=4. This one really does stop indexing:
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.053|                           nothing can start the service, the index goes
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.054|                           stale and content search returns nothing.
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.055|                           Explorer still finds files by name because that
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.056|                           path does not need the index. Not recommended -
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.057|                           demand gives you the light machine without the
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.058|                           dead end.
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.059|
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.060|  Why these profiles : The split is by workload, not by folklore. Office
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.061|                       and laptop index because those are the machines
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.062|                       that search inside documents and mail, and that is
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.063|                       the only thing the index buys you. Gaming and
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.064|                       server sit at Manual because nobody greps a Steam
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.065|                       library or a Plex share by content, and Manual was
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.066|                       verified not to break search on this very machine.
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.067|                       WINDOWS keeps the shipped delayed-auto. Note that
::X|EN|svc.wsearch.068|                       web results in the Start menu are a different knob
