:: ---- svc.themes (repair) ----------------------------------------
::P|svc.themes|auto|auto|auto|auto|auto|
::T|EN|svc.themes.001|THEMES SERVICE: AUTOMATIC
::T|EN|svc.themes.002|Keeps the Themes service running so Windows 11 actually looks like Windows 11 instead of a plain classic style; costs nothing and never touches in-game rendering.
::T|FR|svc.themes.001|SERVICE THEMES : AUTOMATIQUE
::T|FR|svc.themes.002|Garde le service Themes actif pour que Windows 11 ressemble vraiment a Windows 11 au lieu de l aspect classique sans style ; cela ne coute rien et ne touche jamais au rendu en jeu.
::X|EN|svc.themes.001|  What it is      : Themes applies visual styles: accent colour, dark
::X|EN|svc.themes.002|                    mode, rounded window frames, wallpaper themes. It is
::X|EN|svc.themes.003|                    the service that makes Windows 11 look like Windows
::X|EN|svc.themes.004|                    11.
::X|EN|svc.themes.005|
::X|EN|svc.themes.006|  Actual effect   : sc config Themes start= auto. Without it running,
::X|EN|svc.themes.007|                    Windows falls back to an unstyled classic look at
::X|EN|svc.themes.008|                    every logon.
::X|EN|svc.themes.009|
::X|EN|svc.themes.010|  Gain            : The interface looks like Windows 11 instead of Windows
::X|EN|svc.themes.011|                    2000. That is the entire effect - and stating it
::X|EN|svc.themes.012|                    plainly is more useful than pretending there is a
::X|EN|svc.themes.013|                    performance angle.
::X|EN|svc.themes.014|
::X|EN|svc.themes.015|  Cost            : None. 'Disable Themes for performance' is XP-era
::X|EN|svc.themes.016|                    advice; on modern hardware the cost of the service is
::X|EN|svc.themes.017|                    not measurable, and it does not touch in-game
::X|EN|svc.themes.018|                    rendering at all, because a fullscreen game does not
::X|EN|svc.themes.019|                    go through the desktop compositor's visual styles.
::X|EN|svc.themes.020|
::X|EN|svc.themes.021|  Windows default : 2 (Automatic).
::X|EN|svc.themes.022|
::X|EN|svc.themes.023|  Possible values:
::X|EN|svc.themes.024|    auto                 : Start=2, the shipped value. The Themes service
::X|EN|svc.themes.025|                           is up before the shell, so uxtheme has a visual
::X|EN|svc.themes.026|                           style to apply: accent colour, light or dark
::X|EN|svc.themes.027|                           mode, rounded window corners, wallpaper themes
::X|EN|svc.themes.028|                           and the whole Windows 11 look.
::X|EN|svc.themes.029|    demand               : Start=3. Nothing demand-starts Themes early
::X|EN|svc.themes.030|                           enough to matter: the shell asks for the visual
::X|EN|svc.themes.031|                           style at logon, and if the service is not
::X|EN|svc.themes.032|                           already up, Windows falls back to the unstyled
::X|EN|svc.themes.033|                           classic appearance for that session. Manual is
::X|EN|svc.themes.034|                           therefore not a lighter version of Automatic,
::X|EN|svc.themes.035|                           it is the classic look with extra steps.
::X|EN|svc.themes.036|    disabled             : Start=4. The classic unstyled look at every
::X|EN|svc.themes.037|                           logon, permanently. Nothing else changes -
::X|EN|svc.themes.038|                           applications still run, in-game rendering is
::X|EN|svc.themes.039|                           untouched - but the desktop looks like Windows
::X|EN|svc.themes.040|                           2000.
::X|EN|svc.themes.041|    delayed-auto         : Start=2 with DelayedAutostart=1. The worst of
::X|EN|svc.themes.042|                           both: the desktop draws unstyled first and then
::X|EN|svc.themes.043|                           restyles a minute later, which looks like a
::X|EN|svc.themes.044|                           fault. Nobody wants this value.
::X|EN|svc.themes.045|
::X|EN|svc.themes.046|  Why these profiles : All five identical. There is no use case in which
::X|EN|svc.themes.047|                       the classic look is faster - the claim never had a
