:: ---- svc.audioendpointbuilder (repair) --------------------------
::P|svc.audioendpointbuilder|auto|auto|auto|auto|auto|
::T|EN|svc.audioendpointbuilder.001|AUDIO DEVICE DETECTION: AUTOMATIC
::T|EN|svc.audioendpointbuilder.002|Keeps the service that detects your speakers, headset and microphone running, since Windows Audio itself cannot start without it, and it costs nothing while idle.
::T|FR|svc.audioendpointbuilder.001|DETECTION DES PERIPHERIQUES AUDIO : AUTOMATIQUE
::T|FR|svc.audioendpointbuilder.002|Garde actif le service qui detecte vos haut-parleurs, casque et microphone, car Windows Audio lui meme ne peut pas demarrer sans lui, et cela ne coute rien au repos.
::X|EN|svc.audioendpointbuilder.001|  What it is      : The service that enumerates your playback and
::X|EN|svc.audioendpointbuilder.002|                    recording devices and keeps that list current as
::X|EN|svc.audioendpointbuilder.003|                    hardware comes and goes.
::X|EN|svc.audioendpointbuilder.004|
::X|EN|svc.audioendpointbuilder.005|  Actual effect   : sc config AudioEndpointBuilder start= auto, the
::X|EN|svc.audioendpointbuilder.006|                    shipped value.
::X|EN|svc.audioendpointbuilder.007|
::X|EN|svc.audioendpointbuilder.008|  Gain            : Without it you get no sound devices at all - the
::X|EN|svc.audioendpointbuilder.009|                    speaker icon shows a red cross and nothing can be
::X|EN|svc.audioendpointbuilder.010|                    selected. Windows Audio itself cannot start, because
::X|EN|svc.audioendpointbuilder.011|                    it declares a dependency on this service.
::X|EN|svc.audioendpointbuilder.012|
