:: ---- svc.audiosrv (repair) --------------------------------------
::P|svc.audiosrv|auto|auto|auto|auto|auto|
::T|EN|svc.audiosrv.001|WINDOWS AUDIO SERVICE: AUTOMATIC
::T|EN|svc.audiosrv.002|Keeps Windows Audio running so every application actually has sound; with it off, there is no audio anywhere and the cause is not obvious.
::T|FR|svc.audiosrv.001|SERVICE AUDIO WINDOWS : AUTOMATIQUE
::T|FR|svc.audiosrv.002|Garde Windows Audio actif pour que toutes les applications aient vraiment du son ; coupe, il n y a plus aucun audio nulle part, et la cause ne saute pas aux yeux.
::X|EN|svc.audiosrv.001|  What it is      : Windows Audio, the service that actually mixes and
::X|EN|svc.audiosrv.002|                    plays sound for every application on the machine.
::X|EN|svc.audiosrv.003|
::X|EN|svc.audiosrv.004|  Actual effect   : sc config Audiosrv start= auto, the shipped value. It
::X|EN|svc.audiosrv.005|                    also brings AudioEndpointBuilder up through its
::X|EN|svc.audiosrv.006|                    dependency.
::X|EN|svc.audiosrv.007|
::X|EN|svc.audiosrv.008|  Gain            : Sound works. With it disabled there is no audio
::X|EN|svc.audiosrv.009|                    anywhere, in any application, and the cause is not
::X|EN|svc.audiosrv.010|                    obvious from the symptom.
::X|EN|svc.audiosrv.011|
::X|EN|svc.audiosrv.012|  Cost            : None. It is a prerequisite, and it consumes CPU only
::X|EN|svc.audiosrv.013|                    in proportion to the audio actually being played.
::X|EN|svc.audiosrv.014|
::X|EN|svc.audiosrv.015|  Windows default : 2 (Automatic).
::X|EN|svc.audiosrv.016|
::X|EN|svc.audiosrv.017|  Possible values:
::X|EN|svc.audiosrv.018|    auto                 : Start=2, the shipped value. Windows Audio runs
::X|EN|svc.audiosrv.019|                           from boot in an audiodg-backed session, mixes
::X|EN|svc.audiosrv.020|                           every application's streams, applies the per-
::X|EN|svc.audiosrv.021|                           device volume and effects, and hands the result
::X|EN|svc.audiosrv.022|                           to the driver. It also pulls
::X|EN|svc.audiosrv.023|                           AudioEndpointBuilder up as a dependency.
::X|EN|svc.audiosrv.024|    demand               : Start=3. Audiosrv has trigger-start conditions
::X|EN|svc.audiosrv.025|                           tied to audio device arrival, so it may come up
::X|EN|svc.audiosrv.026|                           anyway - but the first sound of a session can
::X|EN|svc.audiosrv.027|                           be lost while the service starts, and any
::X|EN|svc.audiosrv.028|                           application that queries the audio session
::X|EN|svc.audiosrv.029|                           before it is up gets an error rather than
