::X|EN|svc.audiosrv.031|    disabled             : Start=4. There is no audio anywhere, in any
::X|EN|svc.audiosrv.032|                           application, and the volume icon carries a red
::X|EN|svc.audiosrv.033|                           cross. Nothing else on the machine is affected
::X|EN|svc.audiosrv.034|                           - it is a clean, total loss of sound.
::X|EN|svc.audiosrv.035|    delayed-auto         : Start=2 with DelayedAutostart=1. Audio arrives
::X|EN|svc.audiosrv.036|                           a minute or so into the session. There is no
::X|EN|svc.audiosrv.037|                           reason to want this; the service is cheap and
::X|EN|svc.audiosrv.038|                           its whole job is to be there before the first
::X|EN|svc.audiosrv.039|                           sound.
::X|EN|svc.audiosrv.040|
::X|EN|svc.audiosrv.041|  Why these profiles : All five identical. There is no such thing as a
::X|EN|svc.audiosrv.042|                       machine that benefits from disabling audio, and on
