:: ---- svc.securityhealthservice (repair) -------------------------
::P|svc.securityhealthservice|demand|demand|demand|demand|demand|
::T|EN|svc.securityhealthservice.001|Windows Security health service: keep it on Manual
::T|EN|svc.securityhealthservice.002|This only reports whether antivirus and firewall are on, it is not the antivirus itself; Manual is the default, and disabling it just blinds the status page for no real gain.
::T|FR|svc.securityhealthservice.001|Service d état de Sécurité Windows : le garder en Manuel
::T|FR|svc.securityhealthservice.002|Il se contente de signaler si l antivirus et le pare-feu sont actifs, ce n est pas l antivirus lui-même ; Manuel est la valeur d usine, et le désactiver rend juste la page d état aveugle sans aucun gain réel.
::X|EN|svc.securityhealthservice.001|  What it is      : The Windows Security health agent: the shield icon,
::X|EN|svc.securityhealthservice.002|                    the protection status page, and the reporting that
::X|EN|svc.securityhealthservice.003|                    says whether antivirus, firewall and SmartScreen are
::X|EN|svc.securityhealthservice.004|                    on.
::X|EN|svc.securityhealthservice.005|
::X|EN|svc.securityhealthservice.006|  Actual effect   : sc config SecurityHealthService start= demand. Windows
::X|EN|svc.securityhealthservice.007|                    can start it to evaluate and report protection status,
::X|EN|svc.securityhealthservice.008|                    and it stops again afterwards.
::X|EN|svc.securityhealthservice.009|
::X|EN|svc.securityhealthservice.010|  Gain            : Windows Security reports honest status instead of
::X|EN|svc.securityhealthservice.011|                    stale or empty panels. If you run a third-party
::X|EN|svc.securityhealthservice.012|                    antivirus, this is also what registers it correctly so
::X|EN|svc.securityhealthservice.013|                    Defender knows to stand down.
::X|EN|svc.securityhealthservice.014|
::X|EN|svc.securityhealthservice.015|  Cost            : None; Manual is what Windows ships. It is not the
::X|EN|svc.securityhealthservice.016|                    antivirus engine itself - disabling it does not make
::X|EN|svc.securityhealthservice.017|                    Defender faster, it just blinds the status page.
::X|EN|svc.securityhealthservice.018|
::X|EN|svc.securityhealthservice.019|  Windows default : 3 (Manual), confirmed on a live 25H2 install.
::X|EN|svc.securityhealthservice.020|
::X|EN|svc.securityhealthservice.021|  Possible values:
::X|EN|svc.securityhealthservice.022|    demand               : Start=3, the shipped value. Windows starts the
::X|EN|svc.securityhealthservice.023|                           health agent when it needs to evaluate
::X|EN|svc.securityhealthservice.024|                           protection status: when you open the Windows
::X|EN|svc.securityhealthservice.025|                           Security app, when the tray icon refreshes, or
::X|EN|svc.securityhealthservice.026|                           when the Security Center evaluates whether
::X|EN|svc.securityhealthservice.027|                           antivirus, firewall and SmartScreen are on. It
::X|EN|svc.securityhealthservice.028|                           also registers a third-party antivirus so
::X|EN|svc.securityhealthservice.029|                           Defender steps aside correctly.
::X|EN|svc.securityhealthservice.030|    disabled             : Start=4. The Windows Security app shows stale
::X|EN|svc.securityhealthservice.031|                           or empty panels and the shield icon stops
::X|EN|svc.securityhealthservice.032|                           reflecting reality. Note what does NOT change:
::X|EN|svc.securityhealthservice.033|                           Defender's engine, real-time protection and the
::X|EN|svc.securityhealthservice.034|                           firewall all keep running. You have not turned
::X|EN|svc.securityhealthservice.035|                           off protection, you have turned off your
::X|EN|svc.securityhealthservice.036|                           ability to see whether it is on - which is
::X|EN|svc.securityhealthservice.037|                           worse, not better.
::X|EN|svc.securityhealthservice.038|    auto                 : Start=2. Resident all the time. It works, it
::X|EN|svc.securityhealthservice.039|                           just costs memory for something Windows is
::X|EN|svc.securityhealthservice.040|                           perfectly able to start when it needs it.
::X|EN|svc.securityhealthservice.041|    delayed-auto         : Start=2 with DelayedAutostart=1. Same objection
::X|EN|svc.securityhealthservice.042|                           as auto.
::X|EN|svc.securityhealthservice.043|
::X|EN|svc.securityhealthservice.044|  Why these profiles : All five identical. Disabling this is a tweak with
::X|EN|svc.securityhealthservice.045|                       no upside at all: it saves nothing measurable and
::X|EN|svc.securityhealthservice.046|                       costs you the only honest report you have about
::X|EN|svc.securityhealthservice.047|                       whether the machine is protected. That is as true
::X|EN|svc.securityhealthservice.048|                       on a gaming rig as on an office PC, and a headless
::X|EN|svc.securityhealthservice.049|                       server is the one you most need to be able to query
::X|EN|svc.securityhealthservice.050|                       remotely.
::X|EN|svc.securityhealthservice.051|
::X|EN|svc.securityhealthservice.052|  Target          : sc config SecurityHealthService start= demand.
::X|EN|svc.securityhealthservice.053|                    Registry: HKLM\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Services\Secur
::X|EN|svc.securityhealthservice.054|                    ityHealthService\Start = 3
::X|FR|svc.securityhealthservice.001|  Ce que c est    : L agent d état de Sécurité Windows : l icône bouclier,
::X|FR|svc.securityhealthservice.002|                    la page d état de protection, et le compte rendu qui
::X|FR|svc.securityhealthservice.003|                    dit si l antivirus, le pare-feu et SmartScreen sont
::X|FR|svc.securityhealthservice.004|                    actifs.
::X|FR|svc.securityhealthservice.005|
::X|FR|svc.securityhealthservice.006|  Effet reel      : sc config SecurityHealthService start= demand. Windows
::X|FR|svc.securityhealthservice.007|                    peut le démarrer pour évaluer et rapporter l état de
::X|FR|svc.securityhealthservice.008|                    protection, et il s arrête ensuite.
::X|FR|svc.securityhealthservice.009|
::X|FR|svc.securityhealthservice.010|  Gain            : Sécurité Windows affiche un état honnête au lieu de
::X|FR|svc.securityhealthservice.011|                    panneaux périmés ou vides. Si vous utilisez un
::X|FR|svc.securityhealthservice.012|                    antivirus tiers, c est aussi lui qui l enregistre
::X|FR|svc.securityhealthservice.013|                    correctement pour que Defender sache s effacer.
::X|FR|svc.securityhealthservice.014|
::X|FR|svc.securityhealthservice.015|  Cout            : Aucun, Manuel est la valeur d usine. Ce n est pas le
::X|FR|svc.securityhealthservice.016|                    moteur antivirus : le désactiver ne rend pas Defender
::X|FR|svc.securityhealthservice.017|                    plus rapide, cela rend juste la page d état aveugle.
::X|FR|svc.securityhealthservice.018|
::X|FR|svc.securityhealthservice.019|  Defaut Windows  : 3 (Manuel), confirmé sur une installation 25H2 réelle.
::X|FR|svc.securityhealthservice.020|
::X|FR|svc.securityhealthservice.021|  Valeurs possibles :
::X|FR|svc.securityhealthservice.022|    demand               : Start=3, la valeur d usine. Windows démarre
::X|FR|svc.securityhealthservice.023|                           l agent d état quand il doit évaluer la
::X|FR|svc.securityhealthservice.024|                           protection : à l ouverture de l application
::X|FR|svc.securityhealthservice.025|                           Sécurité Windows, au rafraîchissement de
::X|FR|svc.securityhealthservice.026|                           l icône de la barre d état, ou quand le Centre
::X|FR|svc.securityhealthservice.027|                           de sécurité vérifie si l antivirus, le pare-feu
::X|FR|svc.securityhealthservice.028|                           et SmartScreen sont actifs. C est aussi lui qui
::X|FR|svc.securityhealthservice.029|                           enregistre un antivirus tiers pour que Defender
::X|FR|svc.securityhealthservice.030|                           s efface correctement.
::X|FR|svc.securityhealthservice.031|    disabled             : Start=4. L application Sécurité Windows affiche
::X|FR|svc.securityhealthservice.032|                           des panneaux périmés ou vides et l icône
::X|FR|svc.securityhealthservice.033|                           bouclier cesse de refléter la réalité. Ce qui
::X|FR|svc.securityhealthservice.034|                           NE change PAS : le moteur de Defender, la
::X|FR|svc.securityhealthservice.035|                           protection en temps réel et le pare-feu
::X|FR|svc.securityhealthservice.036|                           continuent de tourner. Vous n avez pas coupé la
::X|FR|svc.securityhealthservice.037|                           protection, vous avez coupé votre capacité à
::X|FR|svc.securityhealthservice.038|                           savoir si elle est active - ce qui est pire,
::X|FR|svc.securityhealthservice.039|                           pas mieux.
::X|FR|svc.securityhealthservice.040|    auto                 : Start=2. Résident en permanence. Cela
::X|FR|svc.securityhealthservice.041|                           fonctionne, mais coûte de la mémoire pour
::X|FR|svc.securityhealthservice.042|                           quelque chose que Windows sait parfaitement
::X|FR|svc.securityhealthservice.043|                           démarrer au moment voulu.
::X|FR|svc.securityhealthservice.044|    delayed-auto         : Start=2 avec DelayedAutostart=1. Même objection
::X|FR|svc.securityhealthservice.045|                           qu auto.
::X|FR|svc.securityhealthservice.046|
::X|FR|svc.securityhealthservice.047|  Pourquoi ces profils : Les cinq colonnes identiques. Le désactiver est
::X|FR|svc.securityhealthservice.048|                         une bidouille sans le moindre avantage : on
::X|FR|svc.securityhealthservice.049|                         n économise rien de mesurable et on perd le seul
::X|FR|svc.securityhealthservice.050|                         compte rendu honnête dont on dispose sur l état
::X|FR|svc.securityhealthservice.051|                         de protection de la machine. C est aussi vrai sur
::X|FR|svc.securityhealthservice.052|                         une machine de jeu que sur un poste de bureau, et
::X|FR|svc.securityhealthservice.053|                         un serveur sans écran est justement celui qu on
::X|FR|svc.securityhealthservice.054|                         veut pouvoir interroger à distance.
::X|FR|svc.securityhealthservice.055|
::X|FR|svc.securityhealthservice.056|  Cible           : sc config SecurityHealthService start= demand.
::X|FR|svc.securityhealthservice.057|                    Registry: HKLM\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Services\Secur
::X|FR|svc.securityhealthservice.058|                    ityHealthService\Start = 3
