:: ---- rp.point.create (preference) -----------------------------------
::P|rp.point.create|APPLY|APPLY|APPLY|APPLY|SKIP|
::T|EN|rp.point.create.001|Create a system restore point before changes
::T|EN|rp.point.create.002|This snapshots your registry and system files so you can roll back if a change goes wrong, at the cost of a little disk space and under a minute; it does not back up your documents.
::T|FR|rp.point.create.001|Créer un point de restauration avant les modifications
::T|FR|rp.point.create.002|Cela fige le registre et les fichiers système pour pouvoir revenir en arrière si un changement tourne mal, au prix d un peu d espace disque et de moins d une minute ; ce n est pas une sauvegarde de vos documents.
::X|EN|rp.point.create.001|  What it is      : Before anything destructive runs, OPTY calls
::X|EN|rp.point.create.002|                    :restore_point once per session. It turns System
::X|EN|rp.point.create.003|                    Protection on for the system drive if it was off,
::X|EN|rp.point.create.004|                    briefly sets SystemRestorePointCreationFrequency to 0
::X|EN|rp.point.create.005|                    so Windows cannot refuse a second point inside 24
::X|EN|rp.point.create.006|                    hours, takes one point named after the OPTY version,
::X|EN|rp.point.create.007|                    then writes 1440 back.
::X|EN|rp.point.create.008|
::X|EN|rp.point.create.009|  Actual effect   : A restore point snapshots the registry hives and
::X|EN|rp.point.create.010|                    protected system files through VSS. It does not
::X|EN|rp.point.create.011|                    snapshot your documents, so it is not a backup. The
::X|EN|rp.point.create.012|                    throttle is put back to the Windows default straight
::X|EN|rp.point.create.013|                    afterwards, so OPTY does not leave System Protection
::X|EN|rp.point.create.014|                    permanently altered.
::X|EN|rp.point.create.015|
::X|EN|rp.point.create.016|  Gain            : If a registry write in menu 2 turns out badly on your
::X|EN|rp.point.create.017|                    particular machine, you can roll back from System
::X|EN|rp.point.create.018|                    Restore or from the recovery environment. It is the
::X|EN|rp.point.create.019|                    only undo the script has.
::X|EN|rp.point.create.020|
::X|EN|rp.point.create.021|  Cost            : Shadow-copy storage on C:, typically a few hundred MB
::X|EN|rp.point.create.022|                    to a couple of GB, with Windows deleting the OLDEST
::X|EN|rp.point.create.023|                    point when its quota fills. Plus 10 to 60 seconds. If
::X|EN|rp.point.create.024|                    System Protection was deliberately off, OPTY turns it
::X|EN|rp.point.create.025|                    on and never turns it back off - that part is
::X|EN|rp.point.create.026|                    permanent.
::X|EN|rp.point.create.027|
::X|EN|rp.point.create.028|  Windows default : A clean Windows 11 install ships System Protection OFF
::X|EN|rp.point.create.029|                    for the system drive, and Windows only ever takes
::X|EN|rp.point.create.030|                    points on its own schedule, never on demand. Many OEM
::X|EN|rp.point.create.031|                    images ship it on.
::X|EN|rp.point.create.032|
::X|EN|rp.point.create.033|  Possible values:
::X|EN|rp.point.create.034|    APPLY                : System Protection is switched on for the system
::X|EN|rp.point.create.035|                           drive if it was off, the 24-hour throttle is
::X|EN|rp.point.create.036|                           lifted for the few seconds around the call, one
::X|EN|rp.point.create.037|                           restore point is written, and the throttle is
::X|EN|rp.point.create.038|                           put back to 1440 minutes. Protection stays on
::X|EN|rp.point.create.039|                           afterwards.
::X|EN|rp.point.create.040|    SKIP                 : Nothing is enabled and no point is taken. The
::X|EN|rp.point.create.041|                           machine keeps exactly the System Protection
::X|EN|rp.point.create.042|                           state it had, and the registry writes that
::X|EN|rp.point.create.043|                           follow have no rollback other than a manual
::X|EN|rp.point.create.044|                           undo.
::X|EN|rp.point.create.045|
::X|EN|rp.point.create.046|  Why these profiles : Four profiles agree because a safety net does not
::X|EN|rp.point.create.047|                       depend on what the machine is for. The WINDOWS
::X|EN|rp.point.create.048|                       profile is the only one that skips, and for one
::X|EN|rp.point.create.049|                       mechanical reason: enabling System Protection is a
::X|EN|rp.point.create.050|                       persistent configuration change, and that profile
::X|EN|rp.point.create.051|                       exists to leave the shipped state alone. If your
::X|EN|rp.point.create.052|                       image already has protection on, answering yes
::X|EN|rp.point.create.053|                       under any profile costs you a minute and some
::X|EN|rp.point.create.054|                       shadow storage.
::X|EN|rp.point.create.055|
::X|EN|rp.point.create.056|  Unverified      : Whether System Protection ships on or off differs
::X|EN|rp.point.create.057|                    between a clean Windows 11 install and OEM images.
::X|EN|rp.point.create.058|                    OPTY enables it and never turns it back off - only the
::X|EN|rp.point.create.059|                    creation-frequency throttle is restored.
::X|EN|rp.point.create.060|
::X|EN|rp.point.create.061|  Target          : :restore_point, OPTY.bat 3990-4014 - powershell
::X|EN|rp.point.create.062|                    Enable-ComputerRestore -Drive '%SystemDrive%\', then
::X|EN|rp.point.create.063|                    reg add HKLM\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows
::X|EN|rp.point.create.064|                    NT\CurrentVersion\SystemRestore /v
::X|EN|rp.point.create.065|                    SystemRestorePointCreationFrequency /t REG_DWORD /d 0,
::X|EN|rp.point.create.066|                    then Checkpoint-Computer -Description 'OPTY
::X|EN|rp.point.create.067|                    v%current_version% - before optimization'
::X|EN|rp.point.create.068|                    -RestorePointType MODIFY_SETTINGS, then the frequency
::X|EN|rp.point.create.069|                    written back to 1440. Guarded by RP_DONE, so once per
::X|EN|rp.point.create.070|                    session.
::X|FR|rp.point.create.001|  Ce que c est    : Avant toute operation destructive, OPTY appelle
::X|FR|rp.point.create.002|                    :restore_point une fois par session. Il active la
::X|FR|rp.point.create.003|                    protection du systeme sur le disque systeme si elle
::X|FR|rp.point.create.004|                    etait coupee, met brievement
::X|FR|rp.point.create.005|                    SystemRestorePointCreationFrequency a 0 pour que
::X|FR|rp.point.create.006|                    Windows ne refuse pas un second point dans les 24
::X|FR|rp.point.create.007|                    heures, cree un point nomme d apres la version d OPTY,
::X|FR|rp.point.create.008|                    puis reecrit 1440.
::X|FR|rp.point.create.009|
::X|FR|rp.point.create.010|  Effet reel      : Un point de restauration fige les ruches de registre
::X|FR|rp.point.create.011|                    et les fichiers systeme proteges via VSS. Il ne fige
::X|FR|rp.point.create.012|                    pas vos documents : ce n est donc pas une sauvegarde.
::X|FR|rp.point.create.013|                    Le verrou est remis a la valeur Windows juste apres,
::X|FR|rp.point.create.014|                    OPTY ne laisse donc pas la protection du systeme
::X|FR|rp.point.create.015|                    modifiee derriere lui.
::X|FR|rp.point.create.016|
::X|FR|rp.point.create.017|  Gain            : Si une ecriture registre du menu 2 se passe mal sur
::X|FR|rp.point.create.018|                    votre machine, vous pouvez revenir en arriere depuis
::X|FR|rp.point.create.019|                    la restauration du systeme ou depuis l environnement
::X|FR|rp.point.create.020|                    de recuperation. C est la seule annulation dont
::X|FR|rp.point.create.021|                    dispose le script.
::X|FR|rp.point.create.022|
::X|FR|rp.point.create.023|  Cout            : De l espace de cliches instantanes sur C:, souvent
::X|FR|rp.point.create.024|                    quelques centaines de Mo a deux Go, Windows supprimant
::X|FR|rp.point.create.025|                    le point LE PLUS ANCIEN quand son quota est plein.
::X|FR|rp.point.create.026|                    Plus 10 a 60 secondes. Si la protection du systeme
::X|FR|rp.point.create.027|                    etait volontairement coupee, OPTY l active et ne la
::X|FR|rp.point.create.028|                    recoupe jamais : cette partie-la est definitive.
::X|FR|rp.point.create.029|
::X|FR|rp.point.create.030|  Defaut Windows  : Sur une installation propre de Windows 11, la
::X|FR|rp.point.create.031|                    protection du systeme est DESACTIVEE pour le disque
::X|FR|rp.point.create.032|                    systeme, et Windows ne cree des points que selon son
::X|FR|rp.point.create.033|                    propre calendrier, jamais a la demande. Beaucoup
::X|FR|rp.point.create.034|                    d images constructeur la livrent activee.
::X|FR|rp.point.create.035|
::X|FR|rp.point.create.036|  Valeurs possibles :
::X|FR|rp.point.create.037|    APPLY                : La protection du systeme est activee sur le
::X|FR|rp.point.create.038|                           disque systeme si elle etait coupee, le verrou
::X|FR|rp.point.create.039|                           des 24 heures est leve le temps de l appel, un
::X|FR|rp.point.create.040|                           point de restauration est ecrit, puis le verrou
::X|FR|rp.point.create.041|                           est remis a 1440 minutes. La protection reste
::X|FR|rp.point.create.042|                           active ensuite.
::X|FR|rp.point.create.043|    SKIP                 : Rien n est active et aucun point n est pris. La
::X|FR|rp.point.create.044|                           machine garde exactement l etat de protection
::X|FR|rp.point.create.045|                           qu elle avait, et les ecritures registre qui
::X|FR|rp.point.create.046|                           suivent n ont pas d annulation en un clic.
::X|FR|rp.point.create.047|
::X|FR|rp.point.create.048|  Pourquoi ces profils : Quatre profils sont identiques parce qu un filet
::X|FR|rp.point.create.049|                         de securite ne depend pas de l usage de la
::X|FR|rp.point.create.050|                         machine. Seul le profil WINDOWS passe son tour,
::X|FR|rp.point.create.051|                         pour une raison mecanique : activer la protection
::X|FR|rp.point.create.052|                         du systeme est un changement de configuration
