:: ---- crash.dumps (risky) ---------------------------------------
::P|crash.dumps|DELETE|DELETE|DELETE|DELETE|KEEP|
::T|EN|crash.dumps.001|Delete blue-screen crash dump files
::T|EN|crash.dumps.002|These files are the only record of what caused past blue screens; deleting them only frees disk space, usually not much, and gives up any chance of diagnosing those crashes later.
::T|FR|crash.dumps.001|Supprimer les fichiers de plantage (écran bleu)
::T|FR|crash.dumps.002|Ce sont les seules traces de ce qui a causé vos écrans bleus ; les supprimer ne libère que de l espace disque, souvent peu, et vous prive de toute chance de diagnostiquer ces plantages plus tard.
::X|EN|crash.dumps.001|  What it is      : Every time Windows blue-screens it writes a small dump
::X|EN|crash.dumps.002|                    into C:\Windows\Minidump and, depending on your crash-
::X|EN|crash.dumps.003|                    dump setting, a C:\Windows\MEMORY.DMP. These are the
::X|EN|crash.dumps.004|                    only record of what actually crashed.
::X|EN|crash.dumps.005|
::X|EN|crash.dumps.006|  Actual effect   : Deletes both. Nothing about how Windows writes future
::X|EN|crash.dumps.007|                    dumps is changed, and MEMORY.DMP still needs a
::X|EN|crash.dumps.008|                    pagefile on the system drive to be written at all.
::X|EN|crash.dumps.009|
::X|EN|crash.dumps.010|  Gain            : Space only. Minidumps are a few hundred KB each.
::X|EN|crash.dumps.011|                    MEMORY.DMP is written as an Automatic memory dump on a
::X|EN|crash.dumps.012|                    stock Windows 11, which means kernel memory only -
::X|EN|crash.dumps.013|                    usually a few hundred MB to about 2 GB, NOT the size
::X|EN|crash.dumps.014|                    of your RAM. It only approaches installed RAM if you
::X|EN|crash.dumps.015|                    deliberately picked 'Complete memory dump' in Advanced
::X|EN|crash.dumps.016|                    system settings. Check the file size before deciding
::X|EN|crash.dumps.017|                    this is worth it.
::X|EN|crash.dumps.018|
::X|EN|crash.dumps.019|  Cost            : You permanently destroy the evidence of every past
::X|EN|crash.dumps.020|                    blue screen and GPU driver crash. If you or anyone
::X|EN|crash.dumps.021|                    helping you later wants to know which driver is
::X|EN|crash.dumps.022|                    killing the machine, that answer is gone. And
::X|EN|crash.dumps.023|                    MEMORY.DMP only exists if you have already crashed,
::X|EN|crash.dumps.024|                    which is exactly when it is worth keeping.
::X|EN|crash.dumps.025|
::X|EN|crash.dumps.026|  Windows default : Not applicable. Windows writes these on every bugcheck
::X|EN|crash.dumps.027|                    and keeps them until something deletes them.
::X|EN|crash.dumps.028|
::X|EN|crash.dumps.029|  Possible values:
::X|EN|crash.dumps.030|    DELETE               : Both C:\Windows\Minidump\* and
::X|EN|crash.dumps.031|                           C:\Windows\MEMORY.DMP are removed. Nothing
::X|EN|crash.dumps.032|                           about how Windows writes the NEXT dump changes
::X|EN|crash.dumps.033|                           - the crash-dump setting in Advanced system
::X|EN|crash.dumps.034|                           settings is untouched, so the next bugcheck
::X|EN|crash.dumps.035|                           writes a new file.
::X|EN|crash.dumps.036|    KEEP                 : The files stay. Windows never prunes them
::X|EN|crash.dumps.037|                           itself, so a machine that has crashed a few
::X|EN|crash.dumps.038|                           times keeps every minidump forever and one
::X|EN|crash.dumps.039|                           MEMORY.DMP, overwritten at each bugcheck.
::X|EN|crash.dumps.040|    ASK                  : Look at the actual size of
::X|EN|crash.dumps.041|                           C:\Windows\MEMORY.DMP first, then decide. That
::X|EN|crash.dumps.042|                           single number is the whole argument - a 400 MB
::X|EN|crash.dumps.043|                           file is not worth losing a diagnosis over.
::X|EN|crash.dumps.044|
::X|EN|crash.dumps.045|  Why these profiles : The first four columns are identical on purpose:
::X|EN|crash.dumps.046|                       whether a dump is worth keeping depends on whether
::X|EN|crash.dumps.047|                       you have an unexplained crash to investigate, not
::X|EN|crash.dumps.048|                       on what the machine is for, and inventing a split
::X|EN|crash.dumps.049|                       here would be dishonest. They read DELETE because
::X|EN|crash.dumps.050|                       the owner of this script decided minidumps go. The
::X|EN|crash.dumps.051|                       WINDOWS column is KEEP because Windows itself never
::X|EN|crash.dumps.052|                       removes them. Override the profile for one run if
::X|EN|crash.dumps.053|                       you have blue-screened recently.
::X|EN|crash.dumps.054|
::X|EN|crash.dumps.055|  Target          : OPTY.bat 992-994 - del /F /S /Q
::X|EN|crash.dumps.056|                    "%SystemRoot%\Minidump\*" and del /F /S /Q
::X|EN|crash.dumps.057|                    "%SystemRoot%\MEMORY.DMP". The cleanmgr pass at
::X|EN|crash.dumps.058|                    OPTY.bat 759-760 also sets StateFlags0064=2 on the
::X|EN|crash.dumps.059|                    "System error memory dump files" and "System error
::X|EN|crash.dumps.060|                    minidump files" handlers.
::X|FR|crash.dumps.001|  Ce que c est    : A chaque ecran bleu, Windows ecrit un petit dump dans
::X|FR|crash.dumps.002|                    C:\Windows\Minidump et, selon votre reglage de dump,
::X|FR|crash.dumps.003|                    un C:\Windows\MEMORY.DMP. Ce sont les seules traces de
::X|FR|crash.dumps.004|                    ce qui a reellement plante.
::X|FR|crash.dumps.005|
::X|FR|crash.dumps.006|  Effet reel      : Supprime les deux. La facon dont Windows ecrira les
::X|FR|crash.dumps.007|                    prochains dumps n est pas modifiee, et MEMORY.DMP
::X|FR|crash.dumps.008|                    exige toujours un fichier d echange sur le disque
::X|FR|crash.dumps.009|                    systeme pour pouvoir etre ecrit.
::X|FR|crash.dumps.010|
::X|FR|crash.dumps.011|  Gain            : De la place, uniquement. Les minidumps font quelques
::X|FR|crash.dumps.012|                    centaines de Ko chacun. MEMORY.DMP est ecrit en mode
::X|FR|crash.dumps.013|                    dump memoire automatique sur un Windows 11 d origine,
::X|FR|crash.dumps.014|                    c est-a-dire la memoire noyau seulement : en general
::X|FR|crash.dumps.015|                    de quelques centaines de Mo a 2 Go environ, PAS la
::X|FR|crash.dumps.016|                    taille de votre RAM. Il n approche la taille de la RAM
::X|FR|crash.dumps.017|                    installee que si vous avez choisi vous-meme le dump
::X|FR|crash.dumps.018|                    memoire complet dans les parametres systeme avances.
::X|FR|crash.dumps.019|                    Regardez la taille du fichier avant de decider.
::X|FR|crash.dumps.020|
::X|FR|crash.dumps.021|  Cout            : Vous detruisez definitivement les preuves de tous vos
::X|FR|crash.dumps.022|                    ecrans bleus et plantages de pilote graphique. Si
::X|FR|crash.dumps.023|                    vous, ou quelqu un qui vous aide, cherchez plus tard
::X|FR|crash.dumps.024|                    quel pilote tue la machine, la reponse a disparu. Et
::X|FR|crash.dumps.025|                    MEMORY.DMP n existe que si vous avez deja plante,
::X|FR|crash.dumps.026|                    c est-a-dire exactement quand il merite d etre garde.
::X|FR|crash.dumps.027|
::X|FR|crash.dumps.028|  Defaut Windows  : Sans objet. Windows les ecrit a chaque bugcheck et les
::X|FR|crash.dumps.029|                    conserve jusqu a ce que quelque chose les supprime.
::X|FR|crash.dumps.030|
::X|FR|crash.dumps.031|  Valeurs possibles :
::X|FR|crash.dumps.032|    DELETE               : C:\Windows\Minidump\* et C:\Windows\MEMORY.DMP
::X|FR|crash.dumps.033|                           sont supprimes. La facon dont Windows ecrira le
::X|FR|crash.dumps.034|                           PROCHAIN dump n est pas modifiee : le reglage
::X|FR|crash.dumps.035|                           des dumps dans les parametres systeme avances
::X|FR|crash.dumps.036|                           n est pas touche, le prochain bugcheck ecrira
::X|FR|crash.dumps.037|                           donc un nouveau fichier.
::X|FR|crash.dumps.038|    KEEP                 : Les fichiers restent. Windows ne fait jamais le
::X|FR|crash.dumps.039|                           menage lui-meme : une machine qui a plante
::X|FR|crash.dumps.040|                           plusieurs fois conserve tous ses minidumps
::X|FR|crash.dumps.041|                           indefiniment, plus un MEMORY.DMP ecrase a
::X|FR|crash.dumps.042|                           chaque bugcheck.
::X|FR|crash.dumps.043|    ASK                  : Regardez d abord la taille reelle de
::X|FR|crash.dumps.044|                           C:\Windows\MEMORY.DMP, puis decidez. Ce seul
::X|FR|crash.dumps.045|                           chiffre resume tout le debat : un fichier de
::X|FR|crash.dumps.046|                           400 Mo ne vaut pas la perte d un diagnostic.
::X|FR|crash.dumps.047|
::X|FR|crash.dumps.048|  Pourquoi ces profils : Les quatre premieres colonnes sont identiques a
::X|FR|crash.dumps.049|                         dessein : garder un dump depend de la presence
::X|FR|crash.dumps.050|                         d un plantage inexplique a analyser, pas de
::X|FR|crash.dumps.051|                         l usage de la machine, et inventer une
::X|FR|crash.dumps.052|                         distinction ici serait malhonnete. Elles disent
::X|FR|crash.dumps.053|                         DELETE parce que le proprietaire de ce script a
::X|FR|crash.dumps.054|                         tranche : les minidumps degagent. La colonne
::X|FR|crash.dumps.055|                         WINDOWS dit KEEP parce que Windows ne les
::X|FR|crash.dumps.056|                         supprime jamais de lui-meme. Passez outre le
::X|FR|crash.dumps.057|                         profil pour une execution si vous avez eu un
::X|FR|crash.dumps.058|                         ecran bleu recemment.
::X|FR|crash.dumps.059|
::X|FR|crash.dumps.060|  Cible           : OPTY.bat 992-994 - del /F /S /Q
::X|FR|crash.dumps.061|                    "%SystemRoot%\Minidump\*" and del /F /S /Q
::X|FR|crash.dumps.062|                    "%SystemRoot%\MEMORY.DMP". The cleanmgr pass at
::X|FR|crash.dumps.063|                    OPTY.bat 759-760 also sets StateFlags0064=2 on the
::X|FR|crash.dumps.064|                    "System error memory dump files" and "System error
::X|FR|crash.dumps.065|                    minidump files" handlers.
