:: ---- rad.disablepagingexec (repair) -----------------------------
::P|rad.disablepagingexec|0|0|0|0|0|
::T|EN|rad.disablepagingexec.001|LET WINDOWS PAGE KERNEL CODE AGAIN
::T|EN|rad.disablepagingexec.002|Sets DisablePagingExecutive back to 0 so kernel code and drivers can be paged out when memory is tight, undoing a tweak whose speed benefit was never shown to matter on a modern PC with plenty of RAM and an SSD.
::T|FR|rad.disablepagingexec.001|REAUTORISER LA PAGINATION DU CODE NOYAU
::T|FR|rad.disablepagingexec.002|Remet DisablePagingExecutive a 0 pour que le code noyau et les pilotes puissent de nouveau etre pagines quand la memoire manque, annulant un reglage dont le gain n a jamais ete demontre sur un PC moderne avec assez de RAM et un SSD.
::X|EN|rad.disablepagingexec.001|  What it is      : Decides whether kernel code and drivers may be paged
::X|EN|rad.disablepagingexec.002|                    out of RAM to the pagefile.
::X|EN|rad.disablepagingexec.003|
::X|EN|rad.disablepagingexec.004|  Actual effect   : Writes 0, the shipped value, so the memory manager can
::X|EN|rad.disablepagingexec.005|                    page them again when memory is tight.
::X|EN|rad.disablepagingexec.006|
::X|EN|rad.disablepagingexec.007|  Gain            : None you will feel. It removes a tweak whose
::X|EN|rad.disablepagingexec.008|                    performance claim has never been demonstrated on a
::X|EN|rad.disablepagingexec.009|                    machine with modern amounts of RAM and an SSD.
::X|EN|rad.disablepagingexec.010|
::X|EN|rad.disablepagingexec.011|  Cost            : Nothing. This is a pure repair.
::X|EN|rad.disablepagingexec.012|
::X|EN|rad.disablepagingexec.013|  Windows default : 0.
::X|EN|rad.disablepagingexec.014|
::X|EN|rad.disablepagingexec.015|  Possible values:
::X|EN|rad.disablepagingexec.016|    0                    : The shipped value. Kernel code and drivers that
::X|EN|rad.disablepagingexec.017|                           are marked pageable may be written out to the
::X|EN|rad.disablepagingexec.018|                           pagefile when memory gets tight, and read back
::X|EN|rad.disablepagingexec.019|                           on demand. The memory manager decides, page by
::X|EN|rad.disablepagingexec.020|                           page, based on actual pressure.
::X|EN|rad.disablepagingexec.021|    1                    : Kernel code and drivers must stay resident in
::X|EN|rad.disablepagingexec.022|                           physical RAM and are never paged out. The
::X|EN|rad.disablepagingexec.023|                           tweak-guide promise is that this avoids a disk
::X|EN|rad.disablepagingexec.024|                           read on a driver call; what it actually does is
::X|EN|rad.disablepagingexec.025|                           take that RAM away from applications
::X|EN|rad.disablepagingexec.026|                           permanently, which on a machine with a fast SSD
::X|EN|rad.disablepagingexec.027|                           trades a certainty for a rarity. Microsoft asks
::X|EN|rad.disablepagingexec.028|                           for 1 during live kernel debugging.
::X|EN|rad.disablepagingexec.029|    absent               : Behaves like 0. Windows 11 ships the value
::X|EN|rad.disablepagingexec.030|                           present at 0, so absence usually means a tool
::X|EN|rad.disablepagingexec.031|                           deleted it.
::X|EN|rad.disablepagingexec.032|
::X|EN|rad.disablepagingexec.033|  Why these profiles : Five identical zeros. The only real argument for 1
::X|EN|rad.disablepagingexec.034|                       is live kernel debugging, which is not one of the
::X|EN|rad.disablepagingexec.035|                       five profiles - and even a server gains nothing
::X|EN|rad.disablepagingexec.036|                       from pinning driver code that the memory manager
::X|EN|rad.disablepagingexec.037|                       was never going to evict under normal pressure.
::X|EN|rad.disablepagingexec.038|
::X|EN|rad.disablepagingexec.039|  Unverified      : The claim that value 0 is needed for crash dumps is
::X|EN|rad.disablepagingexec.040|                    not something I can substantiate; Microsoft asks for 1
::X|EN|rad.disablepagingexec.041|                    during live kernel debugging, which points the other
::X|EN|rad.disablepagingexec.042|                    way.
::X|EN|rad.disablepagingexec.043|
::X|EN|rad.disablepagingexec.044|  Target          : call :regset
::X|EN|rad.disablepagingexec.045|                    "HKLM\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\Session
::X|EN|rad.disablepagingexec.046|                    Manager\Memory Management" "DisablePagingExecutive"
::X|EN|rad.disablepagingexec.047|                    REG_DWORD 0 (OPTY.bat 1866, in :reassert_defaults)
::X|FR|rad.disablepagingexec.001|  Ce que c est    : Decide si le code du noyau et les pilotes peuvent etre
::X|FR|rad.disablepagingexec.002|                    dechargés de la RAM vers le fichier d echange.
::X|FR|rad.disablepagingexec.003|
::X|FR|rad.disablepagingexec.004|  Effet reel      : Ecrit 0, la valeur d origine : le gestionnaire de
::X|FR|rad.disablepagingexec.005|                    memoire peut de nouveau les paginer quand la RAM
::X|FR|rad.disablepagingexec.006|                    manque.
::X|FR|rad.disablepagingexec.007|
::X|FR|rad.disablepagingexec.008|  Gain            : Aucun que vous sentirez. Cela retire un tweak dont le
::X|FR|rad.disablepagingexec.009|                    gain n a jamais ete demontre sur une machine avec de
::X|FR|rad.disablepagingexec.010|                    la RAM moderne et un SSD.
::X|FR|rad.disablepagingexec.011|
::X|FR|rad.disablepagingexec.012|  Cout            : Rien. Simple remise en ordre.
::X|FR|rad.disablepagingexec.013|
::X|FR|rad.disablepagingexec.014|  Defaut Windows  : 0.
::X|FR|rad.disablepagingexec.015|
::X|FR|rad.disablepagingexec.016|  Valeurs possibles :
::X|FR|rad.disablepagingexec.017|    0                    : La valeur d origine. Le code noyau et les
::X|FR|rad.disablepagingexec.018|                           pilotes marques paginables peuvent etre ecrits
::X|FR|rad.disablepagingexec.019|                           vers le fichier d echange quand la memoire se
::X|FR|rad.disablepagingexec.020|                           tend, puis relus a la demande. Le gestionnaire
::X|FR|rad.disablepagingexec.021|                           de memoire decide page par page, selon la
::X|FR|rad.disablepagingexec.022|                           pression reelle.
::X|FR|rad.disablepagingexec.023|    1                    : Le code noyau et les pilotes doivent rester
::X|FR|rad.disablepagingexec.024|                           residents en RAM physique et ne sont jamais
::X|FR|rad.disablepagingexec.025|                           pagines. La promesse des guides est d eviter
::X|FR|rad.disablepagingexec.026|                           une lecture disque lors d un appel de pilote ;
::X|FR|rad.disablepagingexec.027|                           en pratique, cela retire definitivement cette
::X|FR|rad.disablepagingexec.028|                           RAM aux applications, ce qui, sur une machine a
::X|FR|rad.disablepagingexec.029|                           SSD rapide, echange une certitude contre une
::X|FR|rad.disablepagingexec.030|                           rarete. Microsoft demande 1 pendant un debogage
::X|FR|rad.disablepagingexec.031|                           noyau en direct.
::X|FR|rad.disablepagingexec.032|    absent               : Se comporte comme 0. Windows 11 livre la valeur
::X|FR|rad.disablepagingexec.033|                           presente a 0 : son absence signifie
::X|FR|rad.disablepagingexec.034|                           generalement qu un outil l a supprimee.
::X|FR|rad.disablepagingexec.035|
::X|FR|rad.disablepagingexec.036|  Pourquoi ces profils : Cinq zeros identiques. Le seul vrai argument pour
::X|FR|rad.disablepagingexec.037|                         1 est le debogage noyau en direct, qui ne fait
::X|FR|rad.disablepagingexec.038|                         partie d aucun des cinq profils - et meme un
::X|FR|rad.disablepagingexec.039|                         serveur ne gagne rien a epingler du code de
::X|FR|rad.disablepagingexec.040|                         pilote que le gestionnaire de memoire n aurait de
::X|FR|rad.disablepagingexec.041|                         toute facon pas evince sous une pression normale.
::X|FR|rad.disablepagingexec.042|
::X|FR|rad.disablepagingexec.043|  Non verifie (en)  : The claim that value 0 is needed for crash dumps is
::X|FR|rad.disablepagingexec.044|                      not something I can substantiate; Microsoft asks for
::X|FR|rad.disablepagingexec.045|                      1 during live kernel debugging, which points the
::X|FR|rad.disablepagingexec.046|                      other way.
::X|FR|rad.disablepagingexec.047|
::X|FR|rad.disablepagingexec.048|  Cible           : call :regset
::X|FR|rad.disablepagingexec.049|                    "HKLM\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\Session
::X|FR|rad.disablepagingexec.050|                    Manager\Memory Management" "DisablePagingExecutive"
::X|FR|rad.disablepagingexec.051|                    REG_DWORD 0 (OPTY.bat 1866, in :reassert_defaults)
