:: ---- rad.pagefile.repair (risky) -------------------------------
::P|rad.pagefile.repair|APPLY|APPLY|APPLY|APPLY|APPLY|
::T|EN|rad.pagefile.repair.001|RESTORE A PAGEFILE IF VIRTUAL MEMORY WAS TURNED OFF
::T|EN|rad.pagefile.repair.002|Checks whether virtual memory was disabled and, only if so, recreates a system-managed pagefile - fixing out-of-memory crashes and restoring the ability to save a crash dump, at the cost of a few GB of disk space chosen by Windows.
::T|FR|rad.pagefile.repair.001|RETABLIR UN FICHIER D ECHANGE S IL A ETE SUPPRIME
::T|FR|rad.pagefile.repair.002|Verifie si la memoire virtuelle a ete desactivee et, seulement dans ce cas, recree un fichier d echange gere par le systeme - corrigeant des plantages par manque de memoire et retablissant les dumps, au prix de quelques Go d espace disque choisis par Windows.
::X|EN|rad.pagefile.repair.001|  What it is      : PagingFiles is the value the kernel actually reads to
::X|EN|rad.pagefile.repair.002|                    know whether there is a pagefile at all, and where.
::X|EN|rad.pagefile.repair.003|                    AutomaticManagedPagefile is only the checkbox the
::X|EN|rad.pagefile.repair.004|                    management UI shows.
::X|EN|rad.pagefile.repair.005|
::X|EN|rad.pagefile.repair.006|  Actual effect   : Reads PagingFiles first and acts only when it is
::X|EN|rad.pagefile.repair.007|                    missing or empty. Then it writes a system-managed
::X|EN|rad.pagefile.repair.008|                    pagefile on the system drive and ticks the checkbox.
::X|EN|rad.pagefile.repair.009|                    Needs a reboot. Note the parsing detail the script
::X|EN|rad.pagefile.repair.010|                    comments on: tokens=2* is used because a REG_MULTI_SZ
::X|EN|rad.pagefile.repair.011|                    entry is multi-word, and the tokens=3 form used
::X|EN|rad.pagefile.repair.012|                    elsewhere for DWORDs reported '0 0' as the whole
::X|EN|rad.pagefile.repair.013|                    pagefile.
::X|EN|rad.pagefile.repair.014|
::X|EN|rad.pagefile.repair.015|  Gain            : Fixes out-of-memory crashes and applications dying for
::X|EN|rad.pagefile.repair.016|                    no visible reason on a machine where someone disabled
::X|EN|rad.pagefile.repair.017|                    virtual memory to save disk space. It also restores
::X|EN|rad.pagefile.repair.018|                    the ability to write MEMORY.DMP on a bugcheck, which
::X|EN|rad.pagefile.repair.019|                    requires a pagefile on the system drive.
::X|EN|rad.pagefile.repair.020|
::X|EN|rad.pagefile.repair.021|  Cost            : Disk space for the pagefile - a few GB, sized by
::X|EN|rad.pagefile.repair.022|                    Windows. A deliberate fixed-size pagefile is never
::X|EN|rad.pagefile.repair.023|                    touched, because the guard reads the value before
::X|EN|rad.pagefile.repair.024|                    writing anything.
::X|EN|rad.pagefile.repair.025|
::X|EN|rad.pagefile.repair.026|  Windows default : A system-managed pagefile on the system drive.
::X|EN|rad.pagefile.repair.027|
::X|EN|rad.pagefile.repair.028|  Possible values:
::X|EN|rad.pagefile.repair.029|    APPLY                : If and only if PagingFiles is absent or empty,
::X|EN|rad.pagefile.repair.030|                           it is written as '%SystemDrive%\pagefile.sys 0
::X|EN|rad.pagefile.repair.031|                           0' - the 0 0 pair meaning system-managed
::X|EN|rad.pagefile.repair.032|                           initial and maximum size - and the
::X|EN|rad.pagefile.repair.033|                           AutomaticManagedPagefile checkbox is set to 1.
::X|EN|rad.pagefile.repair.034|                           Effective at the next reboot. If PagingFiles
::X|EN|rad.pagefile.repair.035|                           already holds anything, the step logs what it
::X|EN|rad.pagefile.repair.036|                           found and writes nothing.
::X|EN|rad.pagefile.repair.037|    SKIP                 : A machine with virtual memory switched off
::X|EN|rad.pagefile.repair.038|                           stays that way: applications keep dying on
::X|EN|rad.pagefile.repair.039|                           commit-limit failures that look like random
::X|EN|rad.pagefile.repair.040|                           crashes, and no kernel dump can be written on a
::X|EN|rad.pagefile.repair.041|                           bugcheck.
::X|EN|rad.pagefile.repair.042|
::X|EN|rad.pagefile.repair.043|  Why these profiles : Five identical APPLY columns, WINDOWS included,
::X|EN|rad.pagefile.repair.044|                       because a pagefile is what Windows ships and the
::X|EN|rad.pagefile.repair.045|                       step is a no-op on any machine that already has
::X|EN|rad.pagefile.repair.046|                       one. Nobody, on any of these five profiles,
::X|EN|rad.pagefile.repair.047|                       benefits from having no pagefile at all - decline
::X|EN|rad.pagefile.repair.048|                       only if you run without one knowingly and accept
::X|EN|rad.pagefile.repair.049|                       the crash-dump loss.
::X|EN|rad.pagefile.repair.050|
::X|EN|rad.pagefile.repair.051|  Unverified      : The exact stock PagingFiles string varies by
::X|EN|rad.pagefile.repair.052|                    installation; '%SystemDrive%\pagefile.sys 0 0' is a
::X|EN|rad.pagefile.repair.053|                    valid system-managed equivalent, not necessarily byte-
::X|EN|rad.pagefile.repair.054|                    identical to the one your image shipped.
::X|EN|rad.pagefile.repair.055|
::X|EN|rad.pagefile.repair.056|  Target          : OPTY.bat 1884-1887, in :reassert_defaults - reads
::X|EN|rad.pagefile.repair.057|                    PagingFiles under
::X|EN|rad.pagefile.repair.058|                    HKLM\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\Session
::X|EN|rad.pagefile.repair.059|                    Manager\Memory Management with tokens=2*, and only
::X|EN|rad.pagefile.repair.060|                    when it is missing or empty writes PagingFiles as
::X|EN|rad.pagefile.repair.061|                    REG_MULTI_SZ "%SystemDrive%\pagefile.sys 0 0" plus
::X|EN|rad.pagefile.repair.062|                    AutomaticManagedPagefile=1
::X|FR|rad.pagefile.repair.001|  Ce que c est    : PagingFiles est la valeur que le noyau lit reellement
::X|FR|rad.pagefile.repair.002|                    pour savoir s il existe un fichier d echange, et ou.
::X|FR|rad.pagefile.repair.003|                    AutomaticManagedPagefile n est que la case a cocher
::X|FR|rad.pagefile.repair.004|                    affichee par l interface de gestion.
::X|FR|rad.pagefile.repair.005|
::X|FR|rad.pagefile.repair.006|  Effet reel      : Lit d abord PagingFiles et n agit que s il est absent
::X|FR|rad.pagefile.repair.007|                    ou vide. Ecrit alors un fichier gere par le systeme
::X|FR|rad.pagefile.repair.008|                    sur le disque systeme et coche la case. Redemarrage
::X|FR|rad.pagefile.repair.009|                    requis. Notez le detail d analyse que le script
::X|FR|rad.pagefile.repair.010|                    commente : tokens=2* est utilise parce qu une entree
::X|FR|rad.pagefile.repair.011|                    REG_MULTI_SZ compte plusieurs mots, et la forme
::X|FR|rad.pagefile.repair.012|                    tokens=3 employee ailleurs pour les DWORD rapportait «
::X|FR|rad.pagefile.repair.013|                    0 0 » comme etant tout le fichier d echange.
::X|FR|rad.pagefile.repair.014|
::X|FR|rad.pagefile.repair.015|  Gain            : Corrige les plantages par manque de memoire et les
::X|FR|rad.pagefile.repair.016|                    applications qui meurent sans raison visible sur une
::X|FR|rad.pagefile.repair.017|                    machine ou quelqu un a coupe la memoire virtuelle pour
::X|FR|rad.pagefile.repair.018|                    gagner de la place. Cela retablit aussi l ecriture de
::X|FR|rad.pagefile.repair.019|                    MEMORY.DMP lors d un bugcheck, qui exige un fichier
::X|FR|rad.pagefile.repair.020|                    d echange sur le disque systeme.
::X|FR|rad.pagefile.repair.021|
::X|FR|rad.pagefile.repair.022|  Cout            : De l espace disque pour le fichier - quelques Go,
::X|FR|rad.pagefile.repair.023|                    dimensionnes par Windows. Un fichier d echange fixe
::X|FR|rad.pagefile.repair.024|                    choisi volontairement n est jamais ecrase : le garde-
::X|FR|rad.pagefile.repair.025|                    fou lit la valeur avant d ecrire quoi que ce soit.
::X|FR|rad.pagefile.repair.026|
::X|FR|rad.pagefile.repair.027|  Defaut Windows  : Un fichier d echange gere par le systeme sur le disque
::X|FR|rad.pagefile.repair.028|                    systeme.
::X|FR|rad.pagefile.repair.029|
::X|FR|rad.pagefile.repair.030|  Valeurs possibles :
::X|FR|rad.pagefile.repair.031|    APPLY                : Si et seulement si PagingFiles est absent ou
::X|FR|rad.pagefile.repair.032|                           vide, il est ecrit comme «
::X|FR|rad.pagefile.repair.033|                           %SystemDrive%\pagefile.sys 0 0 » - le couple 0
::X|FR|rad.pagefile.repair.034|                           0 signifiant taille initiale et maximale gerees
::X|FR|rad.pagefile.repair.035|                           par le systeme - et la case
::X|FR|rad.pagefile.repair.036|                           AutomaticManagedPagefile est mise a 1. Effectif
::X|FR|rad.pagefile.repair.037|                           au prochain redemarrage. Si PagingFiles
