:: ---- rad.mm.leftover.killkeys (repair) --------------------------
::P|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys|DELETE|DELETE|DELETE|DELETE|DELETE|
::T|EN|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.001|REMOVE TEN OLD MEMORY-MANAGER OVERRIDES
::T|EN|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.002|Deletes ten registry values Windows never creates on its own, left behind by old tuning guides - the only one that really matters is MoveImages, whose removal restores full ASLR strength, while the other nine simply stop overriding a memory manager that already sizes itself correctly.
::T|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.001|RETIRER DIX ANCIENS FORCAGES DU GESTIONNAIRE DE MEMOIRE
::T|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.002|Supprime dix valeurs de registre que Windows ne cree jamais lui meme, laissees par de vieux guides de reglage - seule MoveImages compte vraiment : sa suppression retablit la pleine efficacite de l ASLR, et les neuf autres cessent simplement de brider un gestionnaire de memoire qui se dimensionne deja correctement.
::X|EN|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.001|  What it is      : Ten values that Windows ships without, including
::X|EN|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.002|                    MoveImages, PoolUsageMaximum, IoPageLockLimit and
::X|EN|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.003|                    DisablePageCombining. Every one of them is something
::X|EN|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.004|                    an old tuning guide told people to add.
::X|EN|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.005|
::X|EN|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.006|  Actual effect   : Deletes all ten. Writing zero would not restore the
::X|EN|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.007|                    default - only absence does. SessionPoolSize and
::X|EN|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.008|                    SessionViewSize are never touched, because Windows
::X|EN|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.009|                    Setup writes real values there.
::X|EN|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.010|
::X|EN|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.011|  Gain            : One genuine security repair: MoveImages=0 disables
::X|EN|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.012|                    image relocation and therefore weakens ASLR. The other
::X|EN|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.013|                    nine simply stop overriding a memory manager that
::X|EN|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.014|                    sizes itself better than a fixed number can.
::X|EN|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.015|
::X|EN|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.016|  Cost            : Nothing. None of these values has a demonstrated
::X|EN|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.017|                    performance benefit on 64-bit Windows 11.
::X|EN|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.018|
::X|EN|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.019|  Windows default : All ten absent.
::X|EN|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.020|
::X|EN|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.021|  Possible values:
::X|EN|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.022|    DELETE               : All ten values are removed, which is the only
::X|EN|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.023|                           way to restore the default, because Windows
::X|EN|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.024|                           ships this key without any of them. MoveImages
::X|EN|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.025|                           gone means image relocation works normally
::X|EN|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.026|                           again and ASLR keeps its entropy. The pool and
::X|EN|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.027|                           cache limits gone means the memory manager
::X|EN|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.028|                           sizes those pools dynamically as it was
::X|EN|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.029|                           designed to.
::X|EN|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.030|    0                    : What tweak scripts usually write, and it is NOT
::X|EN|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.031|                           the default - it is a third state. MoveImages=0
::X|EN|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.032|                           in particular tells the loader to keep images
::X|EN|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.033|                           at their preferred base address, which defeats
::X|EN|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.034|                           the relocation part of ASLR and is a real
::X|EN|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.035|                           security regression. The pool limits at 0 are
::X|EN|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.036|                           not 'unlimited', they are an explicit value the
::X|EN|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.037|                           memory manager now has to honour.
::X|EN|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.038|    any non-zero number  : A hard cap or preference the memory manager
::X|EN|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.039|                           must obey instead of adapting. IoPageLockLimit,
::X|EN|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.040|                           PoolUsageMaximum, the four *Limit values and
::X|EN|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.041|                           AllocationPreference were tuning knobs for
::X|EN|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.042|                           32-bit address-space problems that a 64-bit
::X|EN|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.043|                           Windows 11 does not have.
::X|EN|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.044|    absent               : The shipped state for all ten, and what this
::X|EN|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.045|                           step restores.
::X|EN|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.046|
::X|EN|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.047|  Why these profiles : Five identical DELETE columns. These are not use-
::X|EN|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.048|                       case settings - they are leftovers, and absence is
::X|EN|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.049|                       correct on every machine including the WINDOWS
::X|EN|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.050|                       profile, where absence is literally the shipped
::X|EN|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.051|                       state.
::X|EN|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.052|
::X|EN|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.053|  Target          : OPTY.bat 1899-1900, in :reassert_defaults - for %%V in
::X|EN|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.054|                    (DisablePageCombining IoPageLockLimit PoolUsageMaximum
::X|EN|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.055|                    MoveImages SystemCacheDirtyPageThreshold
::X|EN|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.056|                    NonPagedPoolLimit PagedPoolLimit SystemCacheLimit
::X|EN|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.057|                    SystemPtesLimit AllocationPreference) do call :killkey
::X|EN|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.058|                    "HKLM\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\Session
::X|EN|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.059|                    Manager\Memory Management" "%%V". SessionPoolSize and
::X|EN|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.060|                    SessionViewSize are deliberately excluded.
::X|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.001|  Ce que c est    : Dix valeurs que Windows ne cree jamais, dont
::X|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.002|                    MoveImages, PoolUsageMaximum, IoPageLockLimit et
::X|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.003|                    DisablePageCombining. Chacune vient d un vieux guide
::X|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.004|                    de reglage.
::X|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.005|
::X|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.006|  Effet reel      : Les supprime toutes. Ecrire zero ne retablirait pas le
::X|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.007|                    defaut : seule l absence le fait. SessionPoolSize et
::X|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.008|                    SessionViewSize ne sont jamais touchees, car le
::X|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.009|                    programme d installation de Windows y ecrit de vraies
::X|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.010|                    valeurs.
::X|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.011|
::X|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.012|  Gain            : Une vraie reparation de securite : MoveImages=0
::X|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.013|                    empeche la relocalisation des images et affaiblit donc
::X|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.014|                    l ASLR. Les neuf autres cessent simplement de brider
::X|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.015|                    un gestionnaire de memoire qui se dimensionne mieux
::X|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.016|                    qu un chiffre fige.
::X|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.017|
::X|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.018|  Cout            : Rien. Aucune de ces valeurs n a de gain demontre sur
::X|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.019|                    un Windows 11 64 bits.
::X|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.020|
::X|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.021|  Defaut Windows  : Les dix absentes.
::X|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.022|
::X|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.023|  Valeurs possibles :
::X|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.024|    DELETE               : Les dix valeurs sont supprimees, seul moyen de
::X|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.025|                           retablir le defaut puisque Windows livre cette
::X|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.026|                           cle sans aucune d elles. MoveImages disparue,
::X|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.027|                           la relocalisation des images redevient normale
::X|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.028|                           et l ASLR garde son entropie. Les limites de
::X|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.029|                           pool et de cache disparues, le gestionnaire de
::X|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.030|                           memoire dimensionne ces pools dynamiquement,
::X|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.031|                           comme prevu.
::X|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.032|    0                    : Ce qu ecrivent generalement les scripts de
::X|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.033|                           bidouille, et ce n est PAS le defaut : c est un
::X|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.034|                           troisieme etat. MoveImages=0 en particulier
::X|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.035|                           demande au chargeur de garder les images a leur
::X|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.036|                           adresse de base preferee, ce qui annule la
::X|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.037|                           partie relocalisation de l ASLR : vraie
::X|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.038|                           regression de securite. Les limites de pool a 0
::X|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.039|                           ne signifient pas « illimite », c est une
::X|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.040|                           valeur explicite que le gestionnaire de memoire
::X|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.041|                           doit desormais respecter.
::X|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.042|    any non-zero number  : Un plafond ou une preference imposes au
::X|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.043|                           gestionnaire de memoire au lieu de le laisser
::X|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.044|                           s adapter. IoPageLockLimit, PoolUsageMaximum,
::X|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.045|                           les quatre valeurs *Limit et
::X|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.046|                           AllocationPreference etaient des reglages pour
::X|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.047|                           des problemes d espace d adressage 32 bits
::X|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.048|                           qu un Windows 11 64 bits n a pas.
::X|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.049|    absent               : L etat d origine pour les dix, et ce que cette
::X|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.050|                           etape retablit.
::X|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.051|
::X|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.052|  Pourquoi ces profils : Cinq colonnes identiques a DELETE. Ce ne sont pas
::X|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.053|                         des reglages lies a l usage mais des reliquats,
::X|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.054|                         et l absence est correcte sur toutes les
::X|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.055|                         machines, profil WINDOWS compris, ou l absence
::X|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.056|                         est litteralement l etat livre.
::X|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.057|
::X|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.058|  Cible           : OPTY.bat 1899-1900, in :reassert_defaults - for %%V in
::X|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.059|                    (DisablePageCombining IoPageLockLimit PoolUsageMaximum
::X|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.060|                    MoveImages SystemCacheDirtyPageThreshold
::X|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.061|                    NonPagedPoolLimit PagedPoolLimit SystemCacheLimit
::X|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.062|                    SystemPtesLimit AllocationPreference) do call :killkey
::X|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.063|                    "HKLM\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\Session
::X|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.064|                    Manager\Memory Management" "%%V". SessionPoolSize and
::X|FR|rad.mm.leftover.killkeys.065|                    SessionViewSize are deliberately excluded.
