:: ---- mo.superfetch.killkey (repair) -----------------------------
::P|mo.superfetch.killkey|DELETE|DELETE|DELETE|DELETE|DELETE|
::T|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.001|DELETE THE LEFTOVER ENABLESUPERFETCH VALUE
::T|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.002|Removes a Windows 7-era registry value that Windows 11 no longer reads, so the registry stops claiming a setting the OS does not actually have - SysMain behaviour is controlled by the service start type, not this value.
::T|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.001|SUPPRIMER LA VALEUR HERITEE ENABLESUPERFETCH
::T|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.002|Supprime une valeur de registre datant de Windows 7 que Windows 11 ne lit plus, pour que le registre cesse d afficher un reglage que le systeme n a plus - le comportement de SysMain depend du type de demarrage du service, pas de cette valeur.
::X|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.001|  What it is      : A leftover from Windows 7 that Windows 11 does not use
::X|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.002|                    or create, sitting in the same PrefetchParameters key
::X|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.003|                    as EnablePrefetcher.
::X|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.004|
::X|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.005|  Actual effect   : Deletes it if present rather than writing a value,
::X|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.006|                    since any value would be a state the OS does not have.
::X|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.007|
::X|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.008|  Gain            : None functional. It stops the registry claiming a
::X|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.009|                    setting the OS no longer has, which matters mostly to
::X|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.010|                    the next person or tool reading it.
::X|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.011|
::X|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.012|  Cost            : Nothing. This is a pure repair.
::X|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.013|
::X|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.014|  Windows default : Absent.
::X|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.015|
::X|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.016|  Possible values:
::X|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.017|    DELETE               : Removed if present, which restores the shipped
::X|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.018|                           state. The behaviour is then decided by the
::X|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.019|                           SysMain service start type alone.
::X|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.020|    0                    : The legacy 'off' value. Writing it on Windows
::X|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.021|                           11 creates a state the OS does not have and
::X|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.022|                           leaves the registry disagreeing with the
::X|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.023|                           service configuration.
::X|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.024|    1, 2 or 3            : The legacy modes from the Vista and Windows 7
::X|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.025|                           Superfetch component - boot only, applications
::X|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.026|                           only, both. That component no longer exists
::X|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.027|                           under this name.
::X|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.028|    absent               : The Windows 11 state. That key holds
::X|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.029|                           EnablePrefetcher and nothing else.
::X|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.030|
::X|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.031|  Why these profiles : Five identical DELETE columns, WINDOWS included,
::X|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.032|                       because absence is the shipped state. To change
::X|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.033|                       SysMain behaviour on any of these profiles, use the
::X|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.034|                       service start type instead.
::X|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.035|
::X|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.036|  Target          : call :killkey
::X|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.037|                    "HKLM\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\Session
::X|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.038|                    Manager\Memory Management\PrefetchParameters"
::X|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.039|                    "EnableSuperfetch" - via :askreg inside :setup_system.
::X|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.040|                    The same removal also happens, unasked, in
::X|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.041|                    :reassert_defaults.
::X|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.001|  Ce que c est    : Un reliquat de Windows 7 que Windows 11 n utilise ni
::X|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.002|                    ne cree, loge dans la meme cle PrefetchParameters
::X|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.003|                    qu EnablePrefetcher.
::X|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.004|
::X|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.005|  Effet reel      : La supprime si elle existe plutot que d y ecrire une
::X|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.006|                    valeur, puisque toute valeur serait un etat que le
::X|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.007|                    systeme n a pas.
::X|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.008|
::X|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.009|  Gain            : Aucun effet fonctionnel. Cela evite que la base de
::X|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.010|                    registre affiche un reglage que le systeme n a plus,
::X|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.011|                    ce qui compte surtout pour la prochaine personne ou le
::X|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.012|                    prochain outil qui la lira.
::X|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.013|
::X|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.014|  Cout            : Rien. Simple remise en ordre.
::X|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.015|
::X|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.016|  Defaut Windows  : Absente.
::X|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.017|
::X|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.018|  Valeurs possibles :
::X|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.019|    DELETE               : Supprimee si presente, ce qui retablit l etat
::X|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.020|                           d origine. Le comportement ne depend alors plus
::X|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.021|                           que du type de demarrage du service SysMain.
::X|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.022|    0                    : L ancienne valeur « desactive ». L ecrire sous
::X|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.023|                           Windows 11 cree un etat que le systeme n a pas
::X|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.024|                           et laisse le registre en desaccord avec la
::X|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.025|                           configuration du service.
::X|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.026|    1, 2 or 3            : Les modes hérités du composant Superfetch de
::X|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.027|                           Vista et Windows 7 - demarrage seul,
::X|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.028|                           applications seules, les deux. Ce composant
::X|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.029|                           n existe plus sous ce nom.
::X|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.030|    absent               : L etat Windows 11. Cette cle contient
::X|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.031|                           EnablePrefetcher et rien d autre.
::X|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.032|
