:: ---- rp.enable.system.protection (preference) -----------------------
::P|rp.enable.system.protection|APPLY|APPLY|APPLY|APPLY|SKIP|
::T|EN|rp.enable.system.protection.001|TURN ON SYSTEM PROTECTION FOR C:
::T|EN|rp.enable.system.protection.002|Enables System Protection on the system drive so restore points can exist at all, giving you a one-click undo for OPTY, Windows Update and driver installs - at the cost of a few GB of disk space for shadow copies, and OPTY never turns it back off.
::T|FR|rp.enable.system.protection.001|ACTIVER LA PROTECTION DU SYSTEME SUR C:
::T|FR|rp.enable.system.protection.002|Active la protection du systeme sur le disque systeme pour que des points de restauration puissent exister, ce qui offre une annulation en un clic pour OPTY, Windows Update et les installations de pilotes - au prix de quelques Go d espace disque pour les cliches, et OPTY ne la redesactive jamais.
::X|EN|rp.enable.system.protection.001|  What it is      : System Protection is the Windows feature behind
::X|EN|rp.enable.system.protection.002|                    restore points. When it is off, no restore point can
::X|EN|rp.enable.system.protection.003|                    exist - not the one OPTY wants to take, and not the
::X|EN|rp.enable.system.protection.004|                    one Windows Update takes before a driver install.
::X|EN|rp.enable.system.protection.005|
::X|EN|rp.enable.system.protection.006|  Actual effect   : Runs Enable-ComputerRestore on the system drive. On a
::X|EN|rp.enable.system.protection.007|                    machine that had it off this is a permanent change,
::X|EN|rp.enable.system.protection.008|                    because OPTY offers no way to turn it back off. That
::X|EN|rp.enable.system.protection.009|                    lives in System Properties, System Protection,
::X|EN|rp.enable.system.protection.010|                    Configure.
::X|EN|rp.enable.system.protection.011|
::X|EN|rp.enable.system.protection.012|  Gain            : You get an undo for everything OPTY, Windows Update
::X|EN|rp.enable.system.protection.013|                    and driver installers do afterwards. Without it the
::X|EN|rp.enable.system.protection.014|                    restore-point step fails silently and nothing this
::X|EN|rp.enable.system.protection.015|                    script does can be rolled back.
::X|EN|rp.enable.system.protection.016|
::X|EN|rp.enable.system.protection.017|  Cost            : Ongoing disk space on C: - the default shadow-copy
::X|EN|rp.enable.system.protection.018|                    quota is a few percent of the volume, so typically
::X|EN|rp.enable.system.protection.019|                    several GB on a large SSD. No measurable CPU or speed
::X|EN|rp.enable.system.protection.020|                    cost.
::X|EN|rp.enable.system.protection.021|
::X|EN|rp.enable.system.protection.022|  Windows default : A clean Windows 11 install ships System Protection OFF
::X|EN|rp.enable.system.protection.023|                    for the system drive. Many OEM images ship it ON. On a
::X|EN|rp.enable.system.protection.024|                    fresh machine this is therefore a change, not a
::X|EN|rp.enable.system.protection.025|                    repair.
::X|EN|rp.enable.system.protection.026|
::X|EN|rp.enable.system.protection.027|  Possible values:
::X|EN|rp.enable.system.protection.028|    APPLY                : Enable-ComputerRestore runs on the system
::X|EN|rp.enable.system.protection.029|                           drive. Windows allocates shadow-copy storage on
::X|EN|rp.enable.system.protection.030|                           C: and starts allowing restore points again -
::X|EN|rp.enable.system.protection.031|                           both the one OPTY takes and the ones Windows
::X|EN|rp.enable.system.protection.032|                           Update takes before a driver install. OPTY
::X|EN|rp.enable.system.protection.033|                           never turns it back off.
::X|EN|rp.enable.system.protection.034|    SKIP                 : Protection stays exactly as it was. If it was
::X|EN|rp.enable.system.protection.035|                           off, the restore point that follows fails
::X|EN|rp.enable.system.protection.036|                           silently and there is no rollback for anything
::X|EN|rp.enable.system.protection.037|                           OPTY, Windows Update or a driver installer does
::X|EN|rp.enable.system.protection.038|                           afterwards.
::X|EN|rp.enable.system.protection.039|
::X|EN|rp.enable.system.protection.040|  Why these profiles : Four profiles say APPLY because the value of an
::X|EN|rp.enable.system.protection.041|                       undo does not depend on what the machine is for,
::X|EN|rp.enable.system.protection.042|                       and the disk cost is small next to the cost of an
::X|EN|rp.enable.system.protection.043|                       unrecoverable registry state. The WINDOWS profile
::X|EN|rp.enable.system.protection.044|                       is the exception, and for a precise reason rather
::X|EN|rp.enable.system.protection.045|                       than a stylistic one: on a clean install,
::X|EN|rp.enable.system.protection.046|                       protection off IS the shipped state, and that
::X|EN|rp.enable.system.protection.047|                       profile exists to preserve it. Decline under any
::X|EN|rp.enable.system.protection.048|                       profile if your system drive is genuinely small,
::X|EN|rp.enable.system.protection.049|                       under about 128 GB, or if you already keep full
::X|EN|rp.enable.system.protection.050|                       disk images.
::X|EN|rp.enable.system.protection.051|
::X|EN|rp.enable.system.protection.052|  Target          : powershell -NoProfile -Command "Enable-ComputerRestore
::X|EN|rp.enable.system.protection.053|                    -Drive '%SystemDrive%\'" (OPTY.bat 3999, first line of
::X|EN|rp.enable.system.protection.054|                    :restore_point)
::X|FR|rp.enable.system.protection.001|  Ce que c est    : La protection du systeme est la fonction Windows
::X|FR|rp.enable.system.protection.002|                    derriere les points de restauration. Quand elle est
::X|FR|rp.enable.system.protection.003|                    desactivee, aucun point ne peut exister : ni celui
::X|FR|rp.enable.system.protection.004|                    qu OPTY veut prendre, ni celui que Windows Update
::X|FR|rp.enable.system.protection.005|                    prend avant d installer un pilote.
::X|FR|rp.enable.system.protection.006|
::X|FR|rp.enable.system.protection.007|  Effet reel      : Lance Enable-ComputerRestore sur le disque systeme.
::X|FR|rp.enable.system.protection.008|                    Sur une machine ou elle etait coupee, c est un
::X|FR|rp.enable.system.protection.009|                    changement permanent, car OPTY ne propose pas de la
::X|FR|rp.enable.system.protection.010|                    redesactiver. Cela se fait dans Proprietes systeme,
::X|FR|rp.enable.system.protection.011|                    Protection du systeme, Configurer.
::X|FR|rp.enable.system.protection.012|
::X|FR|rp.enable.system.protection.013|  Gain            : Vous obtenez une annulation pour tout ce qu OPTY,
::X|FR|rp.enable.system.protection.014|                    Windows Update et les installeurs de pilotes feront
::X|FR|rp.enable.system.protection.015|                    ensuite. Sans elle, l etape du point de restauration
::X|FR|rp.enable.system.protection.016|                    echoue en silence et rien de ce que fait ce script
::X|FR|rp.enable.system.protection.017|                    n est annulable.
::X|FR|rp.enable.system.protection.018|
::X|FR|rp.enable.system.protection.019|  Cout            : De l espace disque occupe en permanence sur C: : le
::X|FR|rp.enable.system.protection.020|                    quota de cliches par defaut represente quelques pour
::X|FR|rp.enable.system.protection.021|                    cent du volume, donc typiquement plusieurs Go sur un
::X|FR|rp.enable.system.protection.022|                    gros SSD. Aucun cout mesurable en CPU ni en vitesse.
::X|FR|rp.enable.system.protection.023|
::X|FR|rp.enable.system.protection.024|  Defaut Windows  : Une installation propre de Windows 11 livre la
::X|FR|rp.enable.system.protection.025|                    protection du systeme DESACTIVEE pour le disque
::X|FR|rp.enable.system.protection.026|                    systeme. Beaucoup d images constructeur la livrent
::X|FR|rp.enable.system.protection.027|                    activee. Sur une machine neuve, c est donc un
::X|FR|rp.enable.system.protection.028|                    changement et pas une reparation.
::X|FR|rp.enable.system.protection.029|
::X|FR|rp.enable.system.protection.030|  Valeurs possibles :
::X|FR|rp.enable.system.protection.031|    APPLY                : Enable-ComputerRestore s execute sur le disque
::X|FR|rp.enable.system.protection.032|                           systeme. Windows reserve de l espace de cliches
::X|FR|rp.enable.system.protection.033|                           instantanes sur C: et reautorise les points de
::X|FR|rp.enable.system.protection.034|                           restauration - celui qu OPTY cree comme ceux
::X|FR|rp.enable.system.protection.035|                           que Windows Update cree avant une installation
::X|FR|rp.enable.system.protection.036|                           de pilote. OPTY ne la redesactive jamais.
::X|FR|rp.enable.system.protection.037|    SKIP                 : La protection reste exactement telle quelle. Si
::X|FR|rp.enable.system.protection.038|                           elle etait coupee, le point de restauration qui
::X|FR|rp.enable.system.protection.039|                           suit echoue en silence et rien de ce que font
::X|FR|rp.enable.system.protection.040|                           ensuite OPTY, Windows Update ou un installeur
::X|FR|rp.enable.system.protection.041|                           de pilote n est annulable.
::X|FR|rp.enable.system.protection.042|
::X|FR|rp.enable.system.protection.043|  Pourquoi ces profils : Quatre profils disent APPLY parce que la valeur
::X|FR|rp.enable.system.protection.044|                         d une annulation ne depend pas de l usage de la
::X|FR|rp.enable.system.protection.045|                         machine, et que le cout en disque est faible face
::X|FR|rp.enable.system.protection.046|                         a celui d un etat de registre irrattrapable. Le
::X|FR|rp.enable.system.protection.047|                         profil WINDOWS fait exception pour une raison
::X|FR|rp.enable.system.protection.048|                         precise et non stylistique : sur une installation
::X|FR|rp.enable.system.protection.049|                         propre, la protection desactivee EST l etat
::X|FR|rp.enable.system.protection.050|                         livre, et ce profil sert a le preserver. Refusez
::X|FR|rp.enable.system.protection.051|                         quel que soit le profil si votre disque systeme
::X|FR|rp.enable.system.protection.052|                         est vraiment petit, moins de 128 Go environ, ou
::X|FR|rp.enable.system.protection.053|                         si vous faites deja des images disque completes.
::X|FR|rp.enable.system.protection.054|
::X|FR|rp.enable.system.protection.055|  Cible           : powershell -NoProfile -Command "Enable-ComputerRestore
::X|FR|rp.enable.system.protection.056|                    -Drive  %SystemDrive%\ " (OPTY.bat 3999, first line of
::X|FR|rp.enable.system.protection.057|                    :restore_point)
