:: ---- rp.checkpoint (preference) -------------------------------------
::P|rp.checkpoint|APPLY|APPLY|APPLY|APPLY|APPLY|
::T|EN|rp.checkpoint.001|CREATE A RESTORE POINT BEFORE CHANGING ANYTHING
::T|EN|rp.checkpoint.002|Takes one system restore point before OPTY touches anything, giving you a one-click rollback of registry and service changes if something goes wrong, at the cost of some VSS shadow-storage space and 10 to 60 seconds of wait.
::T|FR|rp.checkpoint.001|CREER UN POINT DE RESTAURATION AVANT TOUTE MODIFICATION
::T|FR|rp.checkpoint.002|Prend un point de restauration systeme avant qu OPTY ne touche a quoi que ce soit, offrant un retour en arriere en un clic sur les changements de registre et de services en cas de probleme, au prix d un peu d espace de cliches VSS et de 10 a 60 secondes d attente.
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.001|  What it is      : A single system restore point, named after the OPTY
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.002|                    version, taken once per session before any change that
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.003|                    might need undoing.
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.004|
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.005|  Actual effect   : Calls Checkpoint-Computer with type MODIFY_SETTINGS.
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.006|                    Windows snapshots the registry hives and protected
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.007|                    system files through VSS. It does not back up your
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.008|                    documents and never has - System Restore is not a
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.009|                    backup. If System Protection is off, the call simply
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.010|                    fails and OPTY warns and continues.
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.011|
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.012|  Gain            : One-click rollback of the registry and service changes
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.013|                    through System Restore if something in SETUP or Repair
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.014|                    turns out badly on your particular machine.
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.015|
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.016|  Cost            : Uses VSS shadow storage, typically a few hundred MB to
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.017|                    a couple of GB. When the shadow quota is full, Windows
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.018|                    silently deletes the OLDEST restore point to make
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.019|                    room, so an older point you were counting on can
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.020|                    disappear. Creation takes roughly 10 to 60 seconds.
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.021|
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.022|  Windows default : Not applicable - Windows creates restore points on its
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.023|                    own schedule, before driver installs and some updates,
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.024|                    never on demand.
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.025|
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.026|  Possible values:
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.027|    APPLY                : One restore point of type MODIFY_SETTINGS is
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.028|                           created. The 1440-minute throttle is set to 0
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.029|                           for the duration of the call and written
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.030|                           straight back afterwards, so Windows does not
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.031|                           refuse a point taken within a day of an earlier
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.032|                           one and the machine is not left permanently
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.033|                           altered.
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.034|    SKIP                 : No point is taken, and the throttle is never
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.035|                           touched. Whatever the run changes has no one-
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.036|                           click rollback.
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.037|
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.038|  Why these profiles : Five identical APPLY columns, WINDOWS included, and
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.039|                       here is why that profile does not opt out: taking a
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.040|                       point changes no configuration at all. The throttle
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.041|                       is restored immediately, and if System Protection
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.042|                       is off the call just fails harmlessly. The only
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.043|                       sane reason to decline is that you are re-running
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.044|                       OPTY for the fifth time today and would rather keep
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.045|                       this morning's older point than push it out of the
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.046|                       quota.
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.047|
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.048|  Target          : powershell -NoProfile -Command "Checkpoint-Computer
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.049|                    -Description 'OPTY v%current_version% - before
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.050|                    optimization' -RestorePointType 'MODIFY_SETTINGS'"
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.051|                    (OPTY.bat 4005), framed by
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.052|                    SystemRestorePointCreationFrequency set to 0 at line
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.053|                    4004 and back to 1440 at line 4013
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.001|  Ce que c est    : Un seul point de restauration systeme, nomme d apres
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.002|                    la version d OPTY, pris une fois par session avant
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.003|                    tout changement susceptible de devoir etre annule.
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.004|
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.005|  Effet reel      : Appelle Checkpoint-Computer en type MODIFY_SETTINGS.
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.006|                    Windows prend un instantane des ruches de registre et
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.007|                    des fichiers systeme proteges via VSS. Il ne
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.008|                    sauvegarde pas vos documents et ne l a jamais fait :
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.009|                    la restauration du systeme n est pas une sauvegarde.
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.010|                    Si la protection du systeme est coupee, l appel echoue
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.011|                    simplement et OPTY avertit puis continue.
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.012|
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.013|  Gain            : Un retour en arriere en un clic sur les modifications
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.014|                    de registre et de services, si quelque chose dans
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.015|                    SETUP ou dans la reparation tourne mal sur votre
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.016|                    machine.
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.017|
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.018|  Cout            : Occupe de l espace de cliches VSS, en general de
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.019|                    quelques centaines de Mo a deux Go. Quand le quota est
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.020|                    plein, Windows supprime silencieusement le point LE
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.021|                    PLUS ANCIEN pour faire de la place : un point plus
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.022|                    vieux sur lequel vous comptiez peut donc disparaitre.
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.023|                    La creation prend 10 a 60 secondes.
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.024|
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.025|  Defaut Windows  : Sans objet - Windows cree des points selon son propre
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.026|                    calendrier, avant l installation de pilotes et
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.027|                    certaines mises a jour, jamais a la demande.
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.028|
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.029|  Valeurs possibles :
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.030|    APPLY                : Un point de restauration de type
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.031|                           MODIFY_SETTINGS est cree. Le verrou de 1440
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.032|                           minutes est mis a 0 le temps de l appel puis
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.033|                           reecrit aussitot, pour que Windows ne refuse
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.034|                           pas un point pris moins d un jour apres un
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.035|                           autre et que la machine ne reste pas modifiee.
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.036|    SKIP                 : Aucun point n est pris et le verrou n est
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.037|                           jamais touche. Ce que l execution modifie n a
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.038|                           alors aucune annulation en un clic.
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.039|
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.040|  Pourquoi ces profils : Cinq colonnes identiques a APPLY, WINDOWS
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.041|                         compris, et voici pourquoi ce profil ne se retire
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.042|                         pas : prendre un point ne modifie aucune
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.043|                         configuration. Le verrou est retabli
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.044|                         immediatement, et si la protection du systeme est
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.045|                         coupee l appel echoue sans dommage. La seule
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.046|                         raison sensee de refuser : vous relancez OPTY
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.047|                         pour la cinquieme fois de la journee et preferez
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.048|                         garder le point de ce matin plutot que de le
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.049|                         faire sortir du quota.
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.050|
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.051|  Cible           : powershell -NoProfile -Command "Checkpoint-Computer
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.052|                    -Description  OPTY v%current_version% - before
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.053|                    optimization  -RestorePointType  MODIFY_SETTINGS "
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.054|                    (OPTY.bat 4005), framed by
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.055|                    SystemRestorePointCreationFrequency set to 0 at line
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.056|                    4004 and back to 1440 at line 4013
