::X|EN|cl.cleanmgr.pinoff.027|                    another machine image cannot arm them behind your
::X|EN|cl.cleanmgr.pinoff.028|                    back. Zero disk space is reclaimed by this step, by
::X|EN|cl.cleanmgr.pinoff.029|                    design.
::X|EN|cl.cleanmgr.pinoff.030|
::X|EN|cl.cleanmgr.pinoff.031|  Cost            : You forgo the space those handlers would have
::X|EN|cl.cleanmgr.pinoff.032|                    reclaimed. Update Cleanup and Windows ESD installation
::X|EN|cl.cleanmgr.pinoff.033|                    files are the two that matter, and they can be several
::X|EN|cl.cleanmgr.pinoff.034|                    GB. If you genuinely want that space, the DISM
::X|EN|cl.cleanmgr.pinoff.035|                    StartComponentCleanup step reclaims essentially the
::X|EN|cl.cleanmgr.pinoff.036|                    same thing without the collateral, and Windows ESD
::X|EN|cl.cleanmgr.pinoff.037|                    files can be removed separately once you are sure you
::X|EN|cl.cleanmgr.pinoff.038|                    will not need a reset image.
::X|EN|cl.cleanmgr.pinoff.039|
::X|EN|cl.cleanmgr.pinoff.040|  Windows default : Absent. Profile 0064 does not exist until OPTY writes
::X|EN|cl.cleanmgr.pinoff.041|                    it, so there is nothing to compare against - the
