::X|EN|cl.cleanmgr.pinoff.043|
::X|EN|cl.cleanmgr.pinoff.044|  Possible values:
::X|EN|cl.cleanmgr.pinoff.045|    DELETE               : Here DELETE means run the step, and the step
::X|EN|cl.cleanmgr.pinoff.046|                           itself deletes nothing - it writes twelve zeros
::X|EN|cl.cleanmgr.pinoff.047|                           so that DownloadsFolder, User file versions and
::X|EN|cl.cleanmgr.pinoff.048|                           Previous Installations cannot fire during
::X|EN|cl.cleanmgr.pinoff.049|                           cleanmgr /sagerun:64. The token is the answer
