:: ---- cl.vhdx.compact (cleanup) -----------------------------------
::P|cl.vhdx.compact|DELETE|ASK|DELETE|ASK|KEEP|
::T|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.001|SHRINK THE WSL AND DOCKER VIRTUAL DISKS
::T|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.002|Reclaims disk space that WSL and Docker virtual disks never give back on their own, often tens of GB, but it stops Docker and WSL for several minutes and a crash or power loss during the shrink can make the disk unusable with no way to recover it.
::T|FR|cl.vhdx.compact.001|RÉDUIRE LES DISQUES VIRTUELS WSL ET DOCKER
::T|FR|cl.vhdx.compact.002|Récupère de l espace disque que WSL et Docker ne rendent jamais tout seuls, souvent plusieurs dizaines de Go, mais arrête Docker et WSL pendant plusieurs minutes, et une coupure ou un plantage pendant l opération peut rendre le disque inutilisable sans aucun moyen de revenir en arrière.
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.001|  What it is      : WSL and Docker store their Linux filesystems inside
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.002|                    .vhdx virtual disk files. Those files grow when data
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.003|                    is written and never shrink when it is deleted, so a
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.004|                    distro can occupy 60 GB on your disk while holding 8
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.005|                    GB inside. This shrinks them back to their useful
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.006|                    size.
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.007|
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.008|  Actual effect   : First Docker Desktop is asked to quit cleanly and the
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.009|                    script waits up to 120 seconds for the docker-desktop
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.010|                    distro and com.docker.backend.exe to disappear; past
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.011|                    that it force-kills Docker Desktop, the backend, the
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.012|                    build and CLI helpers and vpnkit. Then wsl --shutdown.
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.013|                    Then, for each .vhdx found, diskpart runs select
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.014|                    vdisk, attach vdisk readonly, compact vdisk, detach
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.015|                    vdisk. Attaching read-only is what guarantees the
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.016|                    Linux filesystem inside is never modified - only the
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.017|                    unused space in the container is returned to Windows.
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.018|
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.019|  Gain            : Usually the single largest space win in the whole
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.020|                    script for anyone who uses Docker. Tens of GB is
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.021|                    routine on a developer machine that has built and
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.022|                    pruned a lot of images. Exactly zero for anyone who
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.023|                    uses neither WSL nor Docker, and zero on any machine
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.024|                    whose user folder is not C:\Users\compt, because then
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.025|                    nothing is found at all.
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.026|
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.027|  Cost            : Several minutes per disk - but understand what is
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.028|                    being rewritten. The .vhdx is the entire Linux
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.029|                    filesystem: your home directory, uncommitted work,
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.030|                    container volumes, database files. That is user data,
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.031|                    not a regenerable cache, and OPTY holds no copy of it.
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.032|                    If the machine loses power, is forced to reboot or
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.033|                    crashes during compact vdisk, the disk can be left
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.034|                    unmountable and there is no way back in this script.
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.035|                    Back the distro up first with wsl --export <distro>
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.036|                    <file>.tar, and do not start this if you cannot leave
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.037|                    the machine alone for a few minutes. On top of that,
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.038|                    running containers are stopped - cleanly if they
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.039|                    respond within 120 seconds, by taskkill /f if they do
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.040|                    not.
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.041|
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.042|  Windows default : Not applicable. Windows never compacts WSL or Docker
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.043|                    virtual disks on its own; they only ever grow.
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.044|
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.045|  Possible values:
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.046|    DELETE               : Stop Docker, shut WSL down and compact every
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.047|                           .vhdx found. Nothing inside the Linux
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.048|                           filesystem changes; only the unused space in
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.049|                           the container file is handed back to Windows.
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.050|                           Do it when you can leave the machine alone for
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.051|                           a few minutes.
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.052|    KEEP                 : Leave the virtual disks as they are. They keep
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.053|                           the space they have already claimed and will
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.054|                           claim more as you write; they never shrink on
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.055|                           their own. You lose disk space and nothing
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.056|                           else.
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.057|    ASK                  : For the server and the laptop, because on both
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.058|                           the interruption risk is real rather than
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.059|                           theoretical: on a server this step force-kills
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.060|                           Docker after 120 seconds and takes your
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.061|                           containers down with it, and on a laptop a
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.062|                           battery that dies mid-compact is exactly the
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.063|                           failure this operation cannot survive.
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.064|
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.065|  Why these profiles : Not four identical columns this time, and each
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.066|                       difference has a mechanism. GAMING and OFFICE take
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.067|                       it: either there is no .vhdx and nothing happens,
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.068|                       or there is one and the space is worth having.
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.069|                       SERVER asks, because this is the profile whose
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.070|                       whole job is to keep containers running and the
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.071|                       step force-kills Docker after two minutes. LAPTOP
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.072|                       asks, because several minutes of heavy I/O on
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.073|                       battery is the one situation where the disk can
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.074|                       lose power mid-rewrite. WINDOWS keeps, because
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.075|                       leaving these files alone is genuinely the shipped
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.076|                       behaviour.
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.077|
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.078|  Unverified      : The search paths come from USERHOME, WSL_DOCKER_VHDX,
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.079|                    WSL_SEARCH1 and WSL_SEARCH2, all built from
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.080|                    C:\Users\compt hardcoded at line 81. On any other
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.081|                    machine, or any other account name, this step finds
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.082|                    nothing and silently prints No WSL / Docker virtual
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.083|                    disk found. As written it is not portable, which
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.084|                    contradicts the project's own portability goal.
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.085|
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.086|  Target          : %USERHOME%\AppData\Local\Docker\wsl\disk\docker_data.v
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.087|                    hdx plus every ext4.vhdx found under
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.088|                    %USERHOME%\AppData\Local\Packages and
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.089|                    %USERHOME%\AppData\Local\wsl, where USERHOME is
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.090|                    hardcoded to C:\Users\compt at line 81. Each is fed to
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.091|                    diskpart as select vdisk / attach vdisk readonly /
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.092|                    compact vdisk / detach vdisk. OPTY.bat lines 781 to
::X|EN|cl.vhdx.compact.093|                    859, compact vdisk at line 847.
::X|FR|cl.vhdx.compact.001|  Ce que c est    : WSL et Docker rangent leurs systèmes de fichiers Linux
::X|FR|cl.vhdx.compact.002|                    dans des fichiers de disque virtuel .vhdx. Ces
::X|FR|cl.vhdx.compact.003|                    fichiers grossissent quand on écrit et ne rétrécissent
::X|FR|cl.vhdx.compact.004|                    jamais quand on efface : une distribution peut occuper
::X|FR|cl.vhdx.compact.005| 60 Go sur votre disque tout en n en contenant que 8.
::X|FR|cl.vhdx.compact.006|                    Cette étape les ramène à leur taille utile.
::X|FR|cl.vhdx.compact.007|
::X|FR|cl.vhdx.compact.008| Effet reel : On demande d abord à Docker Desktop de se fermer
::X|FR|cl.vhdx.compact.009|                    proprement, avec une attente de 120 secondes maximum
::X|FR|cl.vhdx.compact.010|                    que la distribution docker-desktop et
::X|FR|cl.vhdx.compact.011|                    com.docker.backend.exe disparaissent ; au-delà, le
::X|FR|cl.vhdx.compact.012|                    script tue de force Docker Desktop, le backend, les
::X|FR|cl.vhdx.compact.013|                    auxiliaires build et CLI, et vpnkit. Puis wsl
::X|FR|cl.vhdx.compact.014|                    --shutdown. Ensuite, pour chaque .vhdx trouvé,
::X|FR|cl.vhdx.compact.015|                    diskpart enchaîne select vdisk, attach vdisk readonly,
::X|FR|cl.vhdx.compact.016| compact vdisk, detach vdisk. L attachement en lecture
::X|FR|cl.vhdx.compact.017|                    seule est ce qui garantit que le système de fichiers
::X|FR|cl.vhdx.compact.018| Linux n est jamais modifié : seul l espace inutilisé
::X|FR|cl.vhdx.compact.019|                    du conteneur est rendu à Windows.
::X|FR|cl.vhdx.compact.020|
::X|FR|cl.vhdx.compact.021|  Gain            : En général le plus gros gain de place de tout le
::X|FR|cl.vhdx.compact.022|                    script pour qui utilise Docker : plusieurs dizaines de
::X|FR|cl.vhdx.compact.023|                    Go sont courantes sur une machine de développement qui
::X|FR|cl.vhdx.compact.024| a construit et élagué beaucoup d images. Exactement
::X|FR|cl.vhdx.compact.025| zéro pour qui n utilise ni WSL ni Docker, et zéro
::X|FR|cl.vhdx.compact.026|                    également sur toute machine dont le dossier
::X|FR|cl.vhdx.compact.027| utilisateur n est pas C:\Users\compt, puisque rien n y
::X|FR|cl.vhdx.compact.028|                    est alors trouvé.
::X|FR|cl.vhdx.compact.029|
::X|FR|cl.vhdx.compact.030|  Cout            : Plusieurs minutes par disque - mais comprenez ce qui
::X|FR|cl.vhdx.compact.031| est réécrit. Le .vhdx, c est tout le système de
::X|FR|cl.vhdx.compact.032|                    fichiers Linux : votre répertoire personnel, le
::X|FR|cl.vhdx.compact.033|                    travail non commité, les volumes de conteneurs, les
::X|FR|cl.vhdx.compact.034|                    fichiers de base de données. Ce sont des données
::X|FR|cl.vhdx.compact.035| utilisateur, pas un cache régénérable, et OPTY n en a
::X|FR|cl.vhdx.compact.036|                    aucune copie. Si la machine perd le courant, est
::X|FR|cl.vhdx.compact.037|                    redémarrée de force ou plante pendant compact vdisk,
::X|FR|cl.vhdx.compact.038| le disque peut rester immontable, et ce script n offre
::X|FR|cl.vhdx.compact.039| aucun retour arrière. Sauvegardez d abord la
::X|FR|cl.vhdx.compact.040|                    distribution avec wsl --export <distribution>
::X|FR|cl.vhdx.compact.041|                    <fichier>.tar, et ne lancez pas ceci si vous ne pouvez
::X|FR|cl.vhdx.compact.042|                    pas laisser la machine tranquille quelques minutes. À
::X|FR|cl.vhdx.compact.043| cela s ajoute l arrêt des conteneurs en cours :
::X|FR|cl.vhdx.compact.044| proprement s ils répondent en moins de 120 secondes,
::X|FR|cl.vhdx.compact.045|                    par taskkill /f sinon.
::X|FR|cl.vhdx.compact.046|
::X|FR|cl.vhdx.compact.047|  Defaut Windows  : Sans objet. Windows ne compacte jamais les disques
::X|FR|cl.vhdx.compact.048|                    virtuels WSL ou Docker de lui-même : ils ne font que
::X|FR|cl.vhdx.compact.049|                    grossir.
::X|FR|cl.vhdx.compact.050|
::X|FR|cl.vhdx.compact.051|  Valeurs possibles :
::X|FR|cl.vhdx.compact.052|    DELETE               : Arrêter Docker, éteindre WSL et compacter
::X|FR|cl.vhdx.compact.053|                           chaque .vhdx trouvé. Rien ne change à
::X|FR|cl.vhdx.compact.054| l intérieur du système de fichiers Linux ; seul
::X|FR|cl.vhdx.compact.055| l espace inutilisé du fichier conteneur est
::X|FR|cl.vhdx.compact.056|                           rendu à Windows. À faire quand vous pouvez
::X|FR|cl.vhdx.compact.057|                           laisser la machine tranquille quelques minutes.
::X|FR|cl.vhdx.compact.058|    KEEP                 : Laisser les disques virtuels tels quels. Ils
::X|FR|cl.vhdx.compact.059|                           gardent la place déjà prise et en prendront
::X|FR|cl.vhdx.compact.060|                           davantage à chaque écriture ; ils ne
::X|FR|cl.vhdx.compact.061|                           rétrécissent jamais tout seuls. Vous y perdez
::X|FR|cl.vhdx.compact.062|                           de la place disque, rien de plus.
