:: ---- cl.wupdate.download (cleanup) -------------------------------
::P|cl.wupdate.download|DELETE|DELETE|DELETE|DELETE|KEEP|
::T|EN|cl.wupdate.download.001|WINDOWS UPDATE DOWNLOAD CACHE
::T|EN|cl.wupdate.download.002|Empties the folder where Windows Update stores packages it has already downloaded, typically freeing a few hundred MB to several GB, at the cost of re-downloading anything that was not yet installed.
::T|FR|cl.wupdate.download.001|CACHE DE TÉLÉCHARGEMENT DE WINDOWS UPDATE
::T|FR|cl.wupdate.download.002|Vide le dossier où Windows Update stocke les paquets déjà téléchargés, libérant en général de quelques centaines de Mo à plusieurs Go, au prix d un retéléchargement de ce qui n était pas encore installé.
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.001|  What it is      : C:\Windows\SoftwareDistribution\Download is where
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.002|                    Windows Update parks the update packages it has
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.003|                    downloaded, before and after installing them. OPTY
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.004|                    stops the wuauserv service, empties that folder and
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.005|                    starts the service again.
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.006|
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.007|  Actual effect   : Three lines: net stop wuauserv, del /S /F /Q on the
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.008|                    folder contents, net start wuauserv. Only the
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.009|                    downloaded payloads go. The service start type is not
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.010|                    changed, no update is uninstalled and nothing in your
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.011|                    update history is touched. Two honest caveats about
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.012|                    what actually happens. First, del removes files but
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.013|                    not folders, so the directory tree is still there
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.014|                    afterwards, just empty. Second, anything still held
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.015|                    open - by a BITS transfer in flight, or by the service
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.016|                    if net stop did not fully take - simply fails to
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.017|                    delete and stays, and because line 905 has no output
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.018|                    redirection you will see the access-denied lines
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.019|                    scroll past on the console. Nothing is force-unlocked.
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.020|
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.021|  Gain            : Reclaims disk space, commonly 500 MB to several GB on
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.022|                    a machine that has taken a feature update, and a
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.023|                    couple of hundred MB on one that has only seen monthly
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.024|                    cumulative updates. It is also the standard first fix
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.025|                    for an update stuck at a percentage or failing with
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.026|                    the same error every time. No speed benefit
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.027|                    whatsoever.
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.028|
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.029|  Cost            : An update that was downloaded but not yet installed is
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.030|                    downloaded again on the next scan. That is bandwidth,
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.031|                    not breakage - typically a few hundred MB, up to
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.032|                    several GB if a feature update was staged. Windows
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.033|                    also prunes this folder on its own after roughly ten
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.034|                    days, so on a well-behaved machine this is a shortcut
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.035|                    rather than a necessity. Nothing user-owned is in that
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.036|                    folder.
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.037|
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.038|  Windows default : Not applicable. It is a regenerable cache that Windows
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.039|                    manages and prunes on its own schedule.
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.040|
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.041|  Possible values:
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.042|    DELETE               : Stop wuauserv, empty the Download folder, start
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.043|                           wuauserv again. Nothing is uninstalled and no
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.044|                           update history is lost; only the downloaded
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.045|                           packages go, and they are fetched again if
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.046|                           still needed.
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.047|    KEEP                 : Leave the folder alone. Windows prunes it by
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.048|                           itself after roughly ten days, so on a healthy
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.049|                           machine the only thing you lose is the space in
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.050|                           the meantime.
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.051|    ASK                  : Not used. The only bad moment is a large update
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.052|                           mid-download on a slow or metered link, and
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.053|                           that is a matter of timing rather than a
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.054|                           decision a profile has to arbitrate.
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.055|
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.056|  Why these profiles : Four DELETE and one KEEP. The four are identical
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.057|                       because a re-download costs the same everywhere and
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.058|                       no machine role changes it - the one real variable,
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.059|                       a metered or slow connection, belongs to the
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.060|                       network rather than to the profile, and it is
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.061|                       called out in the cost instead of being faked into
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.062|                       a column. WINDOWS is KEEP because letting the
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.063|                       folder age out by itself really is the shipped
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.064|                       behaviour.
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.065|
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.066|  Known problems  : The path is hardcoded as C:\Windows rather than
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.067|                    %WINDIR%. Harmless on virtually every machine, wrong
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.068|                    on one where Windows is not on C:. The same line has
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.069|                    no >nul redirection, unlike almost every other delete
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.070|                    in the file, so its errors are printed rather than
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.071|                    logged.
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.072|
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.073|  Target          : C:\Windows\SoftwareDistribution\Download\* - net stop
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.074|                    wuauserv at line 916, del /S /F /Q at line 918, net
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.075|                    start wuauserv at line 920, all inside the :delete
::X|EN|cl.wupdate.download.076|                    block of OPTY.bat.
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.001| Ce que c est : C:\Windows\SoftwareDistribution\Download est l endroit
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.002|                    où Windows Update dépose les paquets de mise à jour
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.003|                    téléchargés, avant et après leur installation. OPTY
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.004|                    arrête le service wuauserv, vide ce dossier, puis
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.005|                    relance le service.
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.006|
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.007|  Effet reel      : Trois lignes : net stop wuauserv, del /S /F /Q sur le
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.008|                    contenu du dossier, net start wuauserv. Seuls les
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.009|                    paquets téléchargés partent. Le type de démarrage du
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.010| service n est pas modifié, aucune mise à jour n est
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.011| désinstallée et l historique des mises à jour n est
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.012|                    pas touché. Deux réserves honnêtes sur ce qui se passe
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.013| réellement. D abord, del supprime les fichiers mais
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.014| pas les dossiers : l arborescence reste en place,
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.015|                    vide. Ensuite, tout ce qui est encore ouvert - un
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.016|                    transfert BITS en cours, ou le service si le net stop
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.017| n a pas complètement abouti - échoue simplement à être
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.018| supprimé et reste, et comme la ligne 905 n a aucune
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.019|                    redirection de sortie, vous verrez défiler les
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.020| messages d accès refusé dans la console. Rien n est
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.021|                    déverrouillé de force.
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.022|
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.023|  Gain            : Récupère de la place, souvent 500 Mo à plusieurs Go
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.024|                    sur une machine ayant reçu une mise à jour de
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.025|                    fonctionnalité, et quelques centaines de Mo sur une
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.026| machine qui n a connu que les cumulatives mensuelles.
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.027| C est aussi le premier remède classique quand une mise
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.028|                    à jour reste bloquée à un pourcentage ou échoue
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.029|                    toujours de la même façon. Aucun gain de vitesse,
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.030| d aucune sorte.
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.031|
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.032|  Cout            : Une mise à jour téléchargée mais pas encore installée
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.033| sera retéléchargée à la prochaine analyse. C est de la
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.034|                    bande passante, pas une casse : quelques centaines de
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.035| Mo en général, jusqu à plusieurs Go si une mise à jour
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.036|                    de fonctionnalité était préparée. Windows purge par
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.037| ailleurs ce dossier tout seul au bout d une dizaine de
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.038|                    jours, donc sur une machine bien portante on ne fait
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.039| qu accélérer les choses. Rien de ce qui vous
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.040|                    appartient ne se trouve dans ce dossier.
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.041|
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.042| Defaut Windows : Sans objet. C est un cache régénérable, géré et purgé
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.043|                    par Windows selon sa propre planification.
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.044|
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.045|  Valeurs possibles :
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.046|    DELETE               : Arrêter wuauserv, vider le dossier Download,
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.047| relancer wuauserv. Rien n est désinstallé et
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.048| aucun historique de mise à jour n est perdu ;
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.049|                           seuls les paquets téléchargés partent, et ils
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.050| sont récupérés à nouveau s ils sont encore
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.051|                           nécessaires.
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.052|    KEEP                 : Laisser le dossier tranquille. Windows le purge
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.053| tout seul au bout d une dizaine de jours : sur
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.054| une machine saine, vous n y perdez que la place
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.055|                           pendant ce laps de temps.
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.056| ASK : Non utilisé. Le seul mauvais moment, c est une
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.057|                           grosse mise à jour en cours de téléchargement
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.058|                           sur une liaison lente ou limitée, ce qui relève
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.059| du calendrier et non d un arbitrage de profil.
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.060|
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.061|  Pourquoi ces profils : Quatre DELETE et un KEEP. Les quatre sont
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.062| identiques parce qu un retéléchargement coûte la
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.063| même chose partout et qu aucun usage de la
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.064|                         machine ne change cela : la seule vraie variable,
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.065|                         une connexion lente ou limitée, relève du réseau
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.066|                         et non du profil, et elle est signalée dans le
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.067|                         coût plutôt que déguisée en colonne. WINDOWS est
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.068|                         à KEEP parce que laisser le dossier vieillir tout
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.069| seul est réellement le comportement d origine.
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.070|
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.071|  Problemes connus : Le chemin est écrit en dur C:\Windows au lieu de
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.072|                     %WINDIR%. Sans conséquence sur la quasi-totalité des
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.073| machines, faux sur une machine où Windows n est pas
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.074| sur C:. La même ligne n a aucune redirection >nul,
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.075|                     contrairement à presque toutes les autres
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.076|                     suppressions du fichier : ses erreurs sont donc
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.077| affichées au lieu d être journalisées.
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.078|
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.079|  Cible           : C:\Windows\SoftwareDistribution\Download\* - net stop
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.080|                    wuauserv at line 916, del /S /F /Q at line 918, net
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.081|                    start wuauserv at line 920, all inside the :delete
::X|FR|cl.wupdate.download.082|                    block of OPTY.bat.
::
:: ---- cl.drivesweep.fixed (risky) -------------------------------
::P|cl.drivesweep.fixed|ASK|ASK|ASK|ASK|KEEP|
::T|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.001|UPDATE CACHES AND UPGRADE LEFTOVERS, EVERY DRIVE
::T|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.002|Can free 5 to 15 GB of leftover update data on a drive that recently took a Windows upgrade, but a .cache folder found at a drive root is often a developer tool cache rather than Windows junk, and the leftovers it also removes are what let you undo a recent upgrade.
::T|FR|cl.drivesweep.fixed.001|CACHES DE MISE À JOUR ET RÉSIDUS D UPGRADE, TOUS LES DISQUES
::T|FR|cl.drivesweep.fixed.002|Peut libérer 5 à 15 Go de données de mise à jour laissées sur un disque ayant récemment reçu une mise à niveau Windows, mais un dossier .cache trouvé à la racine d un disque est souvent un cache d outil de développement plutôt que des déchets Windows, et les résidus supprimés sont aussi ce qui permet d annuler une mise à niveau récente.
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.001|  What it is      : Windows does not always put its Delivery Optimization
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.002|                    and update payload caches on C:. It picks whichever
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.003|                    volume had room. This step visits every FIXED drive,
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.004|                    clears DeliveryOptimization, WUDownloadCache and
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.005|                    .cache, and removes the leftover staging folders
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.006|                    $WINDOWS.~BT, $Windows.~WS and $WinREAgent.
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.007|
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.008|  Actual effect   : Drive letters are collected by comparing each letter's
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.009|                    fsutil drive type against the type of %SystemDrive%,
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.010|                    so the comparison survives a localised Windows.
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.011|                    Network drives are skipped on purpose, because a dead
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.012|                    SMB mapping costs a 30-second timeout per access and
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.013|                    would stall the run. Then per drive: four del /F /S /Q
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.014|                    on the cache paths, then rd /S /Q on the three staging
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.015|                    folders, unconditionally, as soon as each exists. The
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.016|                    .cache path gets a size report first, via :bigcache,
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.017|                    which prints a warning when the folder exceeds about
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.018|                    2000 MB - read that line carefully, because it is a
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.019|                    warning only. The delete on the next line happens
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.020|                    regardless of the size.
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.021|
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.022|  Gain            : Potentially the biggest space win of a cleanup run:
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.023|                    $WINDOWS.~BT alone is often several GB, and Delivery
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.024|                    Optimization can hold gigabytes of peer-shared update
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.025|                    data. On a 256 GB laptop that has recently taken a
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.026|                    feature update, 5 to 15 GB back is realistic. On a
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.027|                    machine that has not upgraded recently, these paths
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.028|                    are frequently empty and the step frees nothing at all
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.029|                    - do not expect a number just because the step ran.
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.030|
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.031|  Cost            : Three of the four cache paths are pure Windows Update
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.032|                    payload and come back on demand. The fourth is a bare
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.033|                    <drive>:\.cache at the root, matched by name alone. On
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.034|                    a developer machine that is very often a tool cache -
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.035|                    Bazel, Yarn, Cargo, pip, Hugging Face models - and
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.036|                    emptying it means a multi-gigabyte re-download, not a
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.037|                    free cleanup. OPTY cannot tell the two apart; it only
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.038|                    prints the size on the way past. Check whether any of
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.039|                    your drives has a .cache folder at its root before
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.040|                    answering yes, and if one does, decline this step and
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.041|                    empty DeliveryOptimization and WUDownloadCache by
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.042|                    hand. Separately, $WINDOWS.~BT and $Windows.~WS are
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.043|                    part of what Settings, Recovery, Go back needs. If you
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.044|                    upgraded to a new Windows build in the last ten days,
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.045|                    deleting them removes your ability to roll that
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.046|                    upgrade back, exactly like deleting Windows.old. And
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.047|                    there is no check for an upgrade that is already
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.048|                    downloaded and waiting for a reboot: delete these mid-
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.049|                    upgrade and Windows re-downloads the whole feature
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.050|                    update.
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.051|
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.052|  Windows default : Not applicable as a setting. These are caches and
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.053|                    post-upgrade staging folders that Windows abandons and
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.054|                    then removes on its own, roughly ten days after the
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.055|                    upgrade.
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.056|
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.057|  Possible values:
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.058|    DELETE               : Empty all four cache paths and remove the three
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.059|                           staging folders on every internal drive. Only
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.060|                           pick this once you have checked that no drive
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.061|                           has a .cache folder at its root and that you
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.062|                           have not upgraded Windows in the last ten days.
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.063|    KEEP                 : Leave every one of those paths alone. Windows
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.064|                           removes $WINDOWS.~BT and $Windows.~WS itself
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.065|                           about ten days after an upgrade, once the
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.066|                           rollback window has closed, and $WinREAgent
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.067|                           once WinRE servicing finishes. Doing nothing
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.068|                           costs you the disk space for those ten days and
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.069|                           nothing else.
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.070|    ASK                  : The only defensible answer for all four real-
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.071|                           machine profiles, and for two independent
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.072|                           reasons. A root-level .cache is matched by name
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.073|                           alone, and on a developer machine that is
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.074|                           routinely a Bazel, Yarn, Cargo, pip or Hugging
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.075|                           Face store - tens of GB of re-download, not
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.076|                           Windows Update payload. And the staging folders
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.077|                           are part of what Settings, Recovery, Go back
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.078|                           needs. Neither depends on what the machine is
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.079|                           for; both depend on facts only you can check.
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.080|
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.081|  Why these profiles : Four ASK and one KEEP. Four identical columns is
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.082|                       the honest outcome here, because both hazards - a
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.083|                       tool cache at the root of a drive, and a rollback
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.084|                       window that may still be open - are facts about
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.085|                       this particular machine's last ten days, not about
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.086|                       whether it plays games or serves Plex. WINDOWS is
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.087|                       KEEP and that is a real answer: Windows genuinely
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.088|                       does clear these folders itself once the rollback
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.089|                       window closes.
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.090|
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.091|  Known problems  : The step ships as apply in manual, Auto lite and Auto
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.092|                    full, which means the unconditional rd /S /Q on the
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.093|                    three staging folders and the delete of
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.094|                    <drive>:\.cache both run unattended with no question
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.095|                    asked. The sibling card that documents the same code,
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.096|                    helper-drivesweep-caches, is ask-no-default - two
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.097|                    cards describing one block with opposite risk levels.
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.098|                    The .cache line also collides head-on with this
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.099|                    project's own standing rule that OPTY must not clear
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.100|                    development caches. Ideally the code should drop the
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.101|                    <drive>:\.cache line entirely and split the staging-
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.102|                    folder removal out of the cache sweep.
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.103|
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.104|  Unverified      : Whether root-level DeliveryOptimization and
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.105|                    WUDownloadCache folders exist at all on a current
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.106|                    Windows 11 25H2 machine was not verified. On several
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.107|                    builds the Delivery Optimization cache lives
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.108|                    elsewhere, which would mean three of the four cache
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.109|                    lines match nothing and the only line that actually
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.110|                    deletes anything is <drive>:\.cache - the one line
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.111|                    that should not be there. Check the log for the Cache
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.112|                    emptied entries after a run before believing the
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.113|                    multi-GB figure.
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.114|
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.fixed.115|  Target          : On every FIXED drive letter:
