:: ---- cl.iconcache.noop (cleanup) ---------------------------------
::P|cl.iconcache.noop|KEEP|KEEP|KEEP|KEEP|KEEP|
::T|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.001|EXPLORER ICON CACHE (THIS STEP DOES NOTHING)
::T|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.002|Used to try clearing the icon database that causes blank or wrong shortcut icons, but the files that actually hold the data are always locked by Explorer while it runs, so the step now does nothing at all, on purpose.
::T|FR|cl.iconcache.noop.001|CACHE D ICÔNES DE L EXPLORATEUR (CETTE ÉTAPE NE FAIT RIEN)
::T|FR|cl.iconcache.noop.002|Essayait autrefois de vider la base d icônes responsable des icônes blanches ou erronées sur les raccourcis, mais les fichiers qui portent vraiment les données sont toujours verrouillés par l Explorateur pendant son exécution, donc l étape ne fait aujourd hui plus rien, volontairement.
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.001|  What it is      : Explorer keeps a database of every icon it has drawn,
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.002|                    in iconcache_16.db, iconcache_32.db, iconcache_48.db,
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.003|                    iconcache_256.db and iconcache_idx.db under
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.004|                    %LOCALAPPDATA%\Microsoft\Windows\Explorer. A stale one
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.005|                    is why you sometimes see a blank white icon or another
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.006|                    program's icon on a shortcut. OPTY used to delete
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.007|                    those files. It no longer does, and this card exists
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.008|                    to say so.
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.009|
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.010|  Actual effect   : No files are deleted. The block is comments plus one
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.011|                    log line. When the delete was still there it was
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.012|                    measured on a live machine: the five files that
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.013|                    actually hold the data, 11.2 MB together, are open by
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.014|                    the running explorer.exe with no sharing, so the
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.015|                    delete never touched them. The ten files it did remove
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.016|                    were 0-byte stubs. The line reported success every
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.017|                    time and freed about 240 bytes.
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.018|
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.019|  Gain            : None. Zero bytes, no speed change, no icons fixed.
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.020|                    That is the whole point of the card: the previous
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.021|                    version of this step reported a clean it was not
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.022|                    performing.
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.023|
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.024|  Cost            : None, because nothing runs. What you give up is the
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.025|                    ability to fix a genuinely corrupt icon cache from
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.026|                    this pass. Doing that for real means stopping
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.027|                    explorer.exe, which closes every open Explorer window
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.028|                    and any dialog hosted by the shell - too disruptive
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.029|                    for an unattended run, and a corrupt icon cache is a
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.030|                    rare failure. thumbcache_*.db was never in scope
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.031|                    either: rebuilding it visibly regenerates every photo
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.032|                    and video thumbnail in large folders.
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.033|
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.034|  Windows default : Not applicable in the registry sense. Explorer
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.035|                    regenerates icon entries on its own, and Windows never
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.036|                    bulk-deletes the database.
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.037|
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.038|  Possible values:
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.039|    DELETE               : Would mean putting the del of iconcache_*.db
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.040|                           back. Measured here, that frees about 240 bytes
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.041|                           and fixes nothing, because the five files
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.042|                           holding the data are open by explorer.exe.
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.043|                           Doing it for real means stopping explorer.exe.
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.044|    KEEP                 : What the code does today: nothing at all.
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.045|                           Explorer keeps its icon database and rebuilds
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.046|                           stale entries by itself.
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.047|    ASK                  : The only honest way to actually do it: ask,
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.048|                           warn that Explorer will be stopped and every
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.049|                           open Explorer window and shell dialog will
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.050|                           close, then delete and restart explorer.exe.
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.051|
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.052|  Why these profiles : Five identical columns, and inventing a difference
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.053|                       would be worse than admitting there is none. No
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.054|                       profile deletes anything here, because the code
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.055|                       deletes nothing. If your icons are actually broken,
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.056|                       the manual fix is to close your Explorer windows,
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.057|                       end explorer.exe from Task Manager, delete
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.058|                       iconcache_*.db and start explorer.exe again.
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.059|
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.060|  Known problems  : Line 989 still logs "Deleting icon cache (thumbnails
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.061|                    kept)" although nothing is deleted any more. The log
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.062|                    therefore claims a clean that never happens, which is
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.063|                    exactly the failure this step was removed for. The
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.064|                    echo should be dropped, or reworded to say the icon
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.065|                    cache is deliberately left alone.
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.066|
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.067|  Unverified      : The 11.2 MB and 240 byte figures come from one
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.068|                    measurement on the maintainer's machine. The general
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.069|                    shape - the populated iconcache files are open by
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.070|                    explorer.exe with no sharing - is how the shell works,
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.071|                    but the exact sizes are that machine's.
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.072|
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.073|  Target          : OPTY.bat lines 988-1001. Line 989 still writes
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.074|                    "Deleting icon cache (thumbnails kept)" to the log;
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.075|                    lines 990-1001 are comments explaining why the del of 
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.076|                    %LOCALAPPDATA%\Microsoft\Windows\Explorer\iconcache_*.
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.077|                    db was removed. There is no del, no rd and no reg
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.078|                    command left in this block. thumbcache_*.db was never
::X|EN|cl.iconcache.noop.079|                    targeted.
::X|FR|cl.iconcache.noop.001| Ce que c est : L Explorateur conserve une base de toutes les icônes
::X|FR|cl.iconcache.noop.002| qu il a affichées, dans iconcache_16.db,
::X|FR|cl.iconcache.noop.003|                    iconcache_32.db, iconcache_48.db, iconcache_256.db et
::X|FR|cl.iconcache.noop.004|                    iconcache_idx.db, sous
::X|FR|cl.iconcache.noop.005|                    %LOCALAPPDATA%\Microsoft\Windows\Explorer. Une base
::X|FR|cl.iconcache.noop.006| périmée, c est l icône blanche vide ou l icône du
::X|FR|cl.iconcache.noop.007|                    mauvais programme sur un raccourci. OPTY supprimait
::X|FR|cl.iconcache.noop.008| ces fichiers autrefois. Ce n est plus le cas, et cette
::X|FR|cl.iconcache.noop.009|                    fiche est là pour le dire.
::X|FR|cl.iconcache.noop.010|
::X|FR|cl.iconcache.noop.011| Effet reel : Aucun fichier n est supprimé. Le bloc n est plus que
::X|FR|cl.iconcache.noop.012|                    des commentaires et une ligne de journal. Quand la
::X|FR|cl.iconcache.noop.013|                    suppression existait encore, elle a été mesurée sur
::X|FR|cl.iconcache.noop.014|                    une machine réelle : les cinq fichiers qui portent
