:: ---- cl.logs.cbspanther (cleanup) --------------------------------
::P|cl.logs.cbspanther|DELETE|DELETE|DELETE|DELETE|KEEP|
::T|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.001|OLD WINDOWS SERVICING AND SETUP LOGS
::T|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.002|Removes archived logs from past Windows updates and installs, typically 100 to 400 MB and no effect on speed, but if a future update ever fails, these are the files that would have explained why.
::T|FR|cl.logs.cbspanther.001|ANCIENS JOURNAUX DE MAINTENANCE ET D INSTALLATION WINDOWS
::T|FR|cl.logs.cbspanther.002|Supprime les journaux archivés des précédentes mises à jour et installations Windows, typiquement 100 à 400 Mo et sans effet sur la vitesse, mais si une future mise à jour échoue, ce sont ces fichiers qui en auraient expliqué la cause.
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.001|  What it is      : CbsPersist_*.log and .cab are the compressed archives
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.002|                    of the component servicing log - the trail every
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.003|                    Windows update leaves behind. C:\Windows\Panther holds
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.004|                    the logs of the last Windows install or in-place
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.005|                    upgrade, setupact.log and setuperr.log among them.
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.006|                    Only the archives are targeted; the live CBS.log,
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.007|                    which TrustedInstaller holds open during servicing, is
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.008|                    left alone.
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.009|
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.010|  Actual effect   : Deletes the CbsPersist archives, and every file under
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.011|                    Panther and its subfolders. The Panther folder and its
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.012|                    subfolders remain as empty directories, because del /S
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.013|                    removes files only. Both paths need administrator
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.014|                    rights. If a servicing operation is running at that
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.015|                    moment, the file it is writing is locked and skipped
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.016|                    without a message.
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.017|
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.018|  Gain            : Space only, and less than the folklore suggests.
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.019|                    CbsPersist was measured at 93 MB on the machine this
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.020|                    rule was written for; Panther is typically 5 to 100
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.021|                    MB, and a few hundred MB on a machine freshly through
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.022|                    an in-place upgrade. Together, expect 100 to 400 MB in
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.023|                    the normal case rather than gigabytes. There is no
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.024|                    performance effect whatsoever.
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.025|
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.026|  Cost            : If a future update or upgrade fails, these are the
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.027|                    files a support engineer reads to find out why, and
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.028|                    the record of the previous ones is gone for good -
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.029|                    nothing regenerates a log of something that already
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.030|                    happened. Windows writes new ones on the next
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.031|                    servicing operation, within minutes. In practice
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.032|                    almost nobody ever opens them. One thing to know:
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.033|                    Panther also caches the answer file from an unattended
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.034|                    or OEM install, so if you deploy this image with
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.035|                    sysprep, look in Panther before wiping it.
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.036|
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.037|  Windows default : Not applicable. CbsPersist archives accumulate
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.038|                    indefinitely, and Panther keeps the last install or
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.039|                    upgrade logs until something removes them.
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.040|
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.041|  Possible values:
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.042|    DELETE               : Remove the archived servicing logs and the
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.043|                           contents of the Panther setup folder.
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.044|    KEEP                 : The right answer if an update or an upgrade
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.045|                           just failed and someone is going to read these
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.046|                           to find out why.
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.047|    ASK                  : Worth asking just before an in-place repair
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.048|                           install, when the before-and-after comparison
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.049|                           is the whole point.
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.050|
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.051|  Why these profiles : Four identical columns: the file is a diagnostic
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.052|                       record or it is dead weight, and that has nothing
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.053|                       to do with the machine's role. The only real
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.054|                       distinction is timing, not profile - say no while
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.055|                       an upgrade problem is still open, yes once
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.056|                       everything works. WINDOWS means leave it alone and
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.057|                       keep the full servicing trail.
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.058|
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.059|  Unverified      : 93 MB of CbsPersist was measured once on the
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.060|                    maintainer's machine. Panther's size depends entirely
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.061|                    on how many in-place upgrades the machine has been
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.062|                    through, and was not measured here. Whether a support
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.063|                    engineer would still want these files months later is
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.064|                    a judgement call, not a fact.
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.065|
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.066|  Target          : OPTY.bat lines 1038-1042. del /F /Q on
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.067|                    %WINDIR%\Logs\CBS\CbsPersist_*.log and
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.068|                    CbsPersist_*.cab, then del /F /S /Q on
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.069|                    %WINDIR%\Panther\*. The live %WINDIR%\Logs\CBS\CBS.log
::X|EN|cl.logs.cbspanther.070|                    is not targeted. No folder is removed.
::X|FR|cl.logs.cbspanther.001|  Ce que c est    : CbsPersist_*.log et .cab sont les archives compressées
::X|FR|cl.logs.cbspanther.002|                    du journal de maintenance des composants - la trace
::X|FR|cl.logs.cbspanther.003|                    que laisse chaque mise à jour Windows.
::X|FR|cl.logs.cbspanther.004|                    C:\Windows\Panther contient les journaux de la
::X|FR|cl.logs.cbspanther.005|                    dernière installation ou mise à niveau sur place, dont
::X|FR|cl.logs.cbspanther.006|                    setupact.log et setuperr.log. Seules les archives sont
::X|FR|cl.logs.cbspanther.007|                    visées ; le CBS.log actif, que TrustedInstaller tient
