:: ---- cl.steam.cache (cleanup) ------------------------------------
::P|cl.steam.cache|DELETE|DELETE|DELETE|DELETE|KEEP|
::T|EN|cl.steam.cache.001|STEAM LOGS, CRASH DUMPS AND WEB CACHE
::T|EN|cl.steam.cache.002|Clears Steam's logs, crash dumps and store-page web cache (roughly 150 to 400 MB) - the standard fix for a blank or stuck store page, and never touches your shader cache or game files.
::T|FR|cl.steam.cache.001|JOURNAUX, DUMPS ET CACHE WEB DE STEAM
::T|FR|cl.steam.cache.002|Vide les journaux, dumps de plantage et cache web des pages boutique de Steam (environ 150 à 400 Mo) - le remède habituel à une page boutique blanche ou figée, sans jamais toucher au cache de shaders ni aux fichiers de jeu.
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.001|  What it is      : Steam writes logs and crash dumps into its own install
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.002|                    folder, and its store and library pages are drawn by
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.003|                    an embedded browser with its own htmlcache. This step
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.004|                    clears the logs and dumps always, and the htmlcache
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.005|                    only when steam.exe is not running.
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.006|
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.007|  Actual effect   : Deletes the files under <Steam>\logs and
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.008|                    <Steam>\dumps, where <Steam> is the install path read
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.009|                    from the registry - so only the Steam program folder;
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.010|                    libraries you keep on other drives are irrelevant here
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.011|                    and never touched. Because the logs are deleted even
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.012|                    while Steam is up, the log files it currently holds
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.013|                    open are simply skipped, silently. The htmlcache under
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.014|                    %LOCALAPPDATA%\Steam is only cleared when Steam is
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.015|                    fully quit, and Steam sits in the tray by default, so
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.016|                    in practice that part is often skipped - quit it from
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.017|                    the tray if the store page is what you want fixed.
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.018|                    Deliberately excluded: steamapps\shadercache and
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.019|                    steamapps\depotcache.
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.020|
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.021|  Gain            : Logs and dumps are usually tens of MB, occasionally a
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.022|                    few hundred if Steam has been crashing. htmlcache was
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.023|                    measured at 141 MB on this machine. Call it 150 to 400
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.024|                    MB in a good pass. Clearing htmlcache is also the
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.025|                    known fix for a store or library page that comes up
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.026|                    blank or stuck on an old layout.
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.027|
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.028|  Cost            : Nothing functional. The two exclusions are the
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.029|                    interesting part. Wiping steamapps\shadercache would
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.030|                    guarantee shader recompilation stutter in your games,
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.031|                    exactly the cost this tool tries not to pay twice. And
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.032|                    wiping depotcache would force Steam to re-fetch the
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.033|                    depot manifests - a few MB - before it could verify or
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.034|                    update, and it would then still validate against your
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.035|                    local game files: pointless churn for no space worth
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.036|                    having, not the full game re-download folklore claims.
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.037|                    Store pages and images refetch in seconds.
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.038|
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.039|  Windows default : Not applicable. Application logs and an application
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.040|                    cache; Windows has no handler for either.
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.041|
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.042|  Possible values:
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.043|    DELETE               : Clear the Steam logs and crash dumps, and the
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.044|                           embedded-browser cache if Steam is fully quit.
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.045|                           Games, saves and the shader cache are
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.046|                           untouched.
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.047|    KEEP                 : Fine to keep. These are logs no one reads and a
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.048|                           bounded web cache; nothing here grows
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.049|                           dangerously.
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.050|    ASK                  : Not needed. The one destructive variant, wiping
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.051|                           steamapps\shadercache, is not in the code at
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.052|                           all.
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.053|
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.054|  Why these profiles : Four identical columns. GAMING is where the
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.055|                       htmlcache fix actually matters and where the
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.056|                       shadercache exclusion earns its keep. SERVER
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.057|                       running Steam game servers gets the same small
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.058|                       benefit. On OFFICE and LAPTOP without Steam the
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.059|                       registry lookup finds nothing and the step exits
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.060|                       immediately. WINDOWS means leave it alone, which
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.061|                       costs a couple of hundred MB and nothing else.
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.062|
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.063|  Unverified      : 141 MB of htmlcache was measured once on this machine.
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.064|                    Log and dump sizes vary with how much Steam has
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.065|                    crashed and were not measured. Whether steam.exe is up
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.066|                    at the time depends on your start-with-Windows
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.067|                    setting.
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.068|
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.069|  Target          : OPTY.bat lines 1114-1126. STEAMPATH is read from
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.070|                    HKLM\SOFTWARE\WOW6432Node\Valve\Steam, value
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.071|                    InstallPath; then del /F /S /Q on %STEAMPATH%\logs and
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.072|                    %STEAMPATH%\dumps. Then call :isrunning "steam.exe"
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.073|                    and, only if it is not running, del /F /S /Q on
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.074|                    %LOCALAPPDATA%\Steam\htmlcache. steamapps\shadercache
::X|EN|cl.steam.cache.075|                    and steamapps\depotcache are deliberately excluded.
::X|FR|cl.steam.cache.001|  Ce que c est    : Steam écrit ses journaux et ses dumps de plantage dans
::X|FR|cl.steam.cache.002|                    son propre dossier d installation, et ses pages
::X|FR|cl.steam.cache.003|                    boutique et bibliothèque sont affichées par un
::X|FR|cl.steam.cache.004|                    navigateur intégré avec son propre htmlcache. Cette
::X|FR|cl.steam.cache.005|                    étape vide toujours les journaux et les dumps, et le
::X|FR|cl.steam.cache.006|                    htmlcache uniquement si steam.exe ne tourne pas.
::X|FR|cl.steam.cache.007|
::X|FR|cl.steam.cache.008|  Effet reel      : Supprime les fichiers de <Steam>\logs et
::X|FR|cl.steam.cache.009|                    <Steam>\dumps, où <Steam> est le chemin d installation
::X|FR|cl.steam.cache.010|                    lu dans le registre - donc uniquement le dossier
::X|FR|cl.steam.cache.011|                    programme de Steam : vos bibliothèques sur d autres
::X|FR|cl.steam.cache.012|                    disques ne sont pas concernées et ne sont jamais
::X|FR|cl.steam.cache.013|                    touchées. Comme les journaux sont supprimés même quand
::X|FR|cl.steam.cache.014|                    Steam tourne, les fichiers qu il tient ouverts sont
::X|FR|cl.steam.cache.015|                    simplement ignorés, en silence. Le htmlcache sous
::X|FR|cl.steam.cache.016|                    %LOCALAPPDATA%\Steam n est vidé que si Steam est
::X|FR|cl.steam.cache.017|                    complètement quitté, et Steam reste par défaut dans la
::X|FR|cl.steam.cache.018|                    zone de notification : en pratique, cette partie est
::X|FR|cl.steam.cache.019|                    souvent sautée. Quittez-le depuis l icône si c est la
::X|FR|cl.steam.cache.020|                    page boutique que vous voulez réparer. Volontairement
::X|FR|cl.steam.cache.021|                    exclus : steamapps\shadercache et
::X|FR|cl.steam.cache.022|                    steamapps\depotcache.
::X|FR|cl.steam.cache.023|
::X|FR|cl.steam.cache.024|  Gain            : Journaux et dumps pèsent en général quelques dizaines
::X|FR|cl.steam.cache.025|                    de Mo, parfois quelques centaines si Steam a beaucoup
::X|FR|cl.steam.cache.026|                    planté. Le htmlcache a été mesuré à 141 Mo sur cette
::X|FR|cl.steam.cache.027|                    machine. Disons 150 à 400 Mo pour un bon passage.
::X|FR|cl.steam.cache.028|                    Vider le htmlcache est aussi le remède connu à une
::X|FR|cl.steam.cache.029|                    page boutique ou bibliothèque qui reste blanche ou
::X|FR|cl.steam.cache.030|                    figée sur une ancienne mise en page.
::X|FR|cl.steam.cache.031|
::X|FR|cl.steam.cache.032|  Cout            : Rien de fonctionnel. Ce sont les deux exclusions qui
::X|FR|cl.steam.cache.033|                    méritent l attention. Effacer steamapps\shadercache
::X|FR|cl.steam.cache.034|                    garantirait des saccades de recompilation de shaders
::X|FR|cl.steam.cache.035|                    dans vos jeux, exactement le coût que cet outil évite
::X|FR|cl.steam.cache.036|                    de payer deux fois. Et effacer depotcache obligerait
::X|FR|cl.steam.cache.037|                    Steam à retélécharger les manifestes de dépôt -
::X|FR|cl.steam.cache.038|                    quelques Mo - avant de pouvoir vérifier ou mettre à
::X|FR|cl.steam.cache.039|                    jour, puis il validerait quand même vos fichiers de
::X|FR|cl.steam.cache.040|                    jeu locaux : du brassage inutile pour une place
::X|FR|cl.steam.cache.041|                    négligeable, et non le retéléchargement complet du jeu
::X|FR|cl.steam.cache.042|                    que raconte la légende. Pages boutique et images se
::X|FR|cl.steam.cache.043|                    rechargent en quelques secondes.
::X|FR|cl.steam.cache.044|
::X|FR|cl.steam.cache.045|  Defaut Windows  : Sans objet. Journaux et cache applicatifs, pour
::X|FR|cl.steam.cache.046|                    lesquels Windows n a aucun gestionnaire.
::X|FR|cl.steam.cache.047|
::X|FR|cl.steam.cache.048|  Valeurs possibles :
::X|FR|cl.steam.cache.049|    DELETE               : Vider les journaux et dumps de Steam, et le
::X|FR|cl.steam.cache.050|                           cache du navigateur intégré si Steam est
::X|FR|cl.steam.cache.051|                           complètement quitté. Jeux, sauvegardes et cache
::X|FR|cl.steam.cache.052|                           de shaders intacts.
::X|FR|cl.steam.cache.053|    KEEP                 : On peut très bien le garder : des journaux que
::X|FR|cl.steam.cache.054|                           personne ne lit et un cache web borné, rien qui
::X|FR|cl.steam.cache.055|                           grossisse dangereusement.
::X|FR|cl.steam.cache.056|    ASK                  : Inutile. La seule variante destructrice,
::X|FR|cl.steam.cache.057|                           effacer steamapps\shadercache, n est pas dans
::X|FR|cl.steam.cache.058|                           le code.
::X|FR|cl.steam.cache.059|
::X|FR|cl.steam.cache.060|  Pourquoi ces profils : Quatre colonnes identiques. GAMING est le profil
::X|FR|cl.steam.cache.061|                         où le correctif htmlcache sert vraiment et où
::X|FR|cl.steam.cache.062|                         l exclusion du shadercache prend tout son sens.
::X|FR|cl.steam.cache.063|                         SERVEUR qui héberge des serveurs de jeu Steam
