:: ---- cl.ea.cache (cleanup) ---------------------------------------
::P|cl.ea.cache|DELETE|DELETE|DELETE|DELETE|KEEP|
::T|EN|cl.ea.cache.001|EA APP CACHE
::T|EN|cl.ea.cache.002|Clears the EA App's cache (50 to 500 MB) - EA's own first fix for a client that will not launch or shows an empty library, though you may need to sign in again.
::T|FR|cl.ea.cache.001|CACHE DE L APPLICATION EA
::T|FR|cl.ea.cache.002|Vide le cache de l application EA (50 à 500 Mo) - le premier remède recommandé par EA elle-même pour un client qui ne se lance pas ou affiche une bibliothèque vide, au prix d une éventuelle reconnexion.
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.001|  What it is      : The EA App, successor to Origin, keeps a cache in your
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.002|                    profile and a second one under %ProgramData%\EA Core:
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.003|                    store artwork, library metadata and web content for
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.004|                    the client's embedded browser. This step clears both,
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.005|                    and only when EADesktop.exe is not running.
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.006|
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.007|  Actual effect   : Deletes the files under %LOCALAPPDATA%\Electronic
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.008|                    Arts\EA Desktop\cache and %ProgramData%\EA Core\cache,
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.009|                    leaving the folders themselves. Installed games, save
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.010|                    data and entitlements are untouched. The user path is
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.011|                    the hardcoded C:\Users\compt profile, so other Windows
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.012|                    accounts keep theirs. The EA App starts with Windows
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.013|                    on a default install, so quit it from the tray before
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.014|                    running OPTY, or the step prints "EA App is running -
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.015|                    skipped" and does nothing.
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.016|
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.017|  Gain            : Modest: typically 50 to 500 MB depending on how large
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.018|                    your library is. The real value is that clearing this
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.019|                    cache is EA's own documented first step for a client
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.020|                    that will not launch, shows an empty library, or loops
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.021|                    on the login screen.
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.022|
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.023|  Cost            : Rebuilt on the next launch, which takes a few seconds
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.024|                    and a small download. You may have to sign in again.
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.025|                    Nothing permanent is lost - no game files, no saves,
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.026|                    no entitlements, and nothing needs re-installing.
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.027|
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.028|  Windows default : Not applicable. Application cache, created and managed
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.029|                    by the EA App.
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.030|
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.031|  Possible values:
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.032|    DELETE               : Empty the EA Desktop cache and the EA Core
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.033|                           cache, provided the client is fully closed.
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.034|                           Games, saves and entitlements are untouched.
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.035|    KEEP                 : Fine if the client works: the cache is small
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.036|                           and clearing it buys you nothing but a possible
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.037|                           sign-in prompt.
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.038|    ASK                  : Not needed. This is EA's own first
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.039|                           troubleshooting step and it risks nothing
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.040|                           beyond re-entering your password.
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.041|
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.042|  Why these profiles : Four identical columns. GAMING is where the client
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.043|                       exists at all; on SERVER, OFFICE and LAPTOP the
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.044|                       folders normally do not exist and the step quietly
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.045|                       does nothing. WINDOWS means leave it alone, which
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.046|                       costs a few hundred MB at most and keeps you signed
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.047|                       in.
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.048|
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.049|  Known problems  : The user path uses the hardcoded %USERHOME%
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.050|                    (C:\Users\compt), so another Windows account keeps its
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.051|                    EA cache while the step still logs a clean. The guard
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.052|                    only looks for EADesktop.exe; EA's background service
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.053|                    can be up without it, but it does not hold the cache
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.054|                    files open, so that is a note rather than a defect.
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.055|
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.056|  Unverified      : Having to sign in again after clearing the EA Desktop
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.057|                    cache is commonly reported and is what EA's own
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.058|                    troubleshooting article prepares you for, but it was
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.059|                    not reproduced here. The size range is typical, not
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.060|                    measured on this machine.
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.061|
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.062|  Target          : OPTY.bat lines 1134-1138. call :isrunning
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.063|                    "EADesktop.exe" then, only if it is not running, del
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.064|                    /F /S /Q on %USERHOME%\AppData\Local\Electronic
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.065|                    Arts\EA Desktop\cache and on %ProgramData%\EA
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.066|                    Core\cache. USERHOME is hardcoded at line 81 to
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.067|                    C:\Users\compt. The legacy Origin log folders are a
::X|EN|cl.ea.cache.068|                    separate step.
