::X|EN|cl.origin.logs.008|                    folders survive. There is deliberately no running-
::X|EN|cl.origin.logs.009|                    process guard, which is safe because a log file Origin
::X|EN|cl.origin.logs.010|                    holds open simply fails to delete and the error is
::X|EN|cl.origin.logs.011|                    swallowed by 2>nul. Note that the two user-level paths
::X|EN|cl.origin.logs.012|                    are built from %USERHOME%, which OPTY.bat line 81
::X|EN|cl.origin.logs.013|                    hardcodes to C:\Users\compt: run from any other
::X|EN|cl.origin.logs.014|                    account, this step points at somebody else's folder.
::X|EN|cl.origin.logs.015|
