::T|EN|cl.optytemp.scratch.002|Deletes two tiny work files OPTY writes for itself while scanning power schemes and network adapters - a few KB, no real gain, listed only so every deletion OPTY makes is documented.
::T|FR|cl.optytemp.scratch.001|FICHIERS DE TRAVAIL D OPTY DANS TEMP
::T|FR|cl.optytemp.scratch.002|Supprime deux minuscules fichiers de travail qu OPTY écrit pour lui-même en listant les modes d alimentation et les cartes réseau - quelques Ko, aucun gain réel, listé seulement pour que chaque suppression faite par OPTY soit documentée.
::X|EN|cl.optytemp.scratch.001|  What it is      : Removes %TEMP%\opty_pc_before.txt and
::X|EN|cl.optytemp.scratch.002|                    %TEMP%\opty_nic_list.txt, two working files OPTY
::X|EN|cl.optytemp.scratch.003|                    writes while listing power schemes and network
::X|EN|cl.optytemp.scratch.004|                    adapters.
::X|EN|cl.optytemp.scratch.005|
::X|EN|cl.optytemp.scratch.006|  Actual effect   : Plain del /f /q on those two exact names in the
::X|EN|cl.optytemp.scratch.007|                    current account's TEMP - no wildcard, so nothing else
::X|EN|cl.optytemp.scratch.008|                    can match. The adapter list is deleted before it is
::X|EN|cl.optytemp.scratch.009|                    built and again after it is consumed, so a stale list
::X|EN|cl.optytemp.scratch.010|                    from a previous run cannot be read by mistake.
::X|EN|cl.optytemp.scratch.011|
::X|EN|cl.optytemp.scratch.012|  Gain            : None worth quoting. Each file is one or two kilobytes;
::X|EN|cl.optytemp.scratch.013|                    this step is listed for completeness, so that every
::X|EN|cl.optytemp.scratch.014|                    file deletion OPTY performs is written down somewhere
::X|EN|cl.optytemp.scratch.015|                    you can read it.
::X|EN|cl.optytemp.scratch.016|
::X|EN|cl.optytemp.scratch.017|  Cost            : None. No user or system data is involved and both
::X|EN|cl.optytemp.scratch.018|                    files are rebuilt on the next run, in the second it
::X|EN|cl.optytemp.scratch.019|                    takes to enumerate the adapters.
::X|EN|cl.optytemp.scratch.020|
::X|EN|cl.optytemp.scratch.021|  Windows default : Not applicable - these files do not exist on a machine
::X|EN|cl.optytemp.scratch.022|                    that has never run OPTY.
::X|EN|cl.optytemp.scratch.023|
::X|EN|cl.optytemp.scratch.024|  Possible values:
