:: ---- cl.drivesweep.caches (cleanup) ------------------------------
::P|cl.drivesweep.caches|ASK|ASK|ASK|ASK|KEEP|
::T|EN|cl.drivesweep.caches.001|UPDATE AND DELIVERY CACHES ON EVERY FIXED DRIVE
::T|EN|cl.drivesweep.caches.002|Clears Windows update caches on every fixed drive plus any folder literally named .cache at the drive root - usually harmless, but that .cache folder could belong to a dev tool holding gigabytes you actually need.
::T|FR|cl.drivesweep.caches.001|CACHES DE MISE À JOUR ET DE DISTRIBUTION SUR CHAQUE DISQUE FIXE
::T|FR|cl.drivesweep.caches.002|Vide les caches de mise à jour de Windows sur chaque disque fixe, plus tout dossier nommé littéralement .cache à la racine du disque - en général sans risque, mais ce dossier .cache peut appartenir à un outil de développement contenant des gigaoctets dont vous avez besoin.
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.caches.001|  What it is      : Windows drops update payload at the root of whichever
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.caches.002|                    volume it picked, not only C:. This clears
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.caches.003|                    DeliveryOptimization, WUDownloadCache, the ProgramData
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.caches.004|                    Delivery Optimization cache and a folder named .cache,
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.caches.005|                    on every fixed drive.
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.caches.006|
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.caches.007|  Actual effect   : del /F /S /Q on those four paths per drive. The drive
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.caches.008|                    filter works: fixed drives here are C, D, E, G and J,
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.caches.009|                    and the eleven mapped SMB shares - F, I, K, L, Q, R,
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.caches.010|                    V, W, X, Y, Z - are correctly excluded, which matters
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.caches.011|                    because a disconnected share costs a 30 second timeout
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.caches.012|                    each. The same routine then removes the feature-update
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.caches.013|                    staging folders, which have their own card. Note that
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.caches.014|                    the third path is built per drive, so on D: it looks
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.caches.015|                    for D:\ProgramData, which does not exist.
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.caches.016|
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.caches.017|  Gain            : Measured on this machine, and it is not what the step
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.caches.018|                    claims. C:\DeliveryOptimization, C:\WUDownloadCache
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.caches.019|                    and C:\ProgramData\Microsoft\Windows\DeliveryOptimizat
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.caches.020|                    ion\Cache are all absent; D:\DeliveryOptimization and
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.caches.021|                    D:\WUDownloadCache exist but hold 0 bytes. The three
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.caches.022|                    Windows paths recover nothing at all here. The
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.caches.023|                    Delivery Optimization cache that does exist is 222 MB
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.caches.024|                    and lives under C:\Windows\ServiceProfiles\NetworkServ
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.caches.025|                    ice\AppData\Local\Microsoft\Windows\DeliveryOptimizati
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.caches.026|                    on, a path this step never touches and which the DoSvc
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.caches.027|                    service holds open. Total measured recovery: 0.9 MB,
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.caches.028|                    all of it from C:\.cache.
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.caches.029|
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.caches.030|  Cost            : For the three Windows paths, nothing: Windows re-
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.caches.031|                    downloads any update payload it still needs. The
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.caches.032|                    fourth path is the one to think about. On this machine
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.caches.033|                    C:\.cache contains AMD\DxCache and AMD\DxcCache - an
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.caches.034|                    AMD DirectX shader cache, 0.9 MB, back in seconds. On
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.caches.035|                    a development machine the same name is often a Bazel,
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.caches.036|                    Yarn, Cargo or Hugging Face store, and that is a
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.caches.037|                    multi-gigabyte refetch measured in hours, which fails
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.caches.038|                    the regeneration test outright.
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.caches.039|
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.caches.040|  Windows default : Not applicable - regenerable Windows Update and
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.caches.041|                    Delivery Optimization data. Windows expires its own
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.caches.042|                    Delivery Optimization cache without help.
::X|EN|cl.drivesweep.caches.043|
